window.ICA_STORY = {"cast":{"cheska":{"name":"Cheska","ja":"チェスカ","art":true,"acc":"#7a8450"},"yen":{"name":"Yến","ja":"イエン","art":true,"acc":"#2f8a8a"},"rodrigo":{"name":"Rodrigo","ja":"ロドリゴ","art":true,"acc":"#b8573a"},"toby":{"name":"Toby","ja":"トビー","art":true,"acc":"#5b9bd5"},"aoi":{"name":"Aoi","ja":"あおい","art":true,"acc":"#7d3c5c"},"mariya":{"name":"Mariya","ja":"まりや","art":true,"acc":"#e8735f"},"kaito":{"name":"Kaito","ja":"かいと","art":true,"acc":"#3f4a8a"},"fumiko":{"name":"Mrs. Satō","ja":"さとうさん","art":true,"acc":"#9b86c2"},"shoichi":{"name":"Mr. Satō","ja":"さとうさん","art":true,"acc":"#c9a03c"},"chiyo":{"name":"Chiyo","ja":"ちよさん","acc":"#8c7a5b"},"matsumoto":{"name":"Mr. Matsumoto","ja":"まつもとさん","acc":"#6f7f8f"},"hiroyuki":{"name":"Hiroyuki","ja":"ひろゆき","acc":"#7a6a58"},"megumi":{"name":"Megumi","ja":"めぐみ","acc":"#a0707e"},"sota":{"name":"Sōta","ja":"そうた","acc":"#7d9a5f"},"kuze":{"name":"Kaito's father","ja":"かいとの父","acc":"#5c6478"},"dewi":{"name":"Dewi","ja":"デウィ","acc":"#5f8f86"},"captain":{"name":"Old captain","ja":"せんちょう","acc":"#4f6d7a"},"amoako":{"name":"Dr. Amoako","ja":"アモアコ先生","acc":"#8a6d3b"},"lorraine":{"name":"Lorraine","ja":"ロレイン","acc":"#a8708f"}},"episodes":[{"unit":"e3u1","n":1,"title":"Names on the mailboxes","month":"April","level":"Kana only","enDefault":true,"parts":[{"t":"narr","text":"Ngô Hải Yến gets off the bus with two suitcases. It is April in Shioura, a harbor town on the Sea of Japan. She has a photo of the house from the rental listing on her phone, so she knows it at once: an old wooden house with two floors. She can hear the sea somewhere behind it."},
{"t":"narr","text":"Before she finds the doorbell, she finds the mailboxes. There are nine on the fence by the gate: one for each room, and one for the Satōs, who own the house. Each one shows only a family name. The house rule is that labels are written in kana, so that new tenants can read them. Some labels are new. Some are faded. One of them is already hers."},
{"t":"mailboxes","title":"The mailboxes","hint":"Read each name, then tap the mailbox to check.","items":[{"room":"101","ja":"イババオ","ro":"Ibabao","who":"Cheska Ibabao, from the Philippines. She moved in last October. Four beats (Japanese counts sounds in beats; here, each kana is one beat), with two ば in a row: イ・バ・バ・オ.","old":true},{"room":"102","ja":"モンドラゴン","ro":"Mondragón","who":"Rodrigo Mondragón, from Mexico. New this April. His label is ready, but he arrives on Saturday. Six beats, two of them ン: モ・ン・ド・ラ・ゴ・ン."},{"room":"103","ja":"せと","ro":"Seto","who":"Mariya Seto, from Shiojima, an island an hour away by ferry. She moved in a year ago, so she has lived here the longest. Two beats: せ・と.","old":true},{"room":"201","ja":"ウィットロック","ro":"Whitlock","who":"Toby Whitlock, from Australia. He moved in last October, after half a year in the university dorm, the same week as Cheska. His name barely fits on the label. ウィ is how katakana writes *wi*. Each small ッ is a one-beat pause: ウィ・ッ・ト・ロ・ッ・ク.","old":true},{"room":"202","ja":"ひらかわ","ro":"Hirakawa","who":"Aoi Hirakawa, a master's student from Saitama. New this April. Four beats: ひ・ら・か・わ."},{"room":"203","ja":"くぜ","ro":"Kuze","who":"Kaito Kuze, a first-year student from a small mountain town in Gifu. New this April. He wrote his own label, in very small letters. Two beats: く・ぜ."},{"room":"204","ja":"ゴー","ro":"Ngô","who":"Ngô Hải Yến, from Vietnam. New today. Katakana can't write the *ng* sound at the start, so Ngô becomes ゴー. The ー makes the vowel two beats long."},{"room":"205","ja":"","ro":"","who":"Room 205. There is no name on the label yet."}],"landlord":{"label":"The Satōs' house","ja":"さとう","ro":"Satō","who":"Shōichi-san and Fumiko-san. They own Kamome House and live in a small house across the street. Three beats: さ・と・う. The う makes the *o* long.","old":true}},
{"t":"narr","text":"Above the gate there is a wooden sign: かもめそう. *Kamome* means seagull. Many small apartment houses have names that end in *-sō*. A real seagull is sitting on the sign."},
{"t":"narr","text":"A young woman hurries down the path toward Yến."},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"yay","ja":"こんにちは！ ゴーさん？","en":"Hi! Are you Ngô-san?","tag":"cheerful","ref":"E1·L1"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"hello","ja":"はい。ゴー・ハイ・イエンと もうします。","en":"Yes. My name is Ngô Hải Yến.","gl":"と もうします: a very polite way to say \"my name is\".","tag":"politely","ref":"E1·L2"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"yay","ja":"せと まりやです！ まりやで いいよ！","en":"I'm Mariya Seto! Just call me Mariya!","gl":"～で いいよ: \"～ is fine\".","tag":"excited","ref":"E1·L3"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Yến worked for four years at a software company in Japan, so she is used to polite business Japanese. Mariya's Japanese is fast and casual. Yến follows it easily, but it is not the kind of Japanese she is used to speaking."},
{"t":"narr","text":"Mariya lives in Room 103. She has been here for a year, and she loves explaining the garbage rules. She starts before Yến has even put down her suitcases. The garbage goes to the ごみステーション (*gomi sutēshon*), the garbage station just down the street. On official signs it is called ごみ[集積所]{しゅうせきじょ}."},
{"t":"gomi","title":"ごみステーション","hint":"Tap a bag to see what goes in it. Every town has its own rules (some have more than twenty types); these are Shioura's main ones.","items":[{"icon":"bag","ja":"もえるごみ","ro":"moeru gomi","en":"burnable garbage","when":"Mon and Thu","note":"Food waste (なまごみ: drain it and wrap it in newspaper first), tissues and anything else that burns, in the city's own see-through bags."},{"icon":"cup","ja":"もえないごみ","ro":"moenai gomi","en":"non-burnable garbage","when":"2nd and 4th Wed","note":"Broken dishes, small metal things, light bulbs. Wrap anything sharp and write きけん (danger) on the bag."},{"icon":"pla","ja":"プラ","ro":"pura","en":"plastic packaging","when":"Tue","note":"Anything with the プラ mark: wrappers, trays, bags, bottle caps. Rinse it first."},{"icon":"pet","ja":"ペットボトル","ro":"petto botoru","en":"plastic (PET) drink bottles","when":"1st and 3rd Wed","note":"Bottles with the PET mark. Take off the caps and labels (they go in プラ), then rinse the bottles and crush them flat."},{"icon":"can","ja":"びん・かん","ro":"bin, kan","en":"glass bottles and cans","when":"1st and 3rd Wed","note":"Glass bottles and drink or food cans, rinsed. Spray cans must be completely empty."},{"icon":"box","ja":"ダンボール・しんぶん","ro":"danbōru, shinbun","en":"cardboard and newspaper","when":"Fri","note":"Flattened cardboard boxes, newspapers and magazines, tied with string. Paper is recycled here, so it doesn't go in burnable garbage."},{"icon":"chair","ja":"そだいごみ","ro":"sodai gomi","en":"large items","when":"by appointment","note":"Furniture, bikes, big appliances. Book a pickup with the city and buy a fee sticker at a convenience store. Air conditioners, TVs, refrigerators and washing machines have their own recycling law."}],"calendar":[["月","げつ","もえるごみ"],["火","か","プラ"],["水","すい","びん・かん・ペットボトル (1st and 3rd), もえないごみ (2nd and 4th)"],["木","もく","もえるごみ"],["金","きん","ダンボール・しんぶん"]],"calnote":"Days of the week are written with kanji; the small kana above each one show how to read it. Garbage goes out by 8 in the morning on its day, never the night before. Food waste goes out twice a week, with the burnables."},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"tip","ja":"プラは かようび！","en":"Plastic goes out on Tuesday!","gl":"かようび: Tuesday.","tag":"proudly","ref":"E1·L4"},
{"t":"note","text":"In a new home, your first Japanese is usually not very exciting. It is names on mailboxes and a garbage calendar. But you will read these every week, so they are worth learning first."},
{"t":"narr","text":"An old man crosses the street from the small house opposite. He has an umbrella under his arm."},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"hello","ja":"さとうさん！ あたらしい ひとです！","en":"Mr. Satō! Our new resident is here!","tag":"calling out","ref":"E1·L5"},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"hello","ja":"おお、よく きたね。","en":"Ah, welcome.","gl":"よく きたね: \"welcome,\" said to someone who has just arrived. Literally, \"you came well.\"","tag":"warmly","ref":"E1·L6"},
{"t":"narr","text":"This is Shōichi-san. He and his wife, Fumiko-san, own the house. He looks up at the sky. It is the same gray as the sea."},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"think","ja":"…あめ。","en":"...Rain.","tag":"quietly, to himself","audio":"雨, high then low.","ref":"E1·L7"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Yến knows he means rain, not candy. She can hear it in the pitch: high, then low. Shōichi-san hangs the umbrella on her suitcase handle and walks back to his house."},
{"t":"narr","text":"A black-and-white cat is watching from the wall. Yến says ミウ quietly. That is a common name for cats in Vietnam. The cat looks at her. Then Mariya calls out ムゥ, her own name for the cat. The cat looks at Mariya. She seems happy with both names."},
{"t":"cat","pose":"curious","alt":"The black-and-white cat, looking up from the wall"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Then it starts to rain, just as Shōichi-san said."},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u1-x1","type":"mcq","q":"Which mailbox belongs to Toby Whitlock?","options":[{"t":"ウィットロック","why":"Right: ウィ (*wi*), ッ (a pause), ト, ロ, ッ, ク.","ok":true},
{"t":"ウイトロク","why":"Close, but this has no pauses. Whitlock has two: a small ッ before ト and another before ク."},
{"t":"モンドラゴン","why":"That's Rodrigo Mondragón, in Room 102."},
{"t":"ウィトロック","why":"Close, but Whitlock has two pauses. This one is missing the small ッ before ト."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u1-x2","type":"mcq","q":"The label on the Satōs' house says さとう. How many beats (morae) does it have?","options":[{"t":"Three","why":"さ・と・う: the long *o* has a beat of its own.","ok":true},
{"t":"Two","why":"Two beats would be さと, like せと (Seto) on Mariya's mailbox. In さとう, the う makes the vowel long and counts as a beat."},
{"t":"Four","why":"There are only three kana here, and each one is one beat."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u1-x3","type":"type","q":"The sign above the gate says *Kamome-sō*. Type it in hiragana.","answer":"かもめそう","why":"かもめそう: か・も・め・そ・う, five beats. Hiragana writes the long *o* with う.","book":"Write *Kamome-sō* in hiragana.","hint":"The long *o* is written with う in hiragana.","wrongs":[{"v":"かもめそ","why":"The *o* in *sō* is long, so it needs a second kana: そう."},{"v":"かもめそお","why":"A long *o* is usually written with う, not お: そう."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u1-x4","type":"mcq","q":"Yến's first piece of garbage at Kamome House is the empty bottle of green tea she drank on the train. It has a plastic cap and a paper-thin plastic label. Where does it all go?","options":[{"t":"The bottle in ペットボトル; the cap and the label in プラ","why":"Right. Read the ペットボトル line again: take off the caps and labels (they go in プラ), then rinse the bottle and crush it.","ok":true},
{"t":"The bottle and the cap in ペットボトル; the label in プラ","why":"The cap is a different plastic from the bottle. Take it off and put it in プラ."},
{"t":"The bottle in ペットボトル; the cap in プラ; the label in もえるごみ","why":"The label is thin like paper, but it's plastic, so it goes in プラ."},
{"t":"The bottle and the label in ペットボトル; the cap in プラ","why":"Take the label off too. Only the bare bottle goes in ペットボトル."}]}},
{"t":"lang","items":["Long vowels: さとう (*Satō*, three beats) and せと (*Seto*, two beats) look alike at first, but the extra beat makes a different name.","Small ッ: the pause in ウィットロック counts as a beat, like the one in きって (stamp).","Pitch: あめ (rain) starts high and goes down. あめ (candy) starts low and goes up. The kana are the same, so you can only tell them apart by ear.","Polite and casual: Yến says ゴー・ハイ・イエンと もうします, the business way. Mariya answers with まりやで いいよ, the friendly way."]},
{"t":"reflect","q":"Which label took you longest to read, and what made it hard?"}]},{"unit":"e3u2","n":2,"title":"はじめまして","month":"April","level":"N5","enDefault":true,"parts":[{"t":"narr","text":"It is the first Sunday in April. On Sundays, the Satōs come over from their house across the street and eat dinner with everyone in the house. Fumiko-san cooks the Sunday dinner. She is a retired elementary-school teacher. On the other days, the residents take turns cooking. The cooking schedule is on the bulletin board."},
{"t":"narr","text":"Cheska is setting the table. She has lived here since October. She came from the Philippines on a scholarship. For her first six months she was a research student, and this April she starts her master's degree. The university dorm only takes new students for one semester, and Cheska didn't want to move twice. So she asked the international office for a place where she could stay for her whole degree, and they sent her here. Her program is taught in English, so her Japanese is still simple. Before she came to Japan, she worked for five years in her city's disaster office."},
{"t":"narr","text":"Her helper tonight is the new man in Room 102. He arrived late last night. All day, he has been waiting for someone to introduce himself to."},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"はじめまして！ロドリゴです！メキシコから[来]{き}ました！","en":"Nice to meet you! I'm Rodrigo! I'm from Mexico!","tag":"excited, loud","ref":"E2·L1"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Rodrigo is twenty-five. He studied art at a university in Mexico. Then he worked for two years at a small animation studio, until it closed. Now he studies at a Japanese language school in town. One day, he wants to work at a Japanese animation studio. He learned a lot of his Japanese from anime. His Japanese is correct, but he talks like an anime hero."},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"はじめまして。チェスカです。フィリピンから[来]{き}ました。","en":"Nice to meet you. I'm Cheska. I'm from the Philippines.","tag":"friendly","ref":"E2·L2"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"hello","ja":"よろしくお[願]{ねが}いします！","en":"I hope we get along!","gl":"よろしくお願いします: what you say after your name when you meet someone. Roughly \"please be kind to me.\"","tag":"excited, loud","ref":"E2·L3"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Cheska gives him a jar of chopsticks. Every pair of chopsticks is different, and each pair belongs to one person. Rodrigo wants to know whose chopsticks are whose."},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"これは、だれのはしですか。","en":"Whose chopsticks are these?","gl":"はし: chopsticks.","tag":"curious","audio":"箸, high then low; not 橋, \"bridge\".","ref":"E2·L4"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"それは、トビーさんのです。","en":"Those are Toby's.","tag":"matter-of-fact","ref":"E2·L5"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"hello","ja":"これは？","en":"And these?","tag":"pointing, eager","ref":"E2·L6"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"まりやさんのです。","en":"Mariya's.","tag":"matter-of-fact","ref":"E2·L7"},
{"t":"narr","text":"At the bottom of the stack of plates, there is a small saucer with a fish painted on it. It is chipped."},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"hello","ja":"これは？","en":"And this?","tag":"intrigued","ref":"E2·L8"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"それは、ミンミンのです。","en":"That's Mingming's.","tag":"fondly","ref":"E2·L9"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"ミンミンさんは、だれですか。[学生]{がくせい}ですか。","en":"Who's Mingming? A student?","tag":"confused","ref":"E2·L10"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"いいえ、[学生]{がくせい}じゃありません。ねこです。","en":"No, not a student. A cat.","tag":"amused","ref":"E2·L11"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Fumiko-san comes in with a dish in each hand. She stops to correct them."},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"tip","ja":"ミンミンじゃありませんよ。ねこさんです。","en":"She isn't Mingming. She's Neko-san.","gl":"ねこさん: \"Ms. Cat,\" Fumiko-san's name for her.","tag":"gently correcting","ref":"E2·L12"},
{"t":"note","text":"The cat doesn't belong to anyone. She visits every evening, and everyone who feeds her gives her a different name. Fumiko-san keeps a list of the names on the bulletin board. She writes it in pencil, because the list keeps growing."},
{"t":"narr","text":"Then the food arrives. Rodrigo looks at the bowl in front of him. It is full of tiny purple squid."},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"hello","ja":"これは[何]{なん}ですか。","en":"What's this?","tag":"peering in, a little wary","ref":"E2·L13"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"それは、いかです。","en":"That's squid.","gl":"いか: squid. These are ほたるいか, firefly squid, a spring food on this coast. Each one is about as long as a thumb.","tag":"casually","ref":"E2·L14"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"あれは、とり[肉]{にく}ですか。","en":"Is that chicken, over there?","gl":"とり肉: chicken (とり, bird + 肉, meat).","tag":"hopeful","ref":"E2·L15"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"いいえ、とり[肉]{にく}じゃありません。たこです。","en":"No, it isn't chicken. It's octopus.","gl":"たこ: octopus. This is たこのからあげ, deep-fried octopus. からあげ is usually chicken, so it is an easy mistake.","tag":"amused","ref":"E2·L16"},
{"t":"narr","text":"One dish is left. It is gray with dark spots, and it is cut into triangles. When Rodrigo leans on the table, it shakes."},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"hello","ja":"じゃあ、これは？","en":"OK, and this?","tag":"suspicious","ref":"E2·L17"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"それは、こんにゃくです。","en":"That's konnyaku.","gl":"こんにゃく: a firm gray jelly made from the root of the konjac plant. It mostly tastes like whatever it was cooked in.","tag":"casually","ref":"E2·L18"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"こんにゃくは[何]{なん}ですか。[魚]{さかな}ですか。","en":"What's konnyaku? Is it fish?","tag":"confused","ref":"E2·L19"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"[魚]{さかな}じゃありません。","en":"It isn't fish.","tag":"patiently","ref":"E2·L20"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"hello","ja":"[肉]{にく}ですか。","en":"Meat?","tag":"guessing","ref":"E2·L21"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"oops","ja":"[肉]{にく}じゃありません。こんにゃくは…こんにゃくです。","en":"It isn't meat. Konnyaku is... konnyaku.","tag":"giving up, laughing","ref":"E2·L22"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Footsteps come down the steep stairs. The other residents arrive one or two at a time. Rodrigo stands up for each person. You can only say はじめまして to someone once, and he doesn't want to miss anyone."},
{"t":"narr","text":"Toby comes first. He is from Australia, and he has lived here since October."},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"はじめまして。トビーです。よろしくお[願]{ねが}いします。","en":"Nice to meet you. I'm Toby. I hope we get along.","tag":"friendly","ref":"E2·L23"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Yến comes next."},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"hello","ja":"はじめまして。ゴー・ハイ・イエンと[申]{もう}します。どうぞよろしくお[願]{ねが}いいたします。","en":"It's a pleasure to meet you. My name is Ngô Hải Yến. I look forward to working with you.","gl":"と申します and お願いいたします: very formal, business-style versions of です and お願いします. You will hear these at work and in shops.","tag":"formal, polished","audio":"read the dots in ゴー・ハイ・イエン as short pauses.","ref":"E2·L24"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Yến worked for four years at a software company in Japan. At work, everyone introduced themselves like this. Now she is doing a master's degree in information engineering. She wants to become a bridge SE (ブリッジSE): an engineer who works between a software team in Vietnam and its clients in Japan. Mariya looks very impressed. She has never heard anyone close to her age talk like this."},
{"t":"narr","text":"Mariya comes in from her room down the hall."},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"yay","ja":"せとまりやです！よろしく！","en":"I'm Mariya Seto! Nice to meet you!","gl":"よろしく: the short, casual よろしくお願いします.","tag":"cheerful","ref":"E2·L25"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Mariya grew up on Shiojima, a small island an hour away by ferry. Her parents run the café at the island's ferry terminal."},
{"t":"narr","text":"Aoi comes down with her bag on her shoulder. She is from Saitama. This month she starts a master's degree in regional disaster and community studies, in the same seminar as Cheska (a small research group with one professor). They have met once, at the university, and they nod to each other now."},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"hello","ja":"ひらかわです。よろしくお[願]{ねが}いします。","en":"I'm Hirakawa. I hope we get along.","tag":"polite, brief","ref":"E2·L26"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Kaito comes last. He is nineteen."},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"hello","ja":"…くぜです。","en":"...Kuze.","tag":"mumbling, shy","ref":"E2·L27"},
{"t":"narr","text":"He looks at the floor when he says it. Then Shōichi-san comes in. He taps the barometer in the hall and sits down. He looks happy with what it says."},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"じゃあ、[食]{た}べましょうか。","en":"All right, let's eat.","tag":"warmly","ref":"E2·L28"},
{"t":"line","who":"Everyone","mood":"hello","ja":"いただきます。","en":"Itadakimasu.","gl":"いただきます: said before every meal. It thanks everyone and everything that went into the food.","tag":"together, cheerful","ref":"E2·L29"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Rodrigo says it a little late, and very loudly. Then he picks up a triangle of konnyaku. He still wants to find out what it is. Cheska watches him eat it."},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"おいしいですか。","en":"Is it good?","tag":"teasing","ref":"E2·L30"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"oops","ja":"……こんにゃくです。","en":"...It's konnyaku.","tag":"chewing, puzzled","ref":"E2·L31"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Aoi eats quickly and leaves early. She is going to help at her grandmother's tea shop on Tsubame Street."},
{"t":"narr","text":"Something moves at the window. A black-and-white cat is sitting on the windowsill. She is looking at the chipped saucer."},
{"t":"cat","pose":"smug","alt":"The cat on the windowsill, looking pleased with herself"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"あ、ねこがいます！ミチ！","en":"Oh, there's a cat! Michi!","gl":"ミチ: *michi*, a word for \"kitty\" in Mexico. ねこがいます: \"there is a cat\" (います is for people and animals).","tag":"excited","ref":"E2·L32"},
{"t":"narr","text":"The cat looks at him. Fumiko-san puts down her chopsticks and goes to get her pencil."},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u2-x1","type":"mcq","q":"Who is ミンミン?","options":[{"t":"The cat","why":"Right. Cheska says ねこです. ミンミン is Cheska's name for her. Fumiko-san calls her ねこさん, and by the end of dinner Rodrigo has added ミチ.","ok":true},
{"t":"A student in the house","why":"That was Rodrigo's guess ([学生]{がくせい}ですか), and Cheska answered いいえ、[学生]{がくせい}じゃありません."},
{"t":"Fumiko-san","why":"Fumiko-san is the one who corrects the name: ミンミンじゃありませんよ。ねこさんです."},
{"t":"The owner of the chopsticks","why":"The chopsticks belong to Toby and Mariya (トビーさんのです, まりやさんのです). ミンミン owns the saucer."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u2-x2","type":"mcq","q":"Rodrigo asks あれは、とり[肉]{にく}ですか. What is the dish?","options":[{"t":"たこ","why":"Right. Cheska answers とり[肉]{にく}じゃありません。たこです. It isn't chicken; it's octopus.","ok":true},
{"t":"とり[肉]{にく}","why":"That was Rodrigo's guess. Cheska says とり[肉]{にく}じゃありません: it is not chicken."},
{"t":"いか","why":"The squid is the bowl right in front of Rodrigo (これ). This dish is farther away (あれ)."},
{"t":"こんにゃく","why":"Konnyaku is the gray dish that shakes."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u2-x3","type":"mcq","q":"Yến says ゴー・ハイ・イエンと[申]{もう}します. What does と申します do?","options":[{"t":"It means \"my name is,\" in a very polite, humble way","why":"Right. Mariya just says せとまりやです. と申します is humble: it makes the speaker sound modest, the way people talk at work.","ok":true},
{"t":"It means \"I'm from\"","why":"\"From\" is から, as in Rodrigo's メキシコから[来]{き}ました."},
{"t":"It means \"please call me\"","why":"That would be like Mariya's まりやで いいよ in E1, and it is casual."},
{"t":"It means \"nice to meet you\"","why":"That is はじめまして, which Yến says first."}]}},
{"t":"lang","items":["これ・それ・あれ: Rodrigo asks about the bowl in front of him with これ. Cheska answers about the same bowl with それ, because it is near him, not her. The plate far from both of them is あれ.","じゃありません: the everyday negative of です. [学生]{がくせい}じゃありません, とり[肉]{にく}じゃありません, [魚]{さかな}じゃありません. Each wrong guess gets a polite correction.","の without the noun: それは、トビーさんのです (*those are Toby's*). When everyone knows you mean the chopsticks, you can leave the word out.","Three ways to say \"nice to meet you\": Mariya's casual よろしく, everyone's よろしくお願いします, and Yến's business-style どうぞよろしくお願いいたします."]},
{"t":"reflect","q":"Rodrigo stands up and says はじめまして to every person who comes down the stairs. What do you do when you walk into a room full of people you don't know yet?"}]},{"unit":"e3u3","n":3,"title":"The rules on the door","month":"April","level":"N5","enDefault":true,"parts":[{"t":"narr","text":"月よう日のあさ八時。","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"It is Monday morning. Rodrigo arrived late on Saturday night and missed the house tour, so Fumiko-san is giving it to him now. Every new resident gets one, and it always starts at the bath door."},
{"t":"narr","text":"Seven people share one bath, so there is a schedule taped to the door. The bath is off the hallway, past the toilets, with a small changing room in front of it. Fumiko-san drew it neatly in pencil: seven names, twenty minutes each. Aoi has already underlined her time twice."},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"tip","ja":"おふろは[一人]{ひとり}[二十分]{にじゅっぷん}です。ロドリゴさんは、[午後]{ごご}[九時]{くじ}から[九時二十分]{くじにじゅっぷん}までです。","en":"The bath is twenty minutes each. Yours is from 9:00 to 9:20 p.m., Rodrigo.","gl":"おふろ: the bath.","tag":"clear, teacherly","ref":"E3·L1"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Because Rodrigo arrived last, he gets the last slot. He doesn't mind, since he likes schedules. He does have a few questions, though."},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"[朝]{あさ}、おふろに[入]{はい}ってもいいですか。","en":"May I take a bath in the morning?","tag":"curious","ref":"E3·L2"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"[朝]{あさ}は、シャワーだけです。","en":"Mornings are showers only.","gl":"だけ: only.","tag":"matter-of-fact","ref":"E3·L3"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"おふろで[歌]{うた}ってもいいですか。","en":"May I sing in the bath?","gl":"歌う (うたう): to sing.","tag":"hopeful","ref":"E3·L4"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"think","ja":"…[小]{ちい}さい[声]{こえ}で[歌]{うた}ってください。","en":"...Please sing quietly.","gl":"声 (こえ): voice. 小さい声で: in a quiet voice.","tag":"pause, patiently","ref":"E3·L5"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Rodrigo has never been asked to sing quietly before. Then he reads the last line on the schedule, which is written in red."},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"「おふろに、わすれものをしてはいけません」。だれがわすれましたか。","en":"\"Do not leave your things in the bath area.\" Who left something?","gl":"わすれもの: something left behind. わすれる: to forget, to leave something behind.","tag":"reading aloud, curious","ref":"E3·L6"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"トビーさんです。","en":"Toby.","tag":"dryly","ref":"E3·L7"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Just then, Toby comes down the stairs from Room 201, sideways, with one hand on the wall. He grew up on an apple farm in Tasmania, in Australia, and taught English at a country school in Japan for two years. Now he is in the second year of a master's degree in Japanese linguistics, taught in Japanese. For his thesis, he hopes to record Shioura's old fishing dialect while there are still people who speak it. He gets along with almost everyone."},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"おはようございます。あ、その[話]{はなし}ですか。[一回]{いっかい}だけですよ。","en":"Morning. Oh, that story. It was only once.","tag":"cheerful, a bit sheepish","ref":"E3·L8"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"tip","ja":"[二回]{にかい}です。シャンプーと、タオルです。","en":"Twice. Your shampoo, and your towel.","tag":"firm but kind","ref":"E3·L9"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"oops","ja":"…すみません。[二回]{にかい}です。もう、わすれません。","en":"...Sorry. It was twice. I won't forget again.","tag":"embarrassed","ref":"E3·L10"},
{"t":"narr","text":"There is a good reason he comes down sideways. Like the stairs in many old Japanese houses, these are so steep they are almost a ladder. Rodrigo looks up at them with great interest."},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"tip","ja":"このかいだんは、あぶないですから、[走]{はし}らないでください。","en":"These stairs are dangerous, so please don't run.","gl":"かいだん: stairs. あぶない: dangerous.","tag":"serious","ref":"E3·L11"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"わかった！[走]{はし}らない！やくそくだ！","en":"Got it! I won't run! That's a promise!","gl":"やくそく: a promise.","tag":"heroic, loud","ref":"E3·L12"},
{"t":"narr","text":"He sounds like an anime hero accepting a mission. Fumiko-san taught young children for thirty-five years, and she knows that tone well."},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"tip","ja":"「わかった」じゃありません。「わかりました」です。","en":"Not \"wakatta.\" \"Wakarimashita.\"","tag":"gently correcting","ref":"E3·L13"},
{"t":"note","text":"わかった and わかりました mean the same thing. The difference is who you say them to. The short, plain forms are for friends and family. With a landlady, you use ます. Fumiko-san will tell you this once, kindly. After that, she expects you to remember."},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"わかりました！","en":"Understood!","tag":"loud, eager","ref":"E3·L14"},
{"t":"narr","text":"He is just as loud as before, but Fumiko-san lets that go, since being loud isn't a grammar mistake. As they move on, she glances at the stairs again. Her husband, Shōichi-san, is seventy-eight. He still climbs them to fix things upstairs when he thinks she isn't looking, and the stairs up to their bedroom in their own house are just as steep."},
{"t":"narr","text":"Next to the stairs, by the toilets, there is an old wooden shelf. People leave broken things on it, and a few days later they are fixed. This morning, a desk lamp is sitting on it, with a brand-new cord. Fumiko-san says it is Mariya's, and that it works now. She doesn't say who fixed it."},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"月よう日のあさ九時。","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Next is the city office. Anyone who moves has to register their new address there within fourteen days, and Fumiko-san offers to go with him. At the bus stop, she starts to tell him the bus times, but Rodrigo already knows them. He even knows that the 9:27 bus takes the long way around the harbor. Fumiko-san looks impressed."},
{"t":"narr","text":"At the city office, the first thing to do is take a numbered ticket."},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"tip","ja":"ここを、おしてください。","en":"Press here, please.","gl":"おす: to push, to press.","tag":"kindly","ref":"E3·L15"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"[四十七番]{よんじゅうななばん}です。[今]{いま}、[何番]{なんばん}ですか。","en":"I'm number 47. What number are they on now?","gl":"～番 (ばん): number ～, in a line or a list.","tag":"cheerful, counting","ref":"E3·L16"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"[三十一番]{さんじゅういちばん}です。すわって、[待]{ま}ってください。","en":"Thirty-one. Please sit down and wait.","gl":"すわる: to sit.","tag":"calmly","ref":"E3·L17"},
{"t":"narr","text":"There are sixteen people ahead of him. While they wait, Fumiko-san helps him with the form: his family name, his given name, and the address he has had for just two days."},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"この[万年筆]{まんねんひつ}で[書]{か}いてもいいですか。","en":"May I write with this fountain pen?","gl":"万年筆 (まんねんひつ): a fountain pen.","tag":"hopeful","ref":"E3·L18"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"think","ja":"…[黒]{くろ}いインクですか。","en":"...Is the ink black?","gl":"黒い (くろい): black. インク: ink.","tag":"pause, careful","ref":"E3·L19"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"[黒]{くろ}です！","en":"It's black!","tag":"proudly","ref":"E3·L20"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"じゃあ、[書]{か}いてもいいですよ。","en":"Then you may.","tag":"smiling","ref":"E3·L21"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Rodrigo only uses fountain pens, and he has eleven bottles of ink at home. He fills in the form slowly and neatly. With fourteen people still ahead of him, he opens his sketchbook and starts to draw, and Fumiko-san leans over to look."},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"think","ja":"[何]{なに}をかいていますか。","en":"What are you drawing?","gl":"かく: here, to draw. It sounds the same as 書く, to write.","tag":"curious","ref":"E3·L22"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"oops","ja":"…さとうさんを、かいています。","en":"...I'm drawing you, Mrs. Satō.","tag":"shy","ref":"E3·L23"},
{"t":"narr","text":"She holds out her hand, and Rodrigo gives her the sketchbook. The drawing is of her, done in just a few lines: her straight back, and her handbag sitting neatly in her lap. She looks at it for a long moment."},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"…もう[一枚]{いちまい}かいてください。しゅじんに[見]{み}せたいです。","en":"...Please draw one more. I want to show my husband.","gl":"もう一枚: one more (sheet). しゅじん: my husband. 見せる: to show.","tag":"softly, touched","ref":"E3·L24"},
{"t":"narr","text":"She gives the sketchbook back with a small smile."},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"ゆうがた。","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"That evening, just after sunset, Rodrigo finds Shōichi-san standing in the garden, looking toward the harbor."},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"さとうさん、[何]{なに}を[見]{み}ていますか。","en":"Mr. Satō, what are you looking at?","tag":"gently","ref":"E3·L25"},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"hello","ja":"とうだいだ。…[三]{さん}びょう、おそい。","en":"The lighthouse. ...Three seconds late.","gl":"とうだい: a lighthouse. びょう: seconds. おそい: late, slow.","tag":"quietly, to himself","ref":"E3·L26"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Out at the end of the long sea wall, the lighthouse has just come on. It is supposed to come on at sunset, but it is always a little late, and Shōichi-san seems to be the only one who notices. He nods to himself and goes back into his house."},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"よる八時五十九分。","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"At 8:59 that night, Rodrigo is waiting in the hallway outside the bath area with his towel. His own room is just across the hall. Mariya comes out with her hair wrapped in a towel and a phone in her hand. The phone is buzzing."},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"tip","ja":"これ、トビーさんのスマホです。だついじょに、ありました。","en":"This is Toby's phone. It was in the changing room.","gl":"スマホ: a smartphone. だついじょ: the changing room in front of the bath.","tag":"amused","ref":"E3·L27"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"tip","ja":"[三回目]{さんかいめ}ですね。","en":"That makes three times.","gl":"三回目 (さんかいめ): the third time.","tag":"teasing","ref":"E3·L28"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"tip","ja":"ロドリゴさんは、さいごですから、おゆをぬいてくださいね。","en":"You're last, Rodrigo, so please let the water out when you're done.","gl":"さいご: the last. おゆ: hot water. ぬく: to pull out; here, to drain.","tag":"friendly","ref":"E3·L29"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"わかりました！やくそくです！","en":"Understood! That's a promise!","tag":"eager","ref":"E3·L30"},
{"t":"narr","text":"He remembers the ます this time. He takes the phone to the foot of the stairs, without running."},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"hello","ja":"トビーさん、[電話]{でんわ}ですよ！","en":"Toby, your phone's ringing!","tag":"calling out loudly","ref":"E3·L31"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Toby comes down sideways and takes it."},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"oops","ja":"あ…すみません。また、わすれました。","en":"Oh... I'm sorry. I forgot it again.","tag":"sincere, flustered","ref":"E3·L32"},
{"t":"narr","text":"He bows to Mariya, and then to Rodrigo, who has been waiting with his towel. The screen says *Home*. It is nearly ten at night in Tasmania, which is late for his family to call."},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"あ、だいじょうぶです。[後]{あと}でかけます。","en":"Oh, it's fine. I'll call back later.","gl":"だいじょうぶ: fine, all right. 電話をかける: to make a phone call.","tag":"brightly, too quickly","ref":"E3·L33"},
{"t":"narr","text":"He smiles, and the buzzing stops. He puts the phone in his pocket and goes back upstairs. When Rodrigo comes out of the bath at 9:19 (he did sing, but quietly, and he let the water out), the house is quiet upstairs. He doesn't call back that night."},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u3-x1","type":"mcq","q":"Fumiko-san says このかいだんは、あぶないですから、[走]{はし}らないでください. What is she asking Rodrigo to do?","options":[{"t":"Not to run on the stairs, because they are dangerous","why":"Right. ～ないでください is \"please don't,\" and から gives her reason: あぶないですから, because they are dangerous.","ok":true},
{"t":"To run, because he is late","why":"[走]{はし}ってください would be \"please run.\" She says [走]{はし}らないでください, with the ない-form: please don't."},
{"t":"Not to use the stairs at all","why":"She only says not to run ([走]{はし}る). Toby uses the stairs a moment earlier, slowly and sideways, and that is fine."},
{"t":"To be quiet on the stairs","why":"The quiet was for the bath: [小]{ちい}さい[声]{こえ}で[歌]{うた}ってください. On the stairs, the problem is speed."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u3-x2","type":"mcq","q":"Which of these is against the rules at Kamome House?","options":[{"t":"おふろに、わすれものをします。","why":"Right. The line in red says おふろに、わすれものをしてはいけません: you must not leave your things in the bath area. Toby has done it [二回]{にかい}, and that night his phone makes it [三回目]{さんかいめ}.","ok":true},
{"t":"おふろで[小]{ちい}さい[声]{こえ}で[歌]{うた}います。","why":"That is allowed. Rodrigo asked [歌]{うた}ってもいいですか, and Fumiko-san answered [小]{ちい}さい[声]{こえ}で[歌]{うた}ってください."},
{"t":"[朝]{あさ}、シャワーをつかいます。","why":"That's fine: [朝]{あさ}は、シャワーだけです. It is a morning bath that isn't allowed."},
{"t":"[黒]{くろ}いインクで[書]{か}きます。","why":"That was at the city office, and Fumiko-san said [書]{か}いてもいいですよ: you may."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u3-x3","type":"type","q":"Rodrigo answers Fumiko-san with わかった. Type the polite form she asks for instead, in hiragana.","answer":"わかりました","why":"わかりました: The polite past of わかる. It means the same as わかった; it is the one you say to a landlady.","book":"Write the polite (ます) past form of わかる in hiragana.","hint":"わかった is a plain past form, so you need the polite past: ～ました.","wrongs":[{"v":"わかります","why":"That is polite, but it is the present. わかった is past, so the polite form is past too: わかりました."},{"v":"わかった","why":"That is the plain form Rodrigo used. Mrs. Satō wants the ます version: わかりました."}]}},
{"t":"lang","items":["～てもいいですか asks for permission. Rodrigo uses it three times: [入]{はい}ってもいいですか, [歌]{うた}ってもいいですか, [書]{か}いてもいいですか. Only the last one gets a yes, after one question: [書]{か}いてもいいですよ.","A rule and a request: the door says おふろに、わすれものをしてはいけません (*you must not*). That is a rule for everyone. Fumiko-san says [走]{はし}らないでください (*please don't*). That is a request to one person. Mariya's おゆをぬいてくださいね is a request too, made friendlier with ね.","Counters: [一人]{ひとり}, [二十分]{にじゅっぷん}, [二回]{にかい}, [三回目]{さんかいめ}, [四十七番]{よんじゅうななばん}, もう[一枚]{いちまい}, [三]{さん}びょう. People, minutes, times, numbers in a line, sheets of paper and seconds each have their own counting word."]},
{"t":"reflect","q":"Fumiko-san corrects Rodrigo once and then trusts him to remember. When someone corrects your Japanese, what makes the correction easy to accept?"}]},{"unit":"e3u4","n":4,"title":"The bulletin board","month":"May","level":"N5","enDefault":true,"parts":[{"t":"narr","text":"五月九日（土）のあさ。","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"It is Saturday, May 9. The bulletin board by the front door holds everything the house needs to know: the garbage calendar, the cooking schedule, and Fumiko-san's list of the cat's names, which now has eight names on it. This morning, there is a new notice pinned in the middle."},
{"t":"plates","title":"The notice","hint":"Read each line of the notice, then tap it to check.","items":[{"ja":"なりはま クリーンデー","ro":"Nari-hama kurīn dē","who":"Nari-hama Cleanup Day. Nari-hama, the \"singing beach,\" is a beach outside the harbor. Its sand squeaks when you walk on it, but only when it is very clean, so every May the whole town comes out to clean it."},{"ja":"五月十七日（日）","ro":"ごがつ じゅうしちにち（にちようび）","who":"Sunday, May 17. The kanji in parentheses is the first kanji of 日よう日 (*nichiyōbi*), Sunday."},{"ja":"午前八時から十時まで","ro":"ごぜん はちじ から じゅうじ まで","who":"From 8 to 10 in the morning. 午前 is a.m.; p.m. is 午後."},{"ja":"雨の日は[中止]{ちゅうし}です","ro":"あめの ひは ちゅうしです","who":"*If it rains, it's canceled.* 雨 (rain) is an N5 kanji. 中止 means canceled."},{"ja":"七人で行きましょう！","ro":"しちにんで いきましょう","who":"*Let's go, all seven of us!* Fumiko-san added this at the bottom in pencil. Everyone is expected to come.","audio":"しちにん"}]},
{"t":"narr","text":"Rodrigo is in the genkan, the entrance where everyone takes off their shoes, putting his shoes on. Today is his first day at his new part-time job, on the packing line at the seafood plant by the harbor. The plant hires a lot of foreign students who are still learning Japanese, and it is close enough to walk to. Mariya stops at the board on her way out."},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"yay","ja":"[五月十七日]{ごがつじゅうしちにち}、[日]{にち}よう[日]{び}！ロドリゴさんも[行]{い}きますか。","en":"May 17, a Sunday! Are you going too, Rodrigo?","tag":"cheerful","ref":"E4·L1"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"[行]{い}きます！なりはまは、どこですか。","en":"I'm going! Where's Nari-hama?","tag":"excited","ref":"E4·L2"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"tip","ja":"みなとの[外]{そと}です。なりはまのすなは、なきますよ。","en":"Just outside the harbor. The sand on Nari-hama sings, you know.","gl":"みなと: a harbor. すな: sand. なく: here, to make a sound, like a bird. Sand that squeaks like this is called なきすな, \"singing sand.\"","tag":"playful","ref":"E4·L3"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"すなが…なきますか。","en":"The sand... sings?","tag":"skeptical","ref":"E4·L4"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"yay","ja":"はい。キュッ、キュッ、となきます。","en":"Yes. It goes kyu, kyu.","tag":"delighted, imitating the sound","ref":"E4·L5"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Rodrigo says he will believe it when he hears it, and hurries off to the plant."},
{"t":"narr","text":"Mariya is in her second year at the university, studying English because she wants to become an interpreter. Next to the cleanup notice, she pins up a small poster of her own: the university's study-abroad program. Applications are due in the fall."},
{"t":"narr","text":"Fumiko-san needs the buckets and tongs for the beach. They are in the downstairs storeroom, along with many years of the Satō family's old things. She asks the first two people who come down the stairs."},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"どうぐは、ものおきの[中]{なか}にあります。トビーさん、あおいさん、お[願]{ねが}いします。","en":"The equipment is in the storeroom. Toby, Aoi, could you get it, please?","gl":"どうぐ: tools, equipment. ものおき: a storeroom.","tag":"kindly","ref":"E4·L6"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"think","ja":"ものおきの、どこですか。","en":"Where in the storeroom?","tag":"brisk","ref":"E4·L7"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"think","ja":"…[中]{なか}です。","en":"...Inside.","tag":"pause, vaguely","ref":"E4·L8"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"ものおき。","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Toby has known this house since he was fifteen, when he stayed with the Satōs for three weeks on a sister-city school exchange. Aoi moved here from Tokyo, where she went to university. She still hasn't unpacked all her boxes. The two of them don't quite get along yet. Aoi suspects nobody is really as polite as Toby seems, and Toby thinks Aoi is a little cold. Neither of them says so."},
{"t":"narr","text":"The storeroom is at the front of the house, next to the bath. It is one of the biggest rooms in the house, and the most crowded. There are boxes everywhere, each one labeled in Fumiko-san's firm handwriting."},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"[上]{うえ}のはこは、「[本]{ほん}」です。","en":"The top box says \"Books.\"","gl":"はこ: a box.","tag":"reading aloud","ref":"E4·L9"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"hello","ja":"[下]{した}のはこは？","en":"And the one under it?","tag":"impatient","ref":"E4·L10"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"「[古]{ふる}い[本]{ほん}」です。","en":"\"Old books.\"","tag":"reading aloud","ref":"E4·L11"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"sleepy","ja":"その[右]{みぎ}は？","en":"And the one to the right of that?","tag":"sighs","ref":"E4·L12"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"oops","ja":"…「もっと[古]{ふる}い[本]{ほん}」です。","en":"...\"Older books.\"","gl":"もっと: more.","tag":"apologetic","ref":"E4·L13"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Toby lifts each box down carefully. When he bumps one, he apologizes to it. Aoi rolls her eyes."},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"tip","ja":"トビーさん、[時間]{じかん}がありません。[大]{おお}きいはこは、[外]{そと}に[出]{だ}してください。","en":"Toby, we don't have time. Please put the big boxes outside.","tag":"impatient","ref":"E4·L14"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"think","ja":"この[小]{ちい}さいはこは？「すてないでください」です。","en":"What about this small one? It says \"Please do not throw away.\"","gl":"すてる: to throw away.","tag":"curious","ref":"E4·L15"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"think","ja":"[中]{なか}は[何]{なん}ですか。","en":"What's in it?","tag":"curious","ref":"E4·L16"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"oops","ja":"…[古]{ふる}いラジオです。[三]{みっ}つあります。","en":"...Old radios. Three of them.","tag":"softly","ref":"E4·L17"},
{"t":"narr","text":"That label is in different handwriting, small and very neat: Shōichi-san's. He was an engineer on the harbor ferry for forty years, and he still likes to fix things. Toby puts the radios back exactly where they were."},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"あおいさんは、もうなりはまへ[行]{い}きましたか。","en":"Have you been to Nari-hama yet, Aoi?","tag":"friendly","audio":"へ is read \"e\".","ref":"E4·L18"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"oops","ja":"…まだです。[時間]{じかん}がありませんから。","en":"...Not yet. I haven't had the time.","tag":"awkward","ref":"E4·L19"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Aoi explains that she came to Shioura to be near her grandmother, and that she is only here for two years, so the beach isn't important to her. But Toby notices sand in the cuffs of her jeans, as if she has been walking on a beach very recently. He is too polite to mention it."},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"yay","ja":"あ、ありました。バケツが[三]{みっ}つ、トングが[七本]{ななほん}。","en":"Oh, here they are. Three buckets and seven pairs of tongs.","gl":"バケツ: a bucket. トング: tongs.","tag":"pleased","ref":"E4·L20"},
{"t":"narr","text":"The equipment is at the very back of the room. Behind the buckets, on the lowest shelf, there is an old cookie tin pushed against the wall. The cat, who has been watching them all morning from the top of the boxes, jumps down and sits next to it."},
{"t":"cat","pose":"curious","alt":"The cat sitting beside the cookie tin, ears forward"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"think","ja":"センセイ、それは[何]{なん}ですか。","en":"Sensei, what's that?","gl":"センセイ: \"Teacher,\" Toby's name for the cat. He says she showed him all the back streets.","tag":"softly, like talking to a pet","ref":"E4·L21"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"think","ja":"…ねこに、ですか。","en":"...You're asking the cat?","tag":"deadpan","ref":"E4·L22"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Aoi says she never gives names to stray cats."},
{"t":"narr","text":"Aoi opens the tin. Inside are bundles of thin, light-blue airmail envelopes, tied with kitchen string. The stamps are Australian, and all the letters come from the same sender in Tasmania. Toby looks surprised. He grew up in Tasmania."},
{"t":"plates","title":"In the tin","hint":"Three things are written in Japanese. Read each one, then tap to check.","items":[{"ja":"文子","ro":"ふみこ","who":"Written inside the lid with a brush, in a schoolgirl's handwriting: *Fumiko*. This is Fumiko-san's name. 文 means writing or letters. 子 (child) is at the end of many girls' names from her generation."},{"ja":"汐浦市 川南 126","ro":"しおうらし かわみなみ ひゃくにじゅうろく","who":"The address on every envelope is written in English, but under it, the sender has carefully copied the kanji too: 126 Kawaminami, Shioura. 川 is river and 南 is south. Neither of them has ever seen this address on a street sign in Shioura."},{"ja":"一九六八年 二月 三日","ro":"せんきゅうひゃくろくじゅうはちねん にがつ みっか","who":"February 3, 1968. It is written in pencil on the back of the top envelope, in the same schoolgirl handwriting as the name inside the lid. Fumiko-san wrote down the day each letter arrived. This is the latest date in the tin."}]},
{"t":"note","text":"The way someone writes kanji tells you something about them. On these envelopes, the address is in English, but the writer also copied the kanji underneath, stroke by stroke, like a drawing. She couldn't read Japanese, and she wrote the water part of 汐 and 浦 from the bottom up. You can see where each stroke starts. Still, every kanji has the right shape."},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"think","ja":"[一九六八年]{せんきゅうひゃくろくじゅうはちねん}の[二月]{にがつ}…。","en":"February 1968...","tag":"surprised, quietly","ref":"E4·L23"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"hello","ja":"[五十年以上]{ごじゅうねんいじょう}[前]{まえ}ですね。[読]{よ}みたいです。","en":"That's more than fifty years ago. I want to read them.","tag":"eager","ref":"E4·L24"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"tip","ja":"[読]{よ}んではいけません。さとうさんのてがみですから。","en":"We shouldn't. They're Mrs. Satō's letters.","gl":"てがみ: a letter.","tag":"firm, gentle","ref":"E4·L25"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"tip","ja":"[中]{なか}は[読]{よ}みません。[外]{そと}だけです。","en":"I won't read the letters. Just the envelopes.","tag":"stubborn","ref":"E4·L26"},
{"t":"narr","text":"It is the first thing they have agreed on all morning. They look through every bundle. The address is always the same, written in the same careful kanji, and the dates run from 1963 to 1968, then stop. They are still looking when Fumiko-san comes to the doorway."},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"あら。それは、[私]{わたし}のです。[古]{ふる}いてがみです。","en":"Oh! Those are mine. They're old letters.","tag":"lightly, a little too quickly","ref":"E4·L27"},
{"t":"narr","text":"She takes the tin from Aoi and tucks it under her arm, as if it were nothing special."},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"バケツは、[三]{みっ}つありましたか。","en":"Were there three buckets?","tag":"casually, changing the subject","ref":"E4·L28"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"はい、[三]{みっ}つありました。","en":"Yes. Three.","tag":"politely","ref":"E4·L29"},
{"t":"narr","text":"She nods and carries the tin back to her house across the street. Aoi and Toby look at each other, but neither of them asks about it."},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"ゆうがた。","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"By evening, all seven residents have written their names under the cleanup notice. Writing your name there means you are coming."},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"五月十七日（日）、なりはま。","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"On Sunday morning, the beach is full of people with bags and tongs. The Satōs' daughter, Megumi, has come too. She is a nurse at the city hospital, and on Sundays she often brings her father's medicine. Her son, Sōta, is nine. He runs straight to his grandfather."},
{"t":"line","who":"sota","mood":"yay","ja":"おじいちゃん、にゃん[助]{すけ}は？","en":"Grandpa, where's Nyansuke?","gl":"にゃん助: Sōta's name for the cat.","tag":"excited, out of breath","ref":"E4·L30"},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"tip","ja":"にゃん[太郎]{たろう}だ。","en":"Nyantarō.","tag":"gruffly","ref":"E4·L31"},
{"t":"line","who":"sota","mood":"hello","ja":"にゃん[助]{すけ}！","en":"Nyansuke!","tag":"insisting, cheeky","ref":"E4·L32"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Two more names for the cat. Both of them are already on Fumiko-san's list. By ten o'clock, the bags are full, and the beach is clean. Rodrigo takes one careful step on the dry sand."},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"…ないた！すなが、ないた！","en":"...It sang! The sand sang!","tag":"amazed, excited","ref":"E4·L33"},
{"t":"narr","text":"Everyone laughs, and then everyone tries it. Aoi doesn't. She walks straight to the quietest part of the beach, where the sand sings best, as if she already knows where it is. Toby notices. He doesn't say anything."},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u4-x1","type":"mcq","q":"The notice says 五月十七日（日）午前八時から十時まで. When is the cleanup?","options":[{"t":"Sunday, May 17, from 8 to 10 in the morning","why":"Right. 五月 is May, 十七日 is the 17th, （日） is Sunday, and 午前 puts 八時から十時まで in the morning.","ok":true},
{"t":"Sunday, May 17, from 8 to 10 in the evening","why":"The evening would be 午後. The notice says 午前: before noon."},
{"t":"Monday, May 17, from 8 to 10 in the morning","why":"Monday is （月）. The kanji in the brackets is 日, for 日よう日, Sunday."},
{"t":"Sunday, May 7, from 8 to 10 in the morning","why":"七日 would be the 7th. The notice says 十七日: ten and seven, the 17th."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u4-x2","type":"mcq","q":"The latest date in the tin is 一九六八年二月三日. Which date is that?","options":[{"t":"February 3, 1968","why":"Right. 一九六八年 gives the year one digit at a time, 二月 is February, and 三日 (みっか) is the 3rd.","ok":true},
{"t":"March 2, 1968","why":"Japanese dates go from big to small: year, then month (月), then day (日). 二月三日 is month 2, day 3."},
{"t":"February 3, 1986","why":"Read the digits in order: 一・九・六・八. Six comes before eight, so it is 1968."},
{"t":"February 3, 1698","why":"Read the digits in order: 一・九・六・八. Nine comes before six, so it is 1968."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u4-x3","type":"mcq","q":"In the storeroom, Aoi counts バケツが[三]{みっ}つ、トングが[七本]{ななほん}. Why does she use 本 for the tongs?","options":[{"t":"本 counts long, thin things","why":"Right. Tongs, pens, bottles and umbrellas are counted with 本. Buckets get the general counter つ.","ok":true},
{"t":"本 means \"book\"","why":"It does, in [古]{ふる}い[本]{ほん}. But after a number, 本 is a counter for long, thin things."},
{"t":"本 counts people","why":"People are counted with 人, as in 七人で行きましょう."},
{"t":"本 means there are many","why":"The number in front of it, 七, says how many. 本 only says what kind of thing is being counted."}]}},
{"t":"lang","items":["One kanji, three readings: 日 is にち in 十七日, ひ in 雨の日, and か in 三日 (みっか). The word around it tells you which one.","Position words do the pointing in the storeroom: [上]{うえ}のはこ, [下]{した}のはこ, その[右]{みぎ}, ものおきの[中]{なか}, [外]{そと}に[出]{だ}してください.","A year can be written digit by digit, as in 一九六八年, but it is read as one number: せんきゅうひゃくろくじゅうはちねん."]},
{"t":"reflect","q":"Toby and Aoi agree to read only the outsides of the envelopes. Where would you have drawn the line?"}]},{"unit":"e3u5","n":5,"title":"Kitchen talk","month":"June","level":"N4","enDefault":true,"parts":[{"t":"narr","text":"四月、[文子]{ふみこ}さんはロドリゴに言いました。「『わかった』じゃありません。『わかりました』です。」五月、トビーとあおいは、ものおきで[古]{ふる}い[手紙]{てがみ}のかんを見つけました。文子さんは「私のです」とだけ言って、かんを[持]{も}って行きました。","en":"In April, Fumiko-san told Rodrigo, \"Not wakatta. Wakarimashita.\" In May, Toby and Aoi found a tin of old letters in the storeroom. Fumiko-san only said they were hers, and took the tin away.","recap":true,"lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"六月です。つゆに[入]{はい}って、毎日雨です。かいだんのそばのたなに、まりやのかさがあります。[風]{かぜ}で、こわれました。[木曜日]{もくようび}の午後五時半。かもめそうの[台所]{だいどころ}です。","en":"June. The rainy season has started, and it rains every day. On the shelf by the stairs is Mariya's umbrella. The wind broke it. Thursday, 5:30 p.m., in the kitchen at Kamome House.","gl":"つゆ: the rainy season, from about June to mid-July.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"台所のコンロは[古]{ふる}くて、右の[火]{ひ}は、よくつきません。かいとは、左の火で、大きいなべにお[湯]{ゆ}をわかしています。そこへ、ロドリゴが来ました。キャベツを一つ[持]{も}っています。","en":"The stove is old, and the right-hand burner often doesn't light. Kaito is heating water in the big pot on the left burner. Then Rodrigo comes in, holding a cabbage.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"oops","ja":"あの…[今日]{きょう}は、ぼくの[番]{ばん}ですけど。","en":"Um... it's my turn today, actually.","gl":"番 (ばん): a turn. ～けど: \"but…\", left hanging to make what you say softer.","tag":"hesitant","ref":"E5·L1"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"え？[今日]{きょう}はぼくの[番]{ばん}ですよ。チェスカさんが「[木曜日]{もくようび}、お[願]{ねが}い」と言いました。","en":"What? It's my turn today. Cheska said, \"Thursday, please.\"","tag":"surprised","ref":"E5·L2"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"oops","ja":"…ぼくにも言いました。グループチャットで。","en":"...She said it to me too. In the group chat.","tag":"quietly, holding up his phone","ref":"E5·L3"},
{"t":"narr","text":"チェスカは、[料理]{りょうり}がきらいです。だから、料理の番を、よくほかの人にたのみます。そのかわり、その人のそうじの番を[二回]{にかい}します。でも[今週]{こんしゅう}は、[同]{おな}じ[木曜日]{もくようび}を、二人にたのみました。こんなことは、はじめてです。","en":"Cheska hates cooking, so she often asks other people to take her cooking turns. In return, she does two of their cleaning turns. But this week she asked two people for the same Thursday. That has never happened before.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"チェスカは、ロドリゴには[朝]{あさ}ごはんのときに、かいとにはグループチャットでたのみました。ロドリゴは、グループチャットを読みません。[漢字]{かんじ}が[多]{おお}くて、むずかしいからです。かいとは、[夜]{よる}、コンビニでアルバイトをしています。だから、朝ごはんのときはねむくて、あまり話しません。それで、二人とも、チェスカがもう一人にもたのんだことを、[知]{し}りませんでした。","en":"Cheska asked Rodrigo at breakfast, and Kaito in the group chat. Rodrigo doesn't read the group chat, because there is too much kanji. Kaito works night shifts at a convenience store, so he is sleepy at breakfast and hardly talks. So neither of them knew she had asked the other one too.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"hello","ja":"かいと、もう[二か月]{にかげつ}だよ。「です・ます」はいらない。[友]{とも}だちだから。","en":"Kaito, it's been two months. We don't need desu and masu. We're friends.","tag":"warm, big-brotherly","ref":"E5·L4"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"think","ja":"…いいんですか。","en":"...Is that really OK?","tag":"unsure","ref":"E5·L5"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"いいんだ！","en":"It is!","tag":"enthusiastic","ref":"E5·L6"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"oops","ja":"…うん。じゃあ、[今日]{きょう}、おれの[番]{ばん}。","en":"...OK. Then today's my turn.","gl":"おれ: a rough, casual \"I\" that men use with friends. ぼく is the softer one.","tag":"shy, then a little bolder","ref":"E5·L7"},
{"t":"narr","text":"かいとのため[口]{ぐち}は、ことばがとても[少]{すく}ないです。ロドリゴのため口は、アニメのヒーローのため口です。","en":"Kaito's casual Japanese uses very few words. Rodrigo's is the casual Japanese of anime heroes.","gl":"ため口 (ためぐち): casual speech, the way friends talk to each other.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"ちがう！[今日]{きょう}はおれの[番]{ばん}だ！このキャベツを見ろ！","en":"No way! Today is MY turn! Look at this cabbage!","gl":"見ろ: \"Look!\", the blunt command form of 見る. Anime heroes use it all the time; housemates almost never do.","tag":"dramatic, heroic","ref":"E5·L8"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"sleepy","ja":"見てる。キャベツだね。","en":"I'm looking. It's a cabbage.","tag":"deadpan","ref":"E5·L9"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"これで[七人]{しちにん}のばんごはんを[作]{つく}る！","en":"With this, I will make dinner for seven!","gl":"ばんごはん: dinner.","tag":"proudly","ref":"E5·L10"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"think","ja":"…キャベツ[一]{ひと}つで？","en":"...With one cabbage?","tag":"doubtful","ref":"E5·L11"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"oops","ja":"…たまごもある。","en":"...There are eggs too.","tag":"sheepish","ref":"E5·L12"},
{"t":"narr","text":"かいとの[家]{いえ}は、[岐阜]{ぎふ}の山の[町]{まち}のそばやです。かいとは、子どものときから、[店]{みせ}を[手伝]{てつだ}っています。だから、やさいを見て、すぐねだんが[分]{わ}かります。キャベツ一つと、たまご。七人で、六百円ぐらいです。","en":"Kaito's family runs a soba shop in a mountain town in Gifu, and he has helped there since he was a child. He can tell what a dinner costs at a glance. One cabbage and some eggs: about six hundred yen for seven people.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"ロドリゴのばんごはんは、いつも[一番]{いちばん}[安]{やす}いです。かいとは、それを[知]{し}っています。でも、何も言いません。","en":"Rodrigo's dinners are always the cheapest. Kaito knows this, but he doesn't say anything.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"think","ja":"…おれ、そば[作]{つく}りたいんだけど。","en":"...I kind of wanted to make soba, though.","gl":"そば: buckwheat noodles. ～んだけど: a soft way to say something and leave the sentence open, like \"…, though.\"","tag":"mumbling","ref":"E5·L13"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"tip","ja":"だめだ！チェスカに「おれが[作]{つく}る」と言った。やくそくはやくそくだ！","en":"No! I told Cheska, \"I'll cook.\" A promise is a promise!","gl":"やくそく: a promise.","tag":"dramatic","ref":"E5·L14"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"sleepy","ja":"おれも「やる」って言ったよ。","en":"I said \"I'll do it\" too.","gl":"やる: to do (casual). って: the casual と for quoting.","tag":"flat, stubborn","ref":"E5·L15"},
{"t":"narr","text":"二人とも、「いいよ」と言いません。なべのお[湯]{ゆ}が、ぐらぐらわいています。中には、何も[入]{はい}っていません。","en":"Neither of them says, \"OK, you do it.\" The water in the pot is boiling hard, with nothing in it.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"ガチャ。ドアが[開]{あ}いて、イエンが大学から[帰]{かえ}って来ました。スーパーのふくろを[持]{も}っています。","en":"The door clicks open, and Yến comes in, back from the university. She is carrying a grocery bag.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"hello","ja":"お[疲]{つか}れさまです。お[話]{はな}し[中]{ちゅう}、[失礼]{しつれい}いたします。[冷蔵庫]{れいぞうこ}を[使]{つか}ってもよろしいでしょうか。","en":"Good evening, both of you. Excuse me for interrupting. Would it be all right if I used the refrigerator?","gl":"お疲れさまです: the greeting coworkers give each other. 失礼いたします: \"excuse me\", very formal. 冷蔵庫 (れいぞうこ): fridge. よろしいでしょうか: a very polite いいですか.","tag":"formal, polished","ref":"E5·L16"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"oops","ja":"…どうぞ。","en":"...Go ahead.","tag":"mumbling","ref":"E5·L17"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"もちろんだ！","en":"Of course!","tag":"booming","ref":"E5·L18"},
{"t":"narr","text":"イエンのうしろに、[文子]{ふみこ}さんもいます。[新聞]{しんぶん}でつつんだ[物]{もの}をかかえています。文子さんは、ドアの外で、三人の話をぜんぶ聞いていました。アニメのヒーローの日本語。ことばの[少]{すく}ない、かいとの日本語。[会社]{かいしゃ}の[会議]{かいぎ}の日本語。でも、文子さんは、一人の日本語だけ、なおします。","en":"Fumiko-san is behind Yến, holding something wrapped in newspaper. She has been outside the door and heard all three: anime-hero Japanese, Kaito's few-word Japanese and business-meeting Japanese. But she only corrects one of them.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"tip","ja":"イエンさん、ここは[会社]{かいしゃ}じゃありませんよ。うちです。「[冷蔵庫]{れいぞうこ}、[使]{つか}うね」でいいんです。","en":"Yến, this isn't an office. It's home. \"I'm using the fridge, OK?\" is all you need.","gl":"うち: home, our place. ～でいい: ～ is fine, ～ is enough.","tag":"gently, smiling","ref":"E5·L19"},
{"t":"note","text":"Being more polite is not always better. Politeness also puts distance between people. In April, Fumiko-san asked Rodrigo to be more polite to her, his landlady. In June, she asks Yến to be less polite with her housemates. It is the same lesson both times: speak the way the people around you speak. She doesn't correct Rodrigo's おれの番だ, because he is talking to a friend, in a kitchen."},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"think","ja":"…[冷蔵庫]{れいぞうこ}、[使]{つか}う…ね。","en":"...I'm using the fridge... OK?","tag":"hesitant, trying it out","ref":"E5·L20"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"hello","ja":"うん。","en":"Yeah.","tag":"casually","ref":"E5·L21"},
{"t":"narr","text":"イエンが、この[家]{いえ}ではじめて言ったため[口]{ぐち}です。お[客]{きゃく}さんの前で話すのは、かんたんです。でも、これはむずかしかったです。かいとは、いつもと[同]{おな}じ[声]{こえ}で、「うん」と言いました。","en":"It is the first casual sentence Yến has said in this house. Speaking in front of clients is easy for her, but this was hard. Kaito just says \"Yeah,\" the way he always does.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"文子さんが、新聞を[開]{ひら}きました。","en":"Fumiko-san opens the newspaper.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"[港]{みなと}で、あじが[安]{やす}かったんです。[七匹]{ななひき}で[八百円]{はっぴゃくえん}。だれが[料理]{りょうり}しますか。","en":"The horse mackerel was cheap at the harbor. Seven for eight hundred yen. Who's cooking?","gl":"港 (みなと): harbor. あじ: horse mackerel, a small silver fish.","tag":"pleased","ref":"E5·L22"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[魚]{さかな}が七ひき、こちらを見ています。ロドリゴは、四月のほたるいかを[思]{おも}い出しました。","en":"Seven fish look up at them. Rodrigo remembers the firefly squid back in April.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"oops","ja":"…これ、どうやって[切]{き}るんだ？","en":"...How do you cut one of these?","gl":"どうやって: how, in what way.","tag":"nervous","ref":"E5·L23"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"think","ja":"[魚]{さかな}の[工場]{こうじょう}で[働]{はたら}いてるのに？","en":"But don't you work at the seafood plant?","gl":"工場 (こうじょう): a factory, a plant. ～のに: even though. Rodrigo works part-time, some evenings, on the packing line at the seafood plant by the harbor.","tag":"surprised","ref":"E5·L24"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"oops","ja":"おれは、[箱]{はこ}に入れるだけだ！","en":"I just put them in boxes!","tag":"defensive","ref":"E5·L25"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"tip","ja":"おれが[切]{き}る。ロドリゴはキャベツ[切]{き}って。ごはんもたいて。","en":"I'll do the fish. You cut the cabbage. And cook the rice.","gl":"切って, たいて: the て-form on its own is a casual request, a short ～てください. ごはんをたく: to cook rice.","tag":"calm, taking charge","ref":"E5·L26"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"じゃあ、[今日]{きょう}はだれの[番]{ばん}だ？","en":"Then whose turn is it today?","tag":"confused","ref":"E5·L27"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"hello","ja":"…[二人]{ふたり}の[番]{ばん}。","en":"...Both of us. It's our turn.","tag":"quietly","ref":"E5·L28"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"[二人]{ふたり}の[番]{ばん}か！よし、行くぞ、かいと！","en":"Both of us! Right. Here we go, Kaito!","gl":"ぞ: a rough, hero-style よ.","tag":"fired up","ref":"E5·L29"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"sleepy","ja":"…[台所]{だいどころ}だよ、ここ。","en":"...This is a kitchen, you know.","gl":"台所 (だいどころ): kitchen.","tag":"deadpan","ref":"E5·L30"},
{"t":"narr","text":"トントントン。ロドリゴが、キャベツを[切]{き}っています。まだ半分です。かいとは、[魚]{さかな}を七ひきぜんぶ、もうさばきました。","en":"Chop, chop, chop. Rodrigo is cutting the cabbage, and he is only halfway through. Kaito has already cleaned and cut all seven fish.","gl":"さばく: to clean and cut up a fish.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"まどの外に、白と[黒]{くろ}の[顔]{かお}が見えます。ねこです。ほうちょうを、じっと見ています。","en":"There is a black-and-white face at the window. It is the cat, staring at the knife.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"cat","pose":"smug","alt":"The cat at the kitchen window"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"hello","ja":"ししょう、まだだよ。","en":"Not yet, Master.","gl":"ししょう (師匠): the master of a craft. It is Kaito's name for the cat, who supervises his cooking.","tag":"softly, to the cat","ref":"E5·L31"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"think","ja":"…ししょう？","en":"...Master?","tag":"curious","ref":"E5·L32"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[文子]{ふみこ}さんは、げんかんへ行きました。げんかんには、ねこの名前のリストがあります。えんぴつも、そこにあります。","en":"Fumiko-san goes out to the front hall. The list of the cat's names is there, with its pencil.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[夜]{よる}七時。ばんごはんです。[今日]{きょう}、あおいはおばあちゃんの[店]{みせ}に行っていて、いません。チェスカは、[魚]{さかな}を二ひき食べました。そして、聞きました。「これ、だれが[作]{つく}ったの？」テーブルの右と左から、二人がいっしょに[答]{こた}えました。「おれ。」","en":"7 p.m., dinner. Aoi is at her grandmother's shop today. Cheska eats two fish. Then she asks, \"Who made this?\" From both sides of the table, the two of them answer together: \"Me.\" (おれ)","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"oops","ja":"…あ！[二人]{ふたり}に、たのんじゃった。ごめん！","en":"...Oh! I asked you both. Sorry!","gl":"たのんじゃった: casual たのんでしまった, \"I ended up asking\".","tag":"embarrassed","ref":"E5·L33"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"そうじ、[四回]{よんかい}するね。","en":"I'll do four cleaning turns.","tag":"apologetic, cheerful","ref":"E5·L34"},
{"t":"narr","text":"チェスカは、二人のそうじの番を、二回ずつします。いつもの[約束]{やくそく}の、[二人分]{ふたりぶん}です。","en":"Cheska will do two cleaning turns for each of them: her usual deal, twice.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"かいだんのそばのたなの、まりやのかさは、もうなおっています。だれがなおしたか、だれも言いません。","en":"Mariya's umbrella on the shelf by the stairs is fixed now. Nobody says who fixed it.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"hello","ja":"イエンさん、おいしい？","en":"Yến, is it good?","tag":"curious, friendly","ref":"E5·L35"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"think","ja":"…おいしい。","en":"...It's good.","tag":"shy","ref":"E5·L36"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"yay","ja":"あ、ため[口]{ぐち}！","en":"Oh, casual Japanese!","tag":"delighted","ref":"E5·L37"},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u5-x1","type":"mcq","q":"Why do Kaito and Rodrigo both think Thursday is their turn to cook?","options":[{"t":"Cheska asked both of them","why":"Right. Rodrigo says チェスカさんが「[木曜日]{もくようび}、お[願]{ねが}い」と言いました, and Kaito answers ぼくにも言いました: she said it to me too.","ok":true},
{"t":"Fumiko-san asked both of them","why":"Fumiko-san only arrives later, with the fish. It was Cheska: チェスカさんが…と言いました."},
{"t":"Rodrigo read the group chat wrong","why":"Rodrigo doesn't read the group chat at all. Cheska asked him in person, and asked Kaito グループチャットで."},
{"t":"Cheska wrote Thursday twice on the bulletin board","why":"She didn't write anything. She asked Rodrigo at breakfast and Kaito グループチャットで."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u5-x2","type":"mcq","q":"Kaito says 見てる。キャベツだね。 What is 見てる short for?","options":[{"t":"見ている","why":"Right. In casual speech, ～ている loses its い: 見ている → 見てる. *I'm looking.* 働いてる (L24) works the same way.","ok":true},
{"t":"見ていた","why":"That is the past, *was looking*. Its casual form is 見てた."},
{"t":"見てください","why":"A casual request is the て-form alone, like Kaito's キャベツ[切]{き}って. 見てる has る on the end: it is ～ている."},
{"t":"見ます","why":"見ます is the polite form of 見る, *look* or *will look*. 見てる is the casual form of 見ている, *am looking*."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u5-x3","type":"mcq","q":"Fumiko-san tells Yến that 「[冷蔵庫]{れいぞうこ}、[使]{つか}うね」でいいんです. What makes that sentence casual?","options":[{"t":"The plain verb 使う, no を, and ね at the end","why":"Right. Yến's version was 冷蔵庫を使ってもよろしいでしょうか. Friends drop the polite ending, often drop を, and add ね to keep it friendly.","ok":true},
{"t":"The word 冷蔵庫","why":"The noun is the same in both versions. It is the verb and the ending that change."},
{"t":"Leaving out the person","why":"Yến's polite version doesn't say \"I\" either. Japanese often leaves the person out in both styles."},
{"t":"It turns the request into a question without か","why":"使うね isn't a question. Yến is saying what she is doing, and ね asks the others to be OK with it."}]}},
{"t":"lang","items":["The switch: Kaito starts politely (ぼくの[番]{ばん}ですけど) and only changes when the older Rodrigo offers: 「です・ます」はいらない. He checks first (いいんですか), then drops everything at once: [今日]{きょう}、おれの[番]{ばん}. At dinner, Yến uses casual Japanese again, and Mariya notices right away.","Quoting: Rodrigo quotes with と (「おれが[作]{つく}る」と言った), and Kaito uses casual って after the quote (おれも「やる」って言ったよ). Both mean *said that…*","～んです explains: Fumiko-san's あじが[安]{やす}かったんです gives the reason she is standing there with seven fish. Kaito's いいんですか asks Rodrigo to make sure before he changes."]},
{"t":"reflect","q":"Rodrigo tells Kaito 「です・ます」はいらない. In your own language, how do you know when you can stop being formal with someone, and who usually says so first?"}]},{"unit":"e3u6","n":6,"title":"The house app","month":"June","level":"N4","enDefault":true,"parts":[{"t":"narr","text":"チェスカが、[同]{おな}じ[木曜日]{もくようび}を二人にたのみました。かいととロドリゴは、二人でばんごはんを[作]{つく}りました。[文子]{ふみこ}さんはイエンに言いました。「ここは[会社]{かいしゃ}じゃありませんよ。」","en":"Cheska asked two people to cook on the same Thursday. Kaito and Rodrigo made dinner together. Fumiko-san told Yến, \"This isn't an office.\"","recap":true,"lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"六月の[土曜日]{どようび}の[朝]{あさ}です。まりやとトビーは、フェリーに[乗]{の}っています。まりやの[島]{しま}、[潮島]{しおじま}まで、[一時間]{いちじかん}です。","en":"It is a Saturday morning in June. Mariya and Toby are on the ferry. The trip to Mariya's island, Shiojima, takes an hour.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"トビーは、[年]{とし}をとった[漁師]{りょうし}さんたちの[言葉]{ことば}を、[録音]{ろくおん}したいと[思]{おも}っています。まりやは、高校の三年間、[毎朝]{まいあさ}このフェリーで、[町]{まち}の学校に行きました。だから、島の[船長]{せんちょう}さんを、みんな[知]{し}っています。","en":"Toby wants to record the way the old fishermen talk. Mariya knows every ferry captain on the island, because she took this ferry to high school in town every morning for three years.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"think","ja":"[島]{しま}の[言葉]{ことば}、ぼく、[聞]{き}き[取]{と}れるかな。","en":"I wonder if I'll be able to understand the island dialect.","gl":"聞き取れる: can catch, can understand (by ear). かな: \"I wonder\".","tag":"a little nervous","ref":"E6·L1"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"yay","ja":"[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}。私が[教]{おし}えてあげる。","en":"Don't worry. I'll teach you.","gl":"教えてあげる: \"I'll teach you,\" offered as a favor between friends.","tag":"confident, cheerful","ref":"E6·L2"},
{"t":"narr","text":"島の[港]{みなと}のすぐそばに、小さいきっさてんがあります。まりやのお父さんとお母さんの[店]{みせ}です。まどのそばに、おじいさんが一人すわっています。昔、フェリーの船長でした。まりやは、子どものときから、この人を「おじいちゃん」とよんでいます。","en":"Right by the island's ferry pier, there is a small café. It belongs to Mariya's parents. An old man is sitting by the window. He used to be a ferry captain. He isn't Mariya's grandfather, but she has always called him Ojii-chan, \"Grandpa.\"","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"hello","ja":"おじいちゃん、この人、トビー。かもめそうに[住]{す}んでるの。[昔]{むかし}の[話]{はなし}、してくれない？","en":"Grandpa, this is Toby. He lives at Kamome House. Would you tell him some old stories?","gl":"おじいちゃん: grandpa; also a friendly way to call an old man you know well. ～てくれない？: \"would you ～ for me?\"","tag":"affectionate","ref":"E6·L3"},
{"t":"line","who":"captain","mood":"hello","ja":"わしの[話]{はなし}か。…いいよ。でも、[正一]{しょういち}の[方]{ほう}が、よう知っとるぞ。","en":"My stories? ...All right. But Shōichi knows more than I do.","gl":"わし: \"I\", used by some older men. よう知っとる: よく知っている, said the local way.","tag":"gravelly, amused","ref":"E6·L4"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"さとうさんですか。ぼくの[大家]{おおや}さんです。","en":"Mr. Satō? He's my landlord.","tag":"surprised","ref":"E6·L5"},
{"t":"line","who":"captain","mood":"tip","ja":"それから、[町]{まち}の[源]{げん}と[岩田]{いわた}にも[会]{あ}うといい。…でも、二人いっしょは、だめだぞ。三十年、[口]{くち}をきいとらん。","en":"You should also meet Gen and Iwata in town. ...But not together. They haven't spoken to each other in thirty years.","gl":"～といい: \"you should ～\". 口をきく: to speak to someone. きいとらん: きいていない, said the local way.","tag":"lowering his voice, chuckling","ref":"E6·L6"},
{"t":"narr","text":"トビーは、ノートに二人の名前を書きました。まりやのお母さんが、コーヒーを[持]{も}って来てくれました。","en":"Toby writes both names in his notebook. Mariya's mother brings them coffee.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[夕方]{ゆうがた}、二人はかもめそうに[帰]{かえ}りました。げんかんのけいじばんに、[新]{あたら}しい[紙]{かみ}があります。QRコードです。","en":"In the evening, the two of them come back to Kamome House. There is a new sheet of paper on the bulletin board in the front hall: a QR code.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"かいとは、この前の木曜日のことが、いやでした。金曜日の[夜]{よる}は、バイトが休みでした。でも、かいとは、ねませんでした。[一晩]{ひとばん}で、[家]{いえ}のアプリを作りました。[料理]{りょうり}の[番]{ばん}、そうじの番、おふろの時間、ごみの日。ぜんぶ、アプリで[分]{わ}かります。「かわる」というボタンもあります。","en":"Kaito didn't like what happened on Thursday. On Friday night he had no shift, but he didn't go to bed. He built an app for the house in one night. It shows the cooking turns, cleaning turns, bath times and garbage days. It also has a button that says かわる, \"swap.\"","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"みんな、アプリを入れました。正一さんだけは、入れません。スマホを持っていないからです。[天気]{てんき}は、ろうかのバロメーターで分かります。文子さんは、すぐに入れました。そして、アプリのまちがいを四つ見つけて、朝ごはんのときに、かいとに一つずつ、やさしく教えました。","en":"Everyone installs the app except Shōichi-san. He doesn't have a smartphone, and he checks the weather on the barometer in the hall. Fumiko-san installs it right away. By breakfast she has found four problems, and she tells Kaito about them one at a time, very kindly.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[一週間後]{いっしゅうかんご}。ばんごはんの前に、イエンが、かいとのとなりにすわりました。[魚]{さかな}の木曜日から、イエンは、かいとにため口で話しています。かいとは、イエンのため口を聞いても、何も言いません。いつもと同じように、「うん」と答えるだけです。だから、イエンは、かいととなら、ため口で話せます。","en":"A week later, before dinner, Yến sits down next to Kaito. Since the night of the fish, she has been practicing casual Japanese with him. When Yến speaks casually, Kaito doesn't comment. He just answers \"Yeah,\" the way he always does. So with Kaito, she can talk casually.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"hello","ja":"かいと、このアプリ、[一人]{ひとり}で[作]{つく}った？","en":"Kaito, did you make this app by yourself?","tag":"casual, still practicing","ref":"E6·L7"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"oops","ja":"…うん。[一晩]{ひとばん}で。","en":"...Yeah. In one night.","gl":"一晩 (ひとばん): one night.","tag":"shy, a little proud","ref":"E6·L8"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"yay","ja":"[一晩]{ひとばん}で[作]{つく}れるんだ。すごいね。","en":"You can build this in one night? That's amazing.","tag":"impressed","ref":"E6·L9"},
{"t":"narr","text":"イエンは、四年間、日本の[会社]{かいしゃ}で、ソフトウェアを作っていました。その会社では、コードは、ほかの人が読んでから使いました。","en":"Yến built software at a company in Japan for four years. There, nobody used code until another person had read it.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"hello","ja":"コード、[見]{み}せてくれない？レビューしてあげる。","en":"Can you show me the code? I'll review it for you.","gl":"コード: code. レビュー: a review. In a code review, another programmer reads your code before it is used.","tag":"businesslike","ref":"E6·L10"},
{"t":"note","text":"～てあげる means \"I'll do this for you.\" Between friends it sounds kind, like Mariya's 教えてあげる on the ferry. But when you offer to check someone's work, it can sound as if you are above them. Yến means it kindly, but Kaito hears a senior checking a junior's homework."},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"oops","ja":"…まだ[見]{み}せられない。","en":"...I can't show you yet.","tag":"defensive, quiet","ref":"E6·L11"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"think","ja":"どうして？","en":"Why not?","tag":"curious","ref":"E6·L12"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"oops","ja":"まだ、きれいじゃないから。きれいになったら、[見]{み}せる。","en":"It isn't clean yet. When it's clean, I'll show you.","tag":"mumbling","ref":"E6·L13"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"tip","ja":"きれいじゃなくてもいいよ。レビューすれば、きれいになるから。","en":"It doesn't have to be clean. A review is how it gets clean.","tag":"matter-of-fact","ref":"E6·L14"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"sleepy","ja":"ちゃんと[動]{うご}いてるよ。みんな[使]{つか}えるし。","en":"It works fine. Everyone can use it.","gl":"ちゃんと: properly. 動く (うごく): to move; of a machine or a program, to work.","tag":"flat, stubborn","ref":"E6·L15"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"tip","ja":"[動]{うご}くだけじゃだめ。テストは書いた？","en":"Working isn't enough. Did you write tests?","tag":"brisk","ref":"E6·L16"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"oops","ja":"…書いてない。","en":"...No.","tag":"barely audible","ref":"E6·L17"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"tip","ja":"書かなきゃ。バグがあったら、どうするの？","en":"You have to. What will you do if there's a bug?","gl":"バグ: a bug, a mistake in a program. 書かなきゃ: casual 書かなければいけない, \"you have to write them\".","tag":"firm","ref":"E6·L18"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"sleepy","ja":"バグはない。","en":"There are no bugs.","tag":"deadpan","ref":"E6·L19"},
{"t":"narr","text":"そこへ、トビーが[庭]{にわ}から入って来ました。ひざに、[土]{つち}がついています。トビーは、さとうさんたちの古い[野菜畑]{やさいばたけ}を、一人で[手入]{てい}れしています。手には、スマホを持っています。","en":"Just then, Toby comes in from the garden with dirt on his knees. He has quietly taken over the Satōs' old vegetable garden. He is holding his phone.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"かいとくん、ちょっといい？ぼく、[今週]{こんしゅう}、[四回]{よんかい}[料理]{りょうり}しなきゃいけないんだけど…。","en":"Kaito, do you have a minute? It says I have to cook four times this week...","gl":"今週 (こんしゅう): this week.","tag":"sheepish","ref":"E6·L20"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"think","ja":"[四回]{よんかい}？どうして？","en":"Four times? Why?","tag":"surprised","ref":"E6·L21"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"oops","ja":"「かわって」が[来]{く}ると、つい「いいよ」をおしちゃうんだ。","en":"Whenever a swap request comes, I just press \"OK\" without thinking.","gl":"かわる: to swap, to take someone's turn. つい: without meaning to. おしちゃう: casual おしてしまう.","tag":"embarrassed laugh","ref":"E6·L22"},
{"t":"narr","text":"トビーは、だれにも「いや」と言いません。アプリで、「いいよ」は、ボタン一つになりました。","en":"Toby can't say no to anyone, and now the app has made saying yes a single tap.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"tip","ja":"ほら、バグだよ。[一人]{ひとり}が[何回]{なんかい}でもかわれる。","en":"See? That's a bug. One person can swap any number of times.","gl":"ほら: \"see?\", \"look\". 何回でも: any number of times.","tag":"triumphant","ref":"E6·L23"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"tip","ja":"バグじゃない。トビーが「いいよ」をおさなければ、いいんだよ。","en":"It's not a bug. It's fine as long as Toby doesn't press \"OK\".","tag":"stubborn","ref":"E6·L24"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"oops","ja":"…それはそうだね。ごめん。","en":"...Well, that's true. Sorry.","gl":"ごめん: sorry (casual).","tag":"apologetic","ref":"E6·L25"},
{"t":"narr","text":"まりやが、ろうかから来ました。まりやも、話を聞いていました。","en":"Mariya comes in from the hallway. She has heard everything too.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"tip","ja":"トビー、[木曜日]{もくようび}は、私がかわってあげる。でも、もう「いいよ」はおさないで！","en":"Toby, I'll take Thursday for you. But stop pressing \"OK\"!","tag":"exasperated, fond","ref":"E6·L26"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"tip","ja":"みんな、おしちゃうの。だから、「かわるのは[一週間]{いっしゅうかん}に[二回]{にかい}まで」というルールを[入]{い}れなければならない。","en":"Everyone presses it. So you have to add a rule: no more than two swaps a week.","gl":"～の at the end: a soft ～んだ. ～というルール: a rule that says ～. 入れなければならない: the formal \"must\"; Yến slips back into textbook Japanese here.","tag":"businesslike","ref":"E6·L27"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"sleepy","ja":"…おれのアプリだよ。","en":"...It's my app.","tag":"sulky","ref":"E6·L28"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"tip","ja":"みんなのアプリだよ。[仕事]{しごと}なら、レビューしていないコードは[出]{だ}せない。","en":"It's everyone's app. At work, you couldn't release code that nobody has reviewed.","gl":"仕事 (しごと): work, a job. 出す: here, to release.","tag":"firm","ref":"E6·L29"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"oops","ja":"[仕事]{しごと}じゃない。…バイト、[行]{い}かなきゃ。","en":"It isn't work. ...I have to go to my shift.","gl":"バイト: a part-time job.","tag":"cold, standing up","ref":"E6·L30"},
{"t":"narr","text":"かいとは、しずかにパソコンをとじて、[部屋]{へや}を出て行きました。イエンの言ったことは、ぜんぶ[正]{ただ}しいです。でも、イエンは、パソコンがあった[所]{ところ}を、だまって見ています。","en":"Kaito quietly closes his laptop and leaves. Everything Yến said was right. Still, she sits and looks at the spot where the laptop was.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"ぼくは、[四回]{よんかい}[作]{つく}ってもいいよ。ほんとに。","en":"I don't mind cooking four times. Really.","gl":"ほんとに: really.","tag":"too cheerfully","ref":"E6·L31"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"sleepy","ja":"…それがバグなんだよ、トビー。","en":"...That's the bug, Toby.","tag":"sighs","ref":"E6·L32"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"ばんごはんです。かいとの[席]{せき}は、あいています。チェスカとあおいは、大学で、同じ[大西]{おおにし}[先生]{せんせい}のゼミにいます。でも、家では、あまり話しません。あおいが、スマホを見て言いました。","en":"Dinner. Kaito's seat is empty. Cheska and Aoi are in the same seminar at the university, taught by Prof. Ōnishi, but at home they don't talk much. Aoi looks at her phone and speaks up.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"hello","ja":"[日曜日]{にちようび}のそうじ、だれか、かわってくれない？おばあちゃんの[店]{みせ}を、[手伝]{てつだ}わなきゃ。","en":"Could someone take my cleaning turn on Sunday? I have to help at my grandmother's shop.","tag":"casual, not looking up","ref":"E6·L33"},
{"t":"narr","text":"チェスカは、自分のスマホで、その「かわって」を見ました。何も言いません。","en":"Cheska sees the swap request on her own phone. She doesn't say anything.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[今日]{きょう}のチェスカは、しずかです。いつものしずかさと、ちがいます。今週は、料理の番を、一回もほかの人にたのみませんでした。おさらのよこに、小さくたたんだ紙があります。","en":"Cheska is quiet tonight, and not in her usual way. She hasn't asked anyone to take a cooking turn all week. Next to her plate there is a sheet of paper, folded into a small square.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"think","ja":"チェスカ、その[紙]{かみ}、[何]{なに}？","en":"Cheska, what's that paper?","gl":"紙 (かみ): paper.","tag":"gently curious","ref":"E6·L34"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"think","ja":"ううん、[何]{なん}でもない。あとで読もうと[思]{おも}って。","en":"Oh, it's nothing. I was going to read it later.","gl":"何でもない: it's nothing. 読もう: the volitional form, \"let's read\" or \"I'll read\".","tag":"quickly, brushing it off","ref":"E6·L35"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"食べよう。さめちゃうよ。","en":"Let's eat. It'll get cold.","gl":"さめる: to go cold.","tag":"forced cheerful","ref":"E6·L36"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[本当]{ほんとう}は、チェスカはもう三回、一人でその地図を読みました。[漢字]{かんじ}が[多]{おお}くて、時間がかかりました。[市]{し}のハザードマップです。地図には、川のそばの古い町がのっています。かもめそうのある[通]{とお}りもあります。そこは、白くありません。[色]{いろ}がついています。ハザードマップでは、色のある所は、水が来るかもしれない所です。","en":"In fact, Cheska has already read the map three times on her own. It had a lot of kanji, so it took her a long time. It is the city's hazard map. It shows the old town by the river, including the street Kamome House is on, and that whole area is colored, not white. On a hazard map, colored areas are places that could flood.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"トビーは、その「何でもない」を、よく知っています。[自分]{じぶん}も、よく使いますから。トビーは、何も聞かないで、チェスカにごはんをわたしました。","en":"Toby knows that kind of \"it's nothing\" well, because he says it a lot himself. He doesn't ask. He just passes Cheska the rice.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[夜中]{よなか}の二時。かいとは、コンビニのうらで、[休]{やす}んでいます。イエンは、[二階]{にかい}の[部屋]{へや}で、まだ[起]{お}きています。ねむれません。イエンのスマホが[光]{ひか}りました。","en":"2 a.m. Kaito is on his break behind the convenience store. Upstairs in her room, Yến is still awake. She can't sleep. Her phone lights up.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"*(The next lines are text messages. Audio: quiet and close, not across a room.)*"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"oops","ja":"[起]{お}きてる？","en":"You awake?","tag":"quietly, tentative","ref":"E6·L37"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"hello","ja":"[起]{お}きてる。","en":"I'm awake.","tag":"softly","ref":"E6·L38"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"oops","ja":"コード、[送]{おく}っておいた。見てもいいよ。でも、[笑]{わら}わないで。","en":"I sent you the code. You can look at it. But don't laugh.","gl":"送る (おくる): to send. 笑う (わらう): to laugh.","tag":"nervous, hushed","ref":"E6·L39"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"think","ja":"[笑]{わら}わないよ。…「してあげる」は、よくなかった。ごめん。","en":"I won't laugh. ...I shouldn't have said I'd review it \"for you.\" Sorry.","tag":"softly, sincere","ref":"E6·L40"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"hello","ja":"[明日]{あした}、いっしょに見よう。","en":"Let's look at it together tomorrow.","tag":"warm, quiet","ref":"E6·L41"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"sleepy","ja":"…うん。トビーのバグ、[直]{なお}しておく。","en":"...OK. I'll fix the Toby bug before then.","gl":"直す (なおす): to fix.","tag":"quiet, a little relieved","ref":"E6·L42"},
{"t":"narr","text":"かいとが、「バグ」と言いました。かいとの「バグ」は、たぶん「ごめん」と[同]{おな}じです。","en":"Kaito called it a bug. From Kaito, that is probably the same as saying sorry.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[一階]{いっかい}の101[号室]{ごうしつ}も、まだ[電気]{でんき}がついています。チェスカの部屋です。いつもは、この時間に、古いホラー[映画]{えいが}の音が、小さく聞こえます。今夜は、何も聞こえません。チェスカは、ゆかの上に、地図を大きく[広]{ひろ}げています。","en":"Downstairs, the light is still on in Room 101, Cheska's room. At this hour you can usually hear one of her old horror movies, very quietly. Tonight there is no sound. Cheska has the map spread open on the floor.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u6-x1","type":"mcq","q":"Kaito says まだ[見]{み}せられない. What does he mean?","options":[{"t":"He can't show the code yet","why":"Right. 見せられない is the potential form of 見せる in the negative: *can't show*. His reason comes next: まだ、きれいじゃないから.","ok":true},
{"t":"He hasn't looked at the code yet","why":"That would be まだ見ていない. 見せる is *show*, not *look*, and ～られない here means *can't*."},
{"t":"He doesn't have to show the code","why":"*Doesn't have to* is ～なくてもいい: 見せなくてもいい. 見せられない is *can't show*."},
{"t":"He must not show the code","why":"*Must not* is ～てはいけない: 見せてはいけない. 見せられない is *can't show*."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u6-x2","type":"mcq","q":"At two in the morning, Kaito writes トビーのバグ、[直]{なお}しておく. What is he promising?","options":[{"t":"To fix the swap problem before he and Yến look at the code tomorrow","why":"Right. ～ておく means doing something now so it is ready for later, and [直]{なお}す is *fix*. For the first time, he calls it a バグ.","ok":true},
{"t":"That he has already fixed it","why":"*Already fixed* would be [直]{なお}しておいた, in the past, like his [送]{おく}っておいた. [直]{なお}しておく is still to come."},
{"t":"To make Toby fix it","why":"Nobody else is in the sentence. トビーのバグ is just Kaito's name for the problem: the bug Toby found by saying yes to everything."},
{"t":"To leave the problem as it is","why":"～ておく can mean leaving something as it is, but not with [直]{なお}す. You can't fix a thing and leave it alone."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u6-x3","type":"mcq","q":"Toby says つい「いいよ」をおしちゃうんだ. What does ～ちゃう add to おす?","options":[{"t":"He does it without meaning to, and he is a little sorry about it","why":"Right. ～ちゃう is the casual form of ～てしまう. With つい (\"without thinking\"), it shows that Toby presses OK before he can stop himself.","ok":true},
{"t":"It puts the verb in the past","why":"The past would be おした. Toby is talking about something that keeps happening."},
{"t":"It means he wants to press it","why":"\"Want to\" is ～たい: おしたい. Toby doesn't want to; he just does."},
{"t":"It asks someone else to press it","why":"A request would be おして or おしてください."}]}},
{"t":"lang","items":["Can and can't: 聞き[取]{と}れる, [一晩]{ひとばん}で[作]{つく}れる, みんな[使]{つか}える, 見せられない, [出]{だ}せない. The potential form carries most of the argument: what Kaito can do alone, and what Yến says nobody can do.","Favors: Mariya's [教]{おし}えてあげる and [木曜日]{もくようび}は私がかわってあげる are kind, between friends. Yến's レビューしてあげる offers to judge someone's work, so it sounds like a favor he didn't ask for. 話してくれない？ and 見せてくれない？ ask someone to do something for you, and those are fine. Yến takes her あげる back herself: 「してあげる」は、よくなかった.","Must, and don't have to: 書かなきゃ and [入]{い}れなければならない are the same *must*, casual and formal. きれいじゃなくてもいい is the opposite: it doesn't have to be."]},
{"t":"reflect","q":"Yến is right about the code, and Kaito still closes the laptop. Think of a time someone was right about your work. What made it easier, or harder, to hear?"}]},{"unit":"e3u7","n":7,"title":"The last festival?","month":"July–August","level":"N4","enDefault":false,"parts":[{"t":"narr","text":"かいとが、[家]{いえ}のアプリを[作]{つく}った。イエンとかいとは、コードのレビューのことでけんかしたが、[夜中]{よなか}に[仲直]{なかなお}りした。トビーは、だれにも「いや」と言えない。","en":"Kaito made an app for the house. He and Yến argued about reviewing his code, then made up in the middle of the night. Toby can't say no to anyone.","recap":true,"lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"七月のはじめ。かもめそうから[歩]{ある}いて五分の[所]{ところ}に、つばめ[通]{どお}りがある。[屋根]{やね}のある[商店街]{しょうてんがい}だ。でも、[店]{みせ}の[半分]{はんぶん}ぐらいは、シャッターがしまったままだ。","en":"Early July. Five minutes' walk from Kamome House is Tsubame Street (*tsubame* means swallow, the bird), a covered shopping street. About half of its shops have closed, and their shutters stay down.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"通りのまん中に、[古]{ふる}いお[茶]{ちゃ}の店がある。[入]{い}り口には、高い石の[段]{だん}がある。[浜田]{はまだ}[千代]{ちよ}さんの店だ。千代さんは八十さいをすぎていて、あおいのおばあちゃんだ。[去年]{きょねん}、[脳]{のう}の[病気]{びょうき}をして、左手が少し[弱]{よわ}くなった。店の[二階]{にかい}に[住]{す}んでいるが、[急]{きゅう}な[階段]{かいだん}は、一人だとこわいそうだ。","en":"In the middle of the street is an old tea shop, with a high stone step at the door. It belongs to Aoi's grandmother, Chiyo Hamada, who is over eighty. Last year she had a small stroke, and her left hand is still weak. She lives above the shop, and she says the steep stairs scare her when she is alone.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[先月]{せんげつ}、千代さんは、ロドリゴにまつりのポスターをたのんだ。","en":"Last month, Chiyo asked Rodrigo to make a poster for the festival.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"chiyo","mood":"hello","ja":"いらっしゃいませ。…あら、ロドリゴさん。","en":"Welcome. ...Oh, it's you, Rodrigo.","gl":"いらっしゃいませ: what shop staff say when you come in.","tag":"warmly, then surprised","ref":"E7·L1"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"ちよさん！ポスターができました！","en":"Chiyo-san! The poster is finished!","tag":"excited, out of breath","ref":"E7·L2"},
{"t":"narr","text":"ロドリゴは、カウンターにポスターを[広]{ひろ}げた。[万年筆]{まんねんひつ}でかいた[絵]{え}で、インクは[三色]{さんしょく}だ。通りの屋根と、ちょうちん。その下を、[七羽]{ななわ}のつばめが[飛]{と}んでいる。お茶の店の段の上には、白と[黒]{くろ}のねこがすわっている。","en":"Rodrigo spreads the poster out on the counter. He drew it with a fountain pen, in three colors of ink: the street's roof, the paper lanterns, and seven swallows flying under them. On the step of the tea shop sits a black-and-white cat.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"plates","title":"The poster","hint":"Read each line of the poster, then tap it to check.","items":[{"ja":"つばめ通り 夏まつり","ro":"つばめどおり なつまつり","who":"The Tsubame Street Summer Festival. 通り is a street and 夏 is summer. Rodrigo wrote つばめ in hiragana. Its kanji, 燕, has sixteen strokes, and he wanted people to read the poster from a moving bus."},{"ja":"八月一日（土）","ro":"はちがつ ついたち（どようび）","who":"Saturday, August 1. The first day of the month has its own word: ついたち."},{"ja":"午後四時から九時まで","ro":"ごご よじ から くじ まで","who":"From 4 to 9 p.m."},{"ja":"雨の日も やります","ro":"あめの ひも やります","who":"*Even if it rains.* The beach clean-up in May said 雨の日は休みです. Tsubame Street has a roof, so it uses も."},{"ja":"英語の あんない あります","ro":"えいごの あんない あります","who":"*English guides available.* あんない (案内) means showing people the way. Rodrigo didn't draw this line. The shopkeepers' association added it, and then had to find some guides."}]},
{"t":"line","who":"chiyo","mood":"think","ja":"…このねこは？","en":"...And this cat?","tag":"curious, peering","ref":"E7·L3"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"ミチです！","en":"That's Michi!","tag":"proudly","ref":"E7·L4"},
{"t":"line","who":"chiyo","mood":"tip","ja":"「ミチ」じゃありませんよ。この[通]{とお}りでは、「まっちゃ」と[呼]{よ}ばれています。","en":"She isn't Michi. On this street, she's called Matcha.","gl":"まっちゃ (抹茶): powdered green tea. 呼ばれる (よばれる): to be called, the passive form of 呼ぶ.","tag":"gently correcting","ref":"E7·L5"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"[白]{しろ}と[黒]{くろ}なのに、まっちゃですか。","en":"She's black and white, and she's called Matcha?","gl":"～のに: even though.","tag":"puzzled","ref":"E7·L6"},
{"t":"line","who":"chiyo","mood":"hello","ja":"うちの[店]{みせ}の[前]{まえ}に、いますから。","en":"Because she sits in front of my tea shop.","gl":"うち: here, \"my\" or \"our\".","tag":"matter-of-fact, smiling","ref":"E7·L7"},
{"t":"narr","text":"この通りでは、それで決まりだ。千代さんは、ポスターのつばめを二回[数]{かぞ}えて、少し笑った。それから、レジの下から、ふうとうを出した。","en":"On this street, that settles it. Chiyo counts the swallows on the poster twice and smiles a little. Then she takes an envelope from under the cash register.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"chiyo","mood":"hello","ja":"はい、これ。ポスターのお金です。","en":"Here you are. This is for the poster.","tag":"kindly, firm","ref":"E7·L8"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"お金はいりません！かきたかったから、かきました！","en":"I don't need money! I drew it because I wanted to!","tag":"embarrassed, waving his hands","ref":"E7·L9"},
{"t":"line","who":"chiyo","mood":"tip","ja":"だめですよ。[人]{ひと}に[仕事]{しごと}をさせて、お金を[払]{はら}わない[店]{みせ}は、[長]{なが}く[続]{つづ}きません。","en":"That won't do. A shop that makes people work and doesn't pay them won't last long.","gl":"させる: to make someone do, the causative form of する. 払う (はらう): to pay. 続く (つづく): to last, to go on.","tag":"firm, motherly","ref":"E7·L10"},
{"t":"narr","text":"千代さんの店は、六十年[続]{つづ}いている。ロドリゴは、[両手]{りょうて}でふうとうを[受]{う}け[取]{と}った。日本で、絵でお金をもらうのは、はじめてだ。","en":"Chiyo's shop has lasted sixty years. Rodrigo takes the envelope with both hands. It is the first time anyone in Japan has paid him for a drawing.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"…ありがとうございます。","en":"...Thank you.","tag":"quietly, moved","ref":"E7·L11"},
{"t":"narr","text":"いつものロドリゴより、ずっと小さい[声]{こえ}だ。そこへ、イエンが店に入って来た。大学の帰りに、ときどきここでお茶を買う。イエンは、カウンターのポスターを見た。","en":"His voice is much quieter than usual. Just then, Yến comes into the shop. She sometimes stops here for tea on her way home from the university. She notices the poster on the counter.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"yay","ja":"この[線]{せん}、きれいですね。","en":"These lines are beautiful.","gl":"線 (せん): a line.","tag":"admiring, quietly","ref":"E7·L12"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"…ありがとう！","en":"...Thank you!","tag":"surprised, happy","ref":"E7·L13"},
{"t":"line","who":"chiyo","mood":"hello","ja":"イエンさんの[名前]{なまえ}は、ベトナム[語]{ご}で「つばめ」らしいですね。","en":"I hear your name means \"swallow\" in Vietnamese, Yến-san.","gl":"～らしい: \"I hear\", \"apparently\".","tag":"warmly","ref":"E7·L14"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"hello","ja":"はい、そうです。","en":"Yes, that's right.","tag":"politely","ref":"E7·L15"},
{"t":"line","who":"chiyo","mood":"yay","ja":"じゃあ、イエンさんは、この[通]{とお}りの[鳥]{とり}ですね。はい、これも食べて。","en":"Then you're this street's own bird. Here, have one of these too.","tag":"delighted, insisting","ref":"E7·L16"},
{"t":"narr","text":"千代さんは、いつもイエンに何か食べさせる。今日は、おまんじゅうだ。イエンは、ことわれない。","en":"Chiyo always makes Yến eat something. Today it is a sweet bean bun, and Yến can't say no.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"ちよさん、あおいさんは？","en":"Chiyo-san, where's Aoi?","tag":"curious","ref":"E7·L17"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"hello","ja":"あおいさんは、[東京]{とうきょう}でインターンらしいです。[台所]{だいどころ}で[聞]{き}きました。","en":"I heard in the kitchen that Aoi's doing an internship in Tokyo.","tag":"matter-of-fact","ref":"E7·L18"},
{"t":"line","who":"chiyo","mood":"sleepy","ja":"[夏]{なつ}の[間]{あいだ}だけね。…東京の仕事は、あまり[楽]{たの}しくないらしいけど。","en":"Just for the summer. ...Though I hear the work in Tokyo isn't much fun.","tag":"sighs, softly","ref":"E7·L19"},
{"t":"narr","text":"千代さんは、それ[以上]{いじょう}言わなかった。でも、夏になってすぐ、あおいが東京へ行ったことを、千代さんはちゃんと見ていた。","en":"Chiyo doesn't say any more. But she noticed that Aoi left for Tokyo the moment summer came.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"ちよさん、まつりは[今年]{ことし}で[終]{お}わるらしいですね。パン[屋]{や}さんで[聞]{き}きました。","en":"Chiyo-san, I hear this year's festival will be the last. They told me at the bakery.","gl":"パン屋 (パンや): a bakery.","tag":"worried","ref":"E7·L20"},
{"t":"line","who":"chiyo","mood":"sleepy","ja":"[去年]{きょねん}も、そう言われましたよ。その[前]{まえ}の[年]{とし}も。","en":"People said that last year too. And the year before.","tag":"tired, wry","ref":"E7·L21"},
{"t":"note","text":"らしい passes on something you have heard, without promising it is true. Chiyo answers with the passive, そう言われました, \"that was said,\" which leaves out the speakers completely. A whole street can talk like this for years."},
{"t":"narr","text":"去年の夏から、また三つの店が[閉]{し}まった。[秋]{あき}に、商店街の人たちが、[来年]{らいねん}のまつりをどうするか[決]{き}める。帰り道、ロドリゴは、ポスターのお金でお[昼]{ひる}ごはんを買った。午後四時だ。[二日間]{ふつかかん}、ちゃんと食べていなかった。","en":"Since last summer, three more shops have closed. In the fall, the shopkeepers will decide whether to hold the festival next year. On the way home, Rodrigo buys lunch with some of the poster money. It is 4 p.m., and he hasn't eaten a proper meal in two days.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"八月の[最初]{さいしょ}の土曜日。七月の間に、ポスターは通りのシャッターぜんぶにはられた。今夜は、[港]{みなと}に大きいクルーズ[船]{せん}も来ている。はじめてのことだ。","en":"The first Saturday of August. During July, the poster went up on every shutter on the street. Tonight a big cruise ship is in the harbor, for the first time.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"通りには、[屋台]{やたい}がならんでいる。チェスカとロドリゴは、歩きながら見ている。","en":"Food stalls line the street. Cheska and Rodrigo walk along, looking at them.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"フィリピンでは、こういう店を「ティアンゲ」と言うの。","en":"In the Philippines, we call stalls like these \"tiangge.\"","tag":"cheerful","ref":"E7·L22"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"メキシコでは、「ティアングイス」だ！","en":"In Mexico, they're \"tianguis\"!","tag":"excited, amazed","ref":"E7·L23"},
{"t":"narr","text":"二人は、びっくりして[顔]{かお}を[見合]{みあ}わせた。四百年ぐらい前、マニラとアカプルコの[間]{あいだ}を、大きい船が行き来していた。言葉も、その船で海をわたったのだ。","en":"They look at each other in surprise. About four hundred years ago, big ships sailed between Manila and Acapulco, and words crossed the ocean on those ships too.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"「ENGLISH」と書いたテーブルに、[案内]{あんない}の人が二人すわっている。商店街の人がたのんだのは、トビーだけだった。でも、トビーは「二人でやります」と言った。もう一人は、まりやだ。","en":"Two guides are sitting at a folding table marked ENGLISH. The shopkeepers only asked Toby, but Toby said, \"The two of us will do it.\" The other guide is Mariya.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"sleepy","ja":"ロドリゴのポスター、フェリーのりばにも、はってあるんだって。…で、私、「やる」って言ってないのに、どうしてここにいるの？","en":"I hear Rodrigo's poster is up at the ferry terminal too. ...So why am I here? I never said I'd do this.","gl":"のりば: a place where you get on a bus, train or boat. はってある: has been put up, and is still there. ～んだって: \"I hear that…\" (casual).","tag":"grumbling","ref":"E7·L24"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"oops","ja":"ちよさんに[頼]{たの}まれて…「[二人]{ふたり}でやります」って言っちゃった。","en":"Chiyo-san asked me, and... I said, \"The two of us will do it.\"","gl":"頼む (たのむ): to ask someone to do something. 頼まれる: to be asked. 言っちゃった: casual 言ってしまった.","tag":"sheepish","ref":"E7·L25"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"tip","ja":"トビーはいつもそう。[頼]{たの}まれると、[何]{なん}でも「はい」。","en":"You always do this. Someone asks, and you say yes to anything.","tag":"rolling her eyes, affectionate","ref":"E7·L26"},
{"t":"narr","text":"まりやは、[英語]{えいご}を書くのは、とても[上手]{じょうず}だ。でも、話すのは[苦手]{にがて}だ。おそろいのむぎわらぼうしの[夫婦]{ふうふ}が、英語で「食べ物の屋台はどこ？」と聞くと、まりやはトビーを見た。次の人のときも、その次の人のときも、[同]{おな}じだった。","en":"Mariya writes English very well, but speaking it is hard for her. When a couple in matching straw hats asks in English where the food stalls are, she turns and looks at Toby. She does the same with the next visitor, and the one after that.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"まりや、[次]{つぎ}は[話]{はな}してみて。","en":"Mariya, you try the next one.","tag":"encouraging","ref":"E7·L27"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"oops","ja":"むり。ぜったい、まちがえそう。","en":"No way. I just know I'll get it wrong.","gl":"むり: impossible. ぜったい: definitely. まちがえる: to make a mistake. ～そう: looks likely to.","tag":"panicking","ref":"E7·L28"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"tip","ja":"まちがえてもいいよ。ぼくも、まちがえながら日本語をおぼえたし。","en":"It's OK to make mistakes. I learned Japanese by making mistakes as I went.","gl":"おぼえる: to learn, to memorize. ～ながら: while doing.","tag":"gently encouraging","ref":"E7·L29"},
{"t":"narr","text":"午後六時五十分。トビーのスマホが、二回ふるえた。トビーは、[笑]{わら}いながら読んだ。[悪]{わる}いニュースのときも、トビーは笑う。","en":"At 6:50 p.m., Toby's phone buzzes twice. He smiles as he reads. Toby smiles even when the news is bad.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"oops","ja":"…まりや。[七時]{しちじ}に、[源]{げん}さんの[屋台]{やたい}を[手伝]{てつだ}うって、[約束]{やくそく}したんだ。","en":"...Mariya. I promised to help at Gen-san's stall at seven.","gl":"屋台 (やたい): a food stall. 手伝う (てつだう): to help. 約束 (やくそく): a promise.","tag":"nervous laugh","ref":"E7·L30"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"hello","ja":"じゃあ、[行]{い}ってきて。すぐ[戻]{もど}ってね。","en":"Go, then. Come back soon.","tag":"sighs","ref":"E7·L31"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"oops","ja":"それと…[岩田]{いわた}さんにも。[七時]{しちじ}に。","en":"And... I promised Iwata-san too. At seven.","tag":"guilty, quietly","ref":"E7·L32"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"think","ja":"[二人]{ふたり}に？[同]{おな}じ[時間]{じかん}なのに？","en":"Both of them? At the same time?","tag":"disbelieving","ref":"E7·L33"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"tip","ja":"あの二人、[三十年]{さんじゅうねん}[話]{はな}してないんだよ。[島]{しま}のおじいちゃんも、言ってたでしょ。","en":"Those two haven't spoken in thirty years. You heard what the old captain on the island said.","tag":"urgent, lowering her voice","ref":"E7·L34"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"oops","ja":"[知]{し}ってる。だから、どっちにも「だめ」と言えなくて…。","en":"I know. That's why I couldn't say no to either of them...","tag":"miserable","ref":"E7·L35"},
{"t":"narr","text":"源さんも岩田さんも、[町]{まち}で長く[漁師]{りょうし}をしてきた人で、トビーの[録音]{ろくおん}にとって[大切]{たいせつ}な人だ。三十年前、二人は同じ船に乗っていた。ある[嵐]{あらし}の夜のあと、大げんかをして、それから一度も話していない。でも、町の人はみんな知っている。二人とも、本当は[相手]{あいて}のことを気にしている。まりやは、港の人をみんな知っている。すぐに、じゅんばんを決めた。","en":"Gen-san and Iwata-san are both old fishermen in town, and both are important for Toby's recordings. Thirty years ago, they worked on the same boat. After a stormy night at sea, they had a big fight, and they haven't spoken since. But everyone in town knows that they still care about each other. Mariya knows everyone at the harbor, and she works out the order right away.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"tip","ja":"[源]{げん}さんが[先]{さき}。[十五分]{じゅうごふん}[手伝]{てつだ}って、それから[岩田]{いわた}さん。「まりやに行かされた」って言っていいから。","en":"Gen-san first. Help him for fifteen minutes, then go to Iwata-san. You can tell them Mariya made you go.","gl":"行かされる: to be made to go, the causative-passive form of 行く.","tag":"taking charge, quick","ref":"E7·L36"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"oops","ja":"…ごめん。すぐ[戻]{もど}る。","en":"...Sorry. I'll be right back.","gl":"戻る (もどる): to come back.","tag":"apologetic, hurrying","ref":"E7·L37"},
{"t":"narr","text":"テーブルに[残]{のこ}ったのは、まりや一人だ。そこへ、クルーズ船の[観光]{かんこう}バスが[着]{つ}いた。せんすを[持]{も}った女の人が、英語で聞いた。「『Tsubame』は、どういう[意味]{いみ}？」","en":"Now Mariya is alone at the table. Just then, the tour bus from the cruise ship arrives. An older woman with a folding fan asks her, in English, what \"Tsubame\" means.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"まりやは、自分の声を聞いた。「Swallow」。でも、英語の swallow には、「[飲]{の}みこむ」という意味もある。まりやは、あわてて言った。「The bird. Not this.」そして、のどに手を[当]{あ}てて、ごくんと飲みこむまねをした。 *(Audio: read \"Swallow\" and \"The bird. Not this.\" in English.)*","en":"Mariya hears herself say, \"Swallow.\" But in English, \"swallow\" is also what your throat does when you eat. So she quickly adds, \"The bird. Not this,\" and puts a hand on her throat and pretends to gulp."},
{"t":"narr","text":"女の人は、[大笑]{おおわら}いした。その人の英語は、[速]{はや}くて、[歌]{うた}のようだ。リスニングテストの英語とは、ぜんぜんちがう。でも、まりやには、ぜんぶ分かった。ここには、[点]{てん}をつける人はいない。おばあさんたちは、お茶を飲みたいそうだ。まりやは、いい店を知っている。","en":"The woman laughs and laughs. Her English is fast and musical, nothing like the English on listening tests, but Mariya understands all of it. Nobody here is grading her. The visitors would like some tea, and Mariya knows a good shop.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"chiyo","mood":"hello","ja":"いらっしゃいませ。…まりやちゃん、[英語]{えいご}、じょうずですね。","en":"Welcome. ...Mariya, your English is very good.","tag":"impressed, warm","ref":"E7·L38"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"oops","ja":"ぜんぜんです。でも、[通]{つう}じたみたいです。","en":"Not at all. But I think they understood me.","gl":"通じる (つうじる): to get through, to be understood. ～みたい: it seems.","tag":"shy, a little proud","ref":"E7·L39"},
{"t":"narr","text":"八時には、店のお茶が、七月ぜんぶより[多]{おお}く[売]{う}れた。イカを[焼]{や}くにおいといっしょに、トビーが[戻]{もど}って来た。","en":"By 8 p.m., the shop has sold more tea than in all of July. Toby comes back, bringing the smell of grilled squid with him.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"sleepy","ja":"ただいま…。[源]{げん}さんにイカを[焼]{や}かされて、[岩田]{いわた}さんにビールを[飲]{の}まされた。","en":"I'm back... Gen-san had me grilling squid, and Iwata-san made me drink beer.","gl":"イカ: squid. 焼く (やく): to grill. 焼かされる, 飲まされる: to be made to grill, to be made to drink.","tag":"tired, slightly tipsy","ref":"E7·L40"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"sleepy","ja":"[楽]{たの}しそうだね。","en":"Sounds like you had a great time.","tag":"dry, teasing","ref":"E7·L41"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"tip","ja":"今日、トビーに[英語]{えいご}、[話]{はな}させられたんだけど。…でも、[楽]{たの}しかった。","en":"Today you made me speak English. ...But it was fun.","gl":"話させられる: to be made to speak.","tag":"accusing, then smiling","ref":"E7·L42"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"tip","ja":"だから、これから[毎週]{まいしゅう}[木曜日]{もくようび}の[夜]{よる}は、[英語]{えいご}で[話]{はな}す[練習]{れんしゅう}をしよう。それから、トビーは、私の言うことに「ノー」と言う練習もしなきゃだめ。","en":"So from now on, let's practice speaking English every Thursday night. And you have to practice saying no to me.","gl":"練習 (れんしゅう): practice.","tag":"decisive","ref":"E7·L43"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"oops","ja":"…はい。","en":"...Yes.","tag":"automatically","ref":"E7·L44"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"yay","ja":"ほら、もう「はい」って言った！","en":"See? You just said yes!","tag":"laughing, triumphant","ref":"E7·L45"},
{"t":"narr","text":"まりやは、もっと英語を話せるようになりたい。トビーは、「ノー」と言えるようになったほうがいい。木曜日の練習は、二人のためだ。","en":"Mariya wants to get better at speaking English, and Toby needs to learn to say no. The Thursday practice will help them both.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"トビーが笑った。まりやは、先に[目]{め}をそらした。","en":"Toby laughs. Mariya is the first to look away.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"夜九時、ちょうちんが[下]{お}ろされた。ロドリゴは、七時ごろから、ずっと、千代さんのカウンターのはしで、お[客]{きゃく}さんの絵を、ただでかいていた。","en":"At 9 p.m., the lanterns are taken down. Since about 7, Rodrigo has been sitting at the end of Chiyo's counter, drawing her customers for free.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"ちよさん、ポスターは、[明日]{あした}はがしますか。","en":"Chiyo-san, will you take the poster down tomorrow?","gl":"はがす: to peel off, to take down.","tag":"hesitant","ref":"E7·L46"},
{"t":"line","who":"chiyo","mood":"tip","ja":"はがしませんよ。[来年]{らいねん}、日にちだけ[書]{か}き[直]{なお}させますから。","en":"No, it stays up. Next year I'll just have you change the date.","gl":"日にち (ひにち): the date. 書き直す (かきなおす): to rewrite. 書き直させる: to have someone rewrite.","tag":"matter-of-fact","ref":"E7·L47"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"yay","ja":"[来年]{らいねん}…！はい！[書]{か}かせてください！","en":"Next year...! Yes! Please let me do it!","gl":"書かせてください: please let me write it. Causative + ください asks for permission.","tag":"overjoyed","ref":"E7·L48"},
{"t":"narr","text":"来年があるかどうか、千代さんにも[分]{わ}からない。でも、千代さんは、もうたのんだ。店の外の、高い段の上で、白と黒のねこが[前足]{まえあし}をなめている。ポスターの絵と、同じ[場所]{ばしょ}だ。月曜日には、かもめそうのけいじばんのねこの名前が、一つふえていた。","en":"Even Chiyo doesn't know if there will be a festival next year, but she has already asked him. Outside, on the high step, a black-and-white cat is licking her paw, in the same place as on the poster. By Monday, the list of the cat's names on the Kamome House bulletin board has one more name.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"cat","pose":"stretch","alt":"The cat licking her paw on the tea-shop step"},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u7-x1","type":"mcq","q":"Toby says [源]{げん}さんにイカを[焼]{や}かされて、[岩田]{いわた}さんにビールを[飲]{の}まされた. Who grilled the squid?","options":[{"t":"Toby, because Gen-san made him","why":"Right. [焼]{や}かされる is the causative-passive of [焼]{や}く: *to be made to grill*. The person who gives the order takes に ([源]{げん}さんに), and the person who does the work is the subject, here Toby.","ok":true},
{"t":"Gen-san, as a treat for Toby","why":"A favor would be [源]{げん}さんがイカを[焼]{や}いてくれた. With [焼]{や}かされた, Toby did the grilling, and it wasn't his choice."},
{"t":"Gen-san, because Toby made him","why":"That would be the plain causative: [源]{げん}さんにイカを[焼]{や}かせた. The passive ending, [焼]{や}かされた, turns it around: Toby was the one who was made to."},
{"t":"Iwata-san","why":"Iwata-san comes in the second half of the sentence, and his job was the beer: ビールを[飲]{の}まされた, *I was made to drink*."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u7-x2","type":"mcq","q":"Rodrigo says まつりは[今年]{ことし}で[終]{お}わるらしいですね. How does he know?","options":[{"t":"He has heard people saying so","why":"Right. ～らしい passes on what you have heard or read, without saying you know it yourself. He even gives his source: パン[屋]{や}さんで[聞]{き}きました.","ok":true},
{"t":"He can see it with his own eyes","why":"For something you can see coming, use the ます-stem + そう: [終]{お}わりそう, *it looks about to end*. らしい is for what you have heard."},
{"t":"Chiyo has just told him","why":"He is the one telling Chiyo, and she isn't impressed: [去年]{きょねん}も、そう言われましたよ."},
{"t":"He has decided it himself","why":"らしい never reports your own decision. It keeps the speaker at a distance from the news: *apparently*, *they say*."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u7-x3","type":"mcq","q":"At the English table, Mariya says ぜったい、まちがえそう. What does ～そう tell us?","options":[{"t":"She can tell a mistake is coming","why":"Right. The ます-stem + そう (まちがえ + そう) means something looks likely to happen. Mariya is guessing from her own feeling.","ok":true},
{"t":"She has heard that she will make mistakes","why":"Hearsay uses the plain form + そう, as in まちがえるそう, or らしい."},
{"t":"She has already made a mistake","why":"That would be まちがえた. She hasn't spoken yet."},
{"t":"She is telling Toby that he will make mistakes","why":"The sentence has no subject, but Mariya is talking about herself. She is the one who has to speak next."}]}},
{"t":"lang","items":["The passive leaves people out: この[通]{とお}りでは、「まっちゃ」と[呼]{よ}ばれています (*she is called Matcha*) and [去年]{きょねん}も、そう言われました (*that was said last year too*). Nobody has to say who calls her that or who said it. When the person matters, に marks them: ちよさんに[頼]{たの}まれて.","Make, and be made to: Chiyo will make Rodrigo change the date (書き[直]{なお}させます). Turn it around and you get the causative-passive, for the person on the receiving end: 行かされた, [焼]{や}かされて, [飲]{の}まされた, [話]{はな}させられた.","How do you know? まちがえそう (*I can tell I'm going to get it wrong*), [終]{お}わるらしい (*people say it will end*), つばめらしい (*I hear it means swallow*) and [通]{つう}じたみたい (*it seems they understood*). Each ending shows a different kind of evidence."]},
{"t":"reflect","q":"Mariya speaks English only after Toby has left the table. Have you ever found you could do something because the person you were relying on wasn't there?"}]},{"unit":"e3u8","n":8,"title":"The hazard map","month":"September","level":"N4 kanji","enDefault":false,"parts":[{"t":"narr","text":"つばめ[通]{どお}りのまつりに、ロドリゴのポスターがはられた。まりやは、知らない人と英語で話した。トビーは、[仲]{なか}の[悪]{わる}い[漁師]{りょうし}の二人に、[同]{おな}じ[七時]{しちじ}の[約束]{やくそく}をした。","en":"Rodrigo's poster went up all over Tsubame Street for the festival. Mariya spoke English with strangers. Toby promised the same seven o'clock to two fishermen who don't get along.","recap":true,"lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"九月の[最初]{さいしょ}の日曜日。[台風]{たいふう}は、まだ[汐浦]{しおうら}に来ていない。いつものように、[文子]{ふみこ}さんと[正一]{しょういち}さんも[道]{みち}をわたって来て、みんなで[夕]{ゆう}ごはんを食べた。今日は、[娘]{むすめ}の[恵]{めぐみ}さんと、[孫]{まご}の[颯太]{そうた}も来ている。おさらを[片付]{かたづ}けると、チェスカがテーブルに紙を一まい[置]{お}いた。いつもなら、デザートが出る[所]{ところ}だ。そして、紙を大きく[広]{ひろ}げた。六月から、ずっとたたんで持っていた紙だ。","en":"The first Sunday in September. No typhoon has reached Shioura yet this year. As usual, Fumiko-san and Shōichi-san have come across the street, and everyone has eaten dinner together. Today their daughter, Megumi, and their grandson, Sōta, are here too. When the plates are cleared, Cheska puts a sheet of paper on the table, where dessert would usually go, and unfolds it all the way. She has been carrying it, folded, since June.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"みんな、ちょっといい？これ、[市役所]{しやくしょ}でもらった[地図]{ちず}なんだけど。","en":"Everyone, do you have a minute? This is a map I got at the city office.","gl":"市役所 (しやくしょ): the city office.","tag":"a little nervous, then steady","ref":"E8·L1"},
{"t":"plates","title":"The map","hint":"Read each line of the map, then tap it to check.","items":[{"ja":"汐浦市 内水ハザードマップ","ro":"しおうらし ないすい ハザードマップ","who":"The Shioura hazard map for *naisui*: flooding from rain that can't drain out of the town. 内 is *inside* and 水 is *water*. Japanese cities publish hazard maps like this one, and you can get one free at the city office."},{"ja":"赤：〇・五メートル以上","ro":"あか：れいてんご メートル いじょう","who":"Red: water half a meter deep or more. 以上 means *that much or more*, and it includes the number. Half a meter is about knee height, and that is deep enough to make walking dangerous."},{"ja":"避難所：東小学校","ro":"ひなんじょ：ひがし しょうがっこう","who":"Evacuation shelter: East Elementary School. 避難 (ひなん) means getting away from danger, and 所 is a place. Neither kanji of 避難 is on the N4 list, but it is a word worth knowing by sight. The school is on the higher ground behind the old town, fifteen minutes away on foot."},{"ja":"大雨のときは、早めにひなんしましょう","ro":"おおあめの ときは、はやめに ひなんしましょう","who":"*In heavy rain, evacuate early.* 早め means *a little early*: before you are sure you need to go."}]},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"think","ja":"「うちみず…ハザードマップ」。","en":"\"Uchimizu... hazard map.\"","tag":"reading slowly, unsure","ref":"E8·L2"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"tip","ja":"「ないすい」だよ。「[内]{うち}」に「水」と書いて、「ないすい」。","en":"It's \"naisui.\" You write \"inside\" and \"water,\" and you read it \"naisui.\"","tag":"gently helping","ref":"E8·L3"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"ありがとう。川の水じゃなくて、[町]{まち}の[中]{なか}にふった雨の水のこと。","en":"Thanks. It doesn't mean river water. It means the rain that falls inside the town.","gl":"ふる (降る): to fall, of rain or snow.","tag":"grateful, focused","ref":"E8·L4"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"大雨で川の水が[高]{たか}くなると、[水門]{すいもん}が[閉]{し}まる。すると、[町]{まち}の水は[外]{そと}に出られない。","en":"When heavy rain makes the river rise, the floodgates close. Then the water in the town can't get out.","gl":"水門 (すいもん): a floodgate, in the river bank. 閉まる (しまる): to close. すると: and then.","tag":"clear, explaining","ref":"E8·L5"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"この[家]{いえ}はどこ？","en":"Where's this house?","tag":"worried","ref":"E8·L6"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"ここ。[赤]{あか}い[所]{ところ}。","en":"Here. In the red part.","tag":"quietly","ref":"E8·L7"},
{"t":"narr","text":"だれも話さない。ロドリゴは、自分のひざの[所]{ところ}に手を[当]{あ}てた。〇・五メートルだ。*(Audio: れいてんご.)* 地図の赤は、川から山の下まで[続]{つづ}いている。この家も、バス[停]{てい}も、つばめ通りも、ぜんぶ赤だ。","en":"Nobody speaks. Rodrigo holds his hand at his knee: half a meter. On the map, the red runs from the river to the foot of the hill. This house, the bus stop and all of Tsubame Street are red.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"think","ja":"おばあちゃんの[店]{みせ}も…[赤]{あか}？","en":"My grandmother's shop too... is it red?","tag":"uneasy","ref":"E8·L8"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"うん。[赤]{あか}。","en":"Yes. Red.","tag":"softly","ref":"E8·L9"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"じゃあ、[白]{しろ}い[所]{ところ}は[安全]{あんぜん}？","en":"So the white parts are safe?","gl":"安全 (あんぜん): safe.","tag":"hopeful","ref":"E8·L10"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"[白]{しろ}は、「[安全]{あんぜん}」という[意味]{いみ}じゃないよ。「ここまでは来ないと[思]{おも}う」という[意味]{いみ}。","en":"White doesn't mean \"safe.\" It means \"we don't think the water will come this far.\"","gl":"意味 (いみ): meaning. ～という意味: it means ～.","tag":"serious","ref":"E8·L11"},
{"t":"narr","text":"恵さんは、地図の赤い所を、しばらく見ていた。それから、[両親]{りょうしん}の[方]{ほう}を[向]{む}いた。","en":"Megumi looks at the red area for a while. Then she turns to her parents.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"megumi","mood":"think","ja":"お父さん、お母さん。大雨のときは、早めに行ってね。私、[夜勤]{やきん}の日は、[来]{こ}られないから。","en":"Dad, Mom. When there's heavy rain, go early, OK? On my night-shift days, I can't come.","gl":"夜勤 (やきん): a night shift. 来られない (こられない): can't come.","tag":"worried, firm","ref":"E8·L12"},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"sleepy","ja":"…分かった。","en":"...All right.","tag":"gruff, after a pause","ref":"E8·L13"},
{"t":"line","who":"sota","mood":"think","ja":"おじいちゃん、にゃん[助]{すけ}も、つれて行く？","en":"Grandpa, are we taking Nyansuke too?","tag":"curious, innocent","ref":"E8·L14"},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"tip","ja":"にゃん[太郎]{たろう}は、自分で行く。","en":"Nyantarō goes on his own.","tag":"matter-of-fact","ref":"E8·L15"},
{"t":"narr","text":"ねこは、いつも自分で決める。","en":"The cat always decides for herself.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"think","ja":"大学の[雨量計]{うりょうけい}、[毎日]{まいにち}見ることにする。","en":"I'm going to check the university's rain gauge every day.","gl":"雨量計 (うりょうけい): a rain gauge.","tag":"determined","ref":"E8·L16"},
{"t":"narr","text":"トビーは、さっきからスマホを手の中で[回]{まわ}している。六月から、土曜日は[港]{みなと}で[録音]{ろくおん}をしている。年をとった漁師にマイクを[向]{む}けると、[天気]{てんき}の話を[始]{はじ}める人が多い。","en":"Toby has been turning his phone over in his hand. Since June, he has spent his Saturdays at the harbor, recording. When you hold a microphone up to an old fisherman, he will often start talking about the weather.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"think","ja":"チェスカ、[源]{げん}さんの[話]{はなし}も[聞]{き}いてくれる？子どものとき、この[町]{まち}で[大水]{おおみず}が出たんだって。","en":"Cheska, would you listen to Gen-san's story too? He says there was a big flood in this town when he was a child.","gl":"大水が出る (おおみずがでる): a flood happens; an everyday way to say it.","tag":"hesitant","ref":"E8·L17"},
{"t":"narr","text":"トビーは、[再生]{さいせい}ボタンをおした。とても古い[声]{こえ}が、[部屋]{へや}に[流]{なが}れた。[教科書]{きょうかしょ}にはない日本語だ。文子さんと正一さんには、ぜんぶ分かる。トビーは、ほかの人のために、ふつうの日本語に[直]{なお}していく。でも、[一か所]{いっかしょ}で[止]{と}まった。トビーにも分からない言い方がある。","en":"Toby presses play. A very old voice fills the room, speaking a Japanese you won't find in any textbook. Fumiko-san and Shōichi-san understand every word. Toby puts it into standard Japanese for everyone else. At one point he stops: there is a phrase even he doesn't know.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"think","ja":"「みずが、でてきたがや」…？","en":"\"Mizu ga detekita ga ya\"...?","gl":"がや: in the old local dialect, it works like ～んだ.","tag":"puzzled, imitating the recording","ref":"E8·L18"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"hello","ja":"「水が出てきたんだ」っていう[意味]{いみ}だよ。[島]{しま}のおじいちゃんも、そう言う。","en":"It means \"the water came out, you see.\" The old captain on my island talks like that too.","tag":"helpful, proud","ref":"E8·L19"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"ありがとう。…「水は川から来なかった。[道]{みち}の[下]{した}から来た」。","en":"Thanks. ...\"The water didn't come from the river. It came up from under the road.\"","tag":"slowly, translating","ref":"E8·L20"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"「[夕方]{ゆうがた}に[始]{はじ}まって、[朝]{あさ}まで[止]{と}まらなかった。でも、つばめ[通]{どお}りまでは来なかった」。","en":"\"It started in the evening and didn't stop until morning. But it never reached Tsubame Street.\"","tag":"reading on, carefully","ref":"E8·L21"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"think","ja":"…それは、[何年前]{なんねんまえ}の[話]{はなし}？","en":"...How long ago was this?","tag":"skeptical","ref":"E8·L22"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"[七十年]{ななじゅうねん}ぐらい[前]{まえ}。[源]{げん}さんが[九]{きゅう}さいのとき。","en":"About seventy years ago. Gen-san was nine.","tag":"earnest","ref":"E8·L23"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"[七十年前]{ななじゅうねんまえ}の[思]{おも}い[出]{で}は、データじゃないよ。今はポンプもあるし、[道]{みち}も[新]{あたら}しいし。[地図]{ちず}では、つばめ[通]{どお}りも[赤]{あか}。","en":"A memory from seventy years ago isn't data. There are pumps now, and the roads are new. On the map, Tsubame Street is red too.","gl":"思い出 (おもいで): a memory. データ: data. ポンプ: a pump.","tag":"firm, not unkind","ref":"E8·L24"},
{"t":"narr","text":"トビーは、いつも人の話に「そうだね」と言う。みんなは、トビーがそう言うのを[待]{ま}った。","en":"Toby usually agrees with whatever people say. Everyone at the table waits for him to agree now.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"think","ja":"…でも、この[地図]{ちず}を[作]{つく}った[人]{ひと}は、その水を見てないよ。[源]{げん}さんは、その[中]{なか}を[歩]{ある}いたんだ。","en":"...But the people who made this map never saw that water. Gen-san walked through it.","tag":"quiet but stubborn","ref":"E8·L25"},
{"t":"narr","text":"チェスカには、言いたいことがある。長い話だ。[十代]{じゅうだい}のころの、フィリピンの台風の話だ。でも、今は言わない。","en":"Cheska has something she could say to that. It is a long story, about a typhoon in the Philippines when she was a teenager. She doesn't tell it now.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"…[地図]{ちず}は、[計算]{けいさん}だよ。[一番]{いちばん}[悪]{わる}い雨のときの。","en":"...A map is a calculation, for the worst rain we could get.","gl":"計算 (けいさん): a calculation.","tag":"sighs, reasonable","ref":"E8·L26"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"[源]{げん}さんの[話]{はなし}は、[一回]{いっかい}の雨だけだね。[本当]{ほんとう}にふった雨の。","en":"And Gen-san's story is about only one storm. But it's a storm that really happened.","gl":"本当に (ほんとうに): really.","tag":"thoughtful","ref":"E8·L27"},
{"t":"narr","text":"二人とも、[片方]{かたほう}だけでは[足]{た}りないと分かっている。正一さんは、テーブルの[向]{む}こうから、地図をさかさまに見ていた。","en":"Both of them know that one side alone isn't enough. Shōichi-san has been reading the map upside down from the other side of the table.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"tip","ja":"[源]{げん}の[話]{はなし}は、[本当]{ほんとう}だ。おれも見た。つばめ[通]{どお}りは、[昔]{むかし}の[堤防]{ていぼう}の[上]{うえ}だから、[少]{すこ}し[高]{たか}い。","en":"Gen's story is true. I saw it too. Tsubame Street is built on top of the old sea wall, so it's a little higher.","gl":"昔 (むかし): long ago. 堤防 (ていぼう): an embankment or sea wall.","tag":"low, certain","ref":"E8·L28"},
{"t":"narr","text":"三百年前、つばめ通りのあたりは、海べだった。今も、まわりより、[階段]{かいだん}[四段]{よんだん}ぐらい高い。でも、地図の四角は大きいので、その高さは地図に出ない。チェスカは、正一さんを見て、それから地図を見た。そして、ねこの名前のリストのえんぴつを[借]{か}りて、つばめ通りに[線]{せん}を[引]{ひ}いた。[横]{よこ}に、「源さんの話」と書いた。これで、地図には、計算と、人が見たことの[両方]{りょうほう}がある。","en":"Three hundred years ago, the area around Tsubame Street was the seashore. Even now, it is about four steps higher than the streets around it, but the map is made of squares, and each square is too big to show such a small rise. Cheska looks at Shōichi-san, and then at the map. She borrows the pencil from the cat-name list and draws a line along Tsubame Street. Beside it she writes 源さんの話, \"Gen-san's story.\" Now the map shows both: the printed calculation and, in pencil, what someone saw.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"じゃあ、[学校]{がっこう}へは、川の[道]{みち}じゃなくて、つばめ[通]{どお}りを[通]{とお}って行こう。","en":"Then let's go to the school along Tsubame Street, not by the river road.","tag":"decisive","ref":"E8·L29"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"うん。それから、[地図]{ちず}の言う[通]{とお}り、[早]{はや}めに出よう。[源]{げん}さんの[家族]{かぞく}は、[朝]{あさ}まで[二階]{にかい}から[下]{お}りられなかったんだって。","en":"Yes. And let's leave early, like the map says. Gen-san's family couldn't come downstairs until morning.","gl":"～の言う通り (いうとおり): just as ～ says. 二階 (にかい): upstairs, the second floor. 下りる (おりる): to come down.","tag":"agreeing, relieved","ref":"E8·L30"},
{"t":"narr","text":"道は、源さんの話から。時間は、地図から。正一さんは、地図のタイトルの、一つ目の漢字に[指]{ゆび}を置いた。町の名前の、むずかしい[方]{ほう}の漢字だ。","en":"The route comes from Gen-san's story, and the timing comes from the map. Shōichi-san puts a finger on the first kanji of the map's title, the harder kanji in the town's name.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"hello","ja":"さんずいに、[夕方]{ゆうがた}の[夕]{ゆう}。「[汐]{しお}」は、夕方のしおだ。[朝]{あさ}のしおは、[別]{べつ}の[字]{じ}を書く。","en":"The water radical, and the 夕 of 夕方, \"evening.\" 汐 is the evening tide. The morning tide is written with a different kanji.","gl":"さんずい: the name of 氵, the three-stroke *water* part on the left of a kanji. しお: the tide. 別の字 (べつのじ): a different character.","tag":"slowly, tracing the kanji","ref":"E8·L31"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"yay","ja":"[朝]{あさ}のしおは、「[潮]{しお}」ですよね。さんずいに、朝。私の[島]{しま}の[字]{じ}です！","en":"The morning tide is 潮, right? The water radical plus 朝. That's my island's kanji!","tag":"delighted","ref":"E8·L32"},
{"t":"note","text":"汐 isn't in the usual JLPT kanji lists, and it isn't one of the jōyō kanji taught in school, which is why I have chosen to give Shioura furigana since April. But you can take it apart now: 氵 is water and 夕 is evening. Japanese has two kanji for the tide: 潮, with 朝 (morning) inside it, and 汐, with 夕 (evening). Mariya's island, 潮島 (しおじま), got the morning one, and this town got the evening one. A kanji you can't read is often made of two that you can."},
{"t":"narr","text":"チェスカは、地図をもうたたまなかった。けいじばんの、ねこの名前のリストのとなりにはった。えんぴつの線もいっしょだ。次の朝、地図の下に、[一行]{いちぎょう}ふえていた。文子さんの字だ。「[九人]{きゅうにん}で行きましょう」。七人の[住人]{じゅうにん}と、文子さんと正一さんで、九人だ。正一さんは、げんかんを通るときにそれを読んで、バロメーターをトントンとたたいた。何も言わなかった。階段のそばの[棚]{たな}では、先週こわれたかいとの[自転車]{じてんしゃ}のライトが、もう[直]{なお}っていた。","en":"Cheska doesn't fold the map up again. She pins it on the bulletin board, next to the list of the cat's names, pencil line and all. The next morning, there is one more line at the bottom, in Fumiko-san's neat teacher's handwriting: 九人で行きましょう, \"Let's go, all nine of us.\" That is the seven residents plus Fumiko-san and Shōichi-san. Shōichi-san reads it on his way through the hall, taps the barometer, and says nothing. On the shelf by the stairs, Kaito's bike light, which stopped working last week, has been fixed.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u8-x1","type":"mcq","q":"On the map, Kamome House is in a 赤 area: 〇・五メートル以上. What does that tell the residents?","options":[{"t":"In the worst rain, the water there could be half a meter deep or more","why":"Right. 以上 means *that much or more*, and it includes the number itself. Cheska explains what the map is: a calculation for the worst rain, [一番]{いちばん}[悪]{わる}い雨のときの[計算]{けいさん}.","ok":true},
{"t":"The water there will be less than half a meter deep","why":"*Half a meter or less* would be 〇・五メートル以下. 以上 goes the other way: from the number up."},
{"t":"The house is half a meter higher than the river","why":"The number is the depth of the water, not the height of the land. Red is where water could be half a meter deep or more."},
{"t":"The house is in a safe area","why":"On this map, color means risk. Even white is not a promise: [白]{しろ}は、「[安全]{あんぜん}」という[意味]{いみ}じゃないよ."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u8-x2","type":"type","q":"Cheska first reads 内水 as うちみず. Type the reading Toby gives her, in hiragana.","answer":"ないすい","why":"ないすい: 内 (ナイ, inside) + 水 (スイ, water). On their own they are read うち and みず, but together they use their on-readings.","book":"Write the reading of 内水 (flooding from rain trapped inside the river bank) in hiragana.","hint":"In a two-kanji word, both kanji usually take their on-readings. 水 is スイ, as in 水よう日.","wrongs":[{"v":"うちみず","why":"Those are the kun-readings, the ones each kanji has when it stands alone: [内]{うち}, [水]{みず}. Inside a two-kanji word they usually switch to the on-readings: ナイ and スイ."},{"v":"ないみず","why":"Half right: 内 is ナイ here. But 水 takes its on-reading too, スイ, as in 水よう日."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u8-x3","type":"mcq","q":"Megumi says [夜勤]{やきん}の日は、[来]{こ}られないから. What does 来られない mean here?","options":[{"t":"\"I can't come\"","why":"Right. 来られる is the potential form of 来る, so 来られない is *can't come*. から gives it as her reason for asking her parents to go early.","ok":true},
{"t":"\"I won't be visited\"","why":"来られる can also be a passive, but nobody is visiting Megumi. She is talking about what she is able to do."},
{"t":"\"I didn't come\"","why":"The past would be 来なかった. She is talking about future night shifts."},
{"t":"\"I mustn't come\"","why":"\"Mustn't\" would be 来てはいけない. Nothing forbids her; her work makes it impossible."}]}},
{"t":"lang","items":["Kun and on: Cheska reads 内水 as うちみず, one kanji at a time. As a word, it is ないすい. The same thing happens with 大水 (おおみず, both kun), 大雨 (おおあめ, both kun) and [地図]{ちず} (both on), so it is always worth checking a new compound.","Things that happen by themselves: [水門]{すいもん}が[閉]{し}まる, [夕方]{ゆうがた}に[始]{はじ}まって, [朝]{あさ}まで[止]{と}まらなかった. These are the intransitive halves of [閉]{し}める・[閉]{し}まる, [始]{はじ}める・[始]{はじ}まる and [止]{と}める・[止]{と}まる. Nobody in the sentence closes, starts or stops anything, so they take が.","One kanji, several jobs: 通 is the street in つばめ[通]{どお}り, the verb in [通]{とお}って行こう, and *just as* in [地図]{ちず}の言う[通]{とお}り. In a street name, とおり becomes どおり."]},
{"t":"reflect","q":"Cheska trusts the map and Toby trusts the fisherman, and in the end they use both. When you have to decide something, which do you reach for first: the numbers, or someone who was there?"}]},{"unit":"e3u9","n":9,"title":"The night of the rain","month":"September","level":"N3","enDefault":false,"parts":[{"t":"narr","text":"九月の日曜日、チェスカが[市]{し}のハザードマップをみんなに見せた。かもめ荘は、地図の赤い所にある。[源]{げん}さんの、七十年前の[大水]{おおみず}の話も聞いた。みんなで[決]{き}めた。大雨のときは、早めに、つばめ[通]{どお}りを通って学校へ行く。[文子]{ふみこ}さんは、地図の下にえんぴつで書いた。「[九人]{きゅうにん}で行きましょう。」","en":"One Sunday in September, Cheska showed everyone the city's hazard map. Kamome House is in a red area. They also heard Gen-san's story about a big flood seventy years ago. Together they decided that in heavy rain, they would leave early and walk to the school along Tsubame Street. At the bottom of the map, Fumiko-san wrote in pencil: \"Let's go, all nine of us.\"","recap":true,"lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[十六日後]{じゅうろくにちご}。朝から雨がふっている。はじめは、しとしとと[弱]{よわ}い雨だった。昼をすぎると、ザーザーと強くなった。[雨雲]{あまぐも}は、町の上から動かない。","en":"Sixteen days later, it has been raining since morning. At first it was a light, steady rain. After noon it grew heavy. The rain clouds sit over the town and don't move.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"think","ja":"[一時間]{いちじかん}に、[五十]{ごじゅう}ミリ[超]{こ}えた。","en":"It's gone over fifty millimeters an hour.","gl":"超える (こえる): to go over. ミリ: millimeters (of rain).","tag":"quietly, tense","ref":"E9·L1"},
{"t":"narr","text":"イエンは昼から、大学の[雨量計]{うりょうけい}のページを見ている。この[数字]{すうじ}を言ってからは、もう声に出して読まなくなった。[夕方]{ゆうがた}になっても、ねこは来ない。午後六時五十分。[家]{いえ}じゅうのスマホが、いっせいに[鳴]{な}った。","en":"Since lunch, Yến has been watching the university's rain-gauge page. After she says this number, she stops reading the numbers aloud. Evening comes, and the cat hasn't come. At 6:50 p.m., every phone in the house rings at the same time.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"plates","title":"The alert","hint":"Read each line of the alert, then tap it to check.","items":[{"ja":"【警戒レベル3】高齢者等避難","ro":"けいかいレベル さん こうれいしゃとう ひなん","who":"*Alert Level 3: older people and others, evacuate.* 警戒 is being on guard, 高齢者 is older people, and 等 means *and others*: anyone who needs extra time. The city sends it. It tells these people to leave now, and everyone else to get ready."},{"ja":"大雨のため、内水氾濫のおそれがあります","ro":"おおあめの ため、ないすいはんらんの おそれが あります","who":"*Because of heavy rain, there is a risk of flooding in town.* 内水氾濫 is flooding from rain that can't drain away. 氾濫 (はんらん) is water overflowing, and おそれ is a risk. Here ～のため means \"because of.\" Notices often use it."},{"ja":"対象：旧市街の全域","ro":"たいしょう：きゅうしがいの ぜんいき","who":"*Applies to: the whole old town.* That is the red area on Cheska's map."},{"ja":"避難所：東小学校 体育館","ro":"ひなんじょ：ひがししょうがっこう たいいくかん","who":"*Shelter: the gym at East Elementary School.*"}]},
{"t":"narr","text":"[文子]{ふみこ}さんは、もうレインコートを[着]{き}て、げんかんに立っていた。[町内会]{ちょうないかい}のグループチャットを[管理]{かんり}しているのは、文子さんだ。","en":"Fumiko-san is already standing in the front hall in her raincoat. She is the one who runs the neighborhood association's group chat.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"tip","ja":"[水門]{すいもん}が[閉]{し}まったそうです。[町内会]{ちょうないかい}のチャットに書いてありました。","en":"They say the floodgates have closed. It was in the neighborhood association's chat.","gl":"水門 (すいもん): a floodgate. 町内会 (ちょうないかい): the neighborhood association.","tag":"calm, reading her phone","ref":"E9·L2"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"sleepy","ja":"それから、「[高齢者]{こうれいしゃ}」というのは、主人と私のことですね。","en":"And \"older people,\" I suppose, means my husband and me.","gl":"高齢者 (こうれいしゃ): older people, the elderly. 主人 (しゅじん): my husband.","tag":"dry, wry","ref":"E9·L3"},
{"t":"narr","text":"みんなが、チェスカを見た。チェスカは、フィリピンの[市役所]{しやくしょ}で五年間、[防災]{ぼうさい}の仕事をしていた。去年の十月に来たときは、日本語があまり話せなかった。今は、ずいぶん上手になった。","en":"Everyone looks at Cheska. She worked in disaster prevention at a city office in the Philippines for five years. When she arrived last October, she could speak very little Japanese. She has improved a lot since then.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"レベル3は、さとうさんたちにとって「今すぐ」という意味です。それに、[安全]{あんぜん}のために、[全員]{ぜんいん}で今出た[方]{ほう}がいいと思います。","en":"For you and Mr. Satō, Level 3 means \"right now.\" And to be safe, I think all of us should go now.","gl":"全員 (ぜんいん): everyone, all of us. 今すぐ: right now.","tag":"urgent but calm","ref":"E9·L4"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"[内水氾濫]{ないすいはんらん}は、始まると早いですから。出るのは、早ければ早いほどいいです。","en":"Once this kind of flooding starts, it's quick. The earlier we go, the better.","tag":"steady, serious","ref":"E9·L5"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"think","ja":"…でも、これは私の意見です。みんなに[決]{き}めてほしいです。","en":"...But that's my opinion. I'd like all of you to decide.","gl":"決める (きめる): to decide.","tag":"softer, careful","ref":"E9·L6"},
{"t":"narr","text":"チェスカは、そこで話をやめた。みんなの[顔]{かお}を見て、待っている。","en":"Cheska stops there. She looks at everyone's faces and waits.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"主人と私は、行くことにしました。","en":"My husband and I have decided to go.","tag":"calm, decided","ref":"E9·L7"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[正一]{しょういち}さんは、ぼうしをかぶって、[文子]{ふみこ}さんのうしろに立っていた。げんかんのバロメーターを、[指]{ゆび}でトントンとたたく。","en":"Shōichi-san is standing behind her with his cap on. He taps the barometer in the hall with one finger.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"think","ja":"…まだ[下]{さ}がる。","en":"...It's still dropping.","gl":"下がる (さがる): to go down.","tag":"low, certain","ref":"E9·L8"},
{"t":"narr","text":"ほかのみんなも、何も言わないで、じゅんびを始めた。トビーは、もうくつをはいている。動かないのは、あおいだけだ。スマホを耳に[当]{あ}てている。","en":"The others start getting ready without a word. Toby already has his shoes on. Only Aoi is standing still, her phone at her ear.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"あおい、[手伝]{てつだ}って。下の物を[二階]{にかい}に[上]{あ}げたいの。","en":"Aoi, help me. I want to carry the things from downstairs up to the second floor.","tag":"brisk, urgent","ref":"E9·L9"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"oops","ja":"ごめん、今、おばあちゃんに電話してるとこ。[三回]{さんかい}かけたのに、出ないの。","en":"Sorry, I'm in the middle of calling my grandmother. I've tried three times, and she isn't picking up.","gl":"～てるとこ: casual ～ているところ, right in the middle of doing. 電話に出る: to answer the phone.","tag":"anxious, phone to her ear","ref":"E9·L10"},
{"t":"narr","text":"「おばあちゃん」という言葉を聞いて、チェスカはすぐに分かった。","en":"When she hears おばあちゃん, Cheska understands at once.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"think","ja":"…あ、出た。おばあちゃん？うん。うん。動かないで。今から行くから。","en":"...Oh, she's picked up. Grandma? Yes. Yes. Don't move. I'm coming now.","tag":"relieved, then firm","ref":"E9·L11"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"tip","ja":"チェスカ、私は学校じゃなくて、おばあちゃんの[所]{ところ}に行くことにする。おばあちゃんの家は店の[二階]{にかい}だし、つばめ[通]{どお}りは少し高いはずだから。","en":"Cheska, I've decided to go to my grandmother's, not the school. She lives above the shop, and Tsubame Street should be a little higher.","tag":"determined","ref":"E9·L12"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[計画]{けいかく}は「[九人]{きゅうにん}で学校へ」だ。地図に、えんぴつで書いてある。","en":"The plan is \"all nine to the school.\" It is written on the map, in pencil.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"think","ja":"…[本当]{ほんとう}は、[全員]{ぜんいん}で学校に行ってほしい。","en":"...I'd really rather we all went to the school.","tag":"torn, quietly","ref":"E9·L13"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"hello","ja":"分かってる。でも、おばあちゃんは[一人]{ひとり}で[階段]{かいだん}を[下]{お}りられないの。雨の中を学校まで歩かせたくない。","en":"I know. But she can't get down the stairs by herself. And I don't want to make her walk to the school in this rain.","gl":"階段 (かいだん): stairs.","tag":"pleading, firm","ref":"E9·L14"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"…分かった。おばあちゃんと[二階]{にかい}にいて。[下]{お}りないで。[着]{つ}いたら、すぐ[連絡]{れんらく}して。","en":"...All right. Stay upstairs with your grandmother, and don't come down. Message me as soon as you get there.","gl":"連絡 (れんらく)する: to get in touch.","tag":"calm, giving instructions","ref":"E9·L15"},
{"t":"narr","text":"おばあちゃんのことは、あおいが[決]{き}める。それに、外に出る[方]{ほう}があぶないときは、じょうぶな[建物]{たてもの}の二階にいることも、ひなんの[方法]{ほうほう}の一つだ。[市]{し}のホームページにも、そう書いてある。あおいも、みんなといっしょに出て、とちゅうでわかれる。","en":"It is Aoi's grandmother, so it is Aoi's decision. And when going outside is more dangerous, staying upstairs in a strong building is also a way to evacuate. The city's website says so too. Aoi will set out with everyone else and split off on the way.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[運]{はこ}べる物は、ぜんぶ二階に上げた。すいはんき。ロドリゴのインク十一本。ふとんを上げる時間は、なかった。文子さんは、ハンドバッグと手紙のかんを持って、いそいで[道]{みち}のむこうの家から[戻]{もど}って来た。","en":"Everything they can carry goes upstairs: the rice cooker, Rodrigo's eleven bottles of ink. There is no time for the futons. Fumiko-san hurries back from her house across the street with her handbag and the tin of letters.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"はぐれないように、[二人]{ふたり}ずつ歩いて。川の道じゃなくて、つばめ[通]{どお}りを通って行くよ。","en":"Walk in pairs, so nobody gets separated. We're going by Tsubame Street, not the river road.","gl":"はぐれる: to get separated from the people you are with. ～ずつ: ～ at a time.","tag":"clear, commanding","ref":"E9·L16"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"tip","ja":"じゃあ、トビーとは私が歩くことにするね。だれかに「手伝って」って言われたら、すぐ止まっちゃう人だから。","en":"Then I'll walk with Toby. If anyone asks him for help, he'll stop right there. That's just how he is.","gl":"止まっちゃう: casual 止まってしまう, \"he'll end up stopping\".","tag":"brisk, teasing","ref":"E9·L17"},
{"t":"narr","text":"かいとは、今夜のバイトが休みになった。[正一]{しょういち}さんのかばんに、手をのばす。","en":"Kaito's night shift has been canceled. He reaches for Shōichi-san's bag.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"hello","ja":"ぼくが持ちます。","en":"I'll carry it.","tag":"quiet, serious","ref":"E9·L18"},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"sleepy","ja":"…たのむ。","en":"...Thanks.","tag":"gruff, after a pause","ref":"E9·L19"},
{"t":"narr","text":"正一さんが、かいとにこんなに話したのは、はじめてだ。","en":"It is the most Shōichi-san has ever said to Kaito.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"午後七時二十分。[九人]{きゅうにん}は、家を出た。[角]{かど}を[曲]{ま}がると、マンホールのふたのまわりから、水がぶくぶくとわき出していた。トビーは、チェスカの[顔]{かお}を見た。二人とも、[源]{げん}さんの話を思い出している。でも、何も言わない。つばめ[通]{どお}りは、[屋根]{やね}のある[商店街]{しょうてんがい}だ。屋根の下は、まだかわいていた。おばあちゃんの店の前で、あおいがグループからはなれた。「二階に上がったら、[連絡]{れんらく}するね。」ほかの八人は、[坂]{さか}を[上]{のぼ}って、学校へ[向]{む}かった。","en":"At 7:20 p.m., all nine leave the house. At the corner, water is bubbling up around a manhole cover. Toby looks at Cheska. They are both thinking of Gen-san's story, but neither says anything. Tsubame Street is a covered shopping street, and under its roof the ground is still dry. In front of her grandmother's shop, Aoi leaves the group: \"I'll message you when I'm upstairs.\" The other eight go up the hill to the school.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"ひなん[所]{じょ}は、[東小学校]{ひがししょうがっこう}の[体育館]{たいいくかん}だ。[入口]{いりぐち}で、[市役所]{しやくしょ}の[防災課]{ぼうさいか}の[松本]{まつもと}さんが、名前のリストを持って立っていた。文子さんは、[昔]{むかし}この学校の先生だった。だから、[毛布]{もうふ}がある場所を知っている。体育館は明るい。[窓]{まど}から見える古い町にも、電気がついている。でも、その道は水の下だ。","en":"The shelter is the gym at East Elementary School. At the door stands Mr. Matsumoto, from the disaster-prevention section of the city office, holding a list of names. Fumiko-san used to teach at this school, so she knows where the blankets are. The gym is bright. Through the windows, they can see lights on in the old town too. But its streets are under water.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"午後九時半。また、スマホが[鳴]{な}った。","en":"At 9:30 p.m., every phone goes off again.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"plates","title":"The second alert","hint":"Read each line, then tap it to check.","items":[{"ja":"【警戒レベル4】避難指示","ro":"けいかいレベル よん ひなんしじ","who":"*Alert Level 4: evacuation instruction.* Everyone in the area should get somewhere safe. There is a Level 5, but it is not a signal to leave: it means the disaster is already happening. The rule is to leave by Level 4 at the latest."},{"ja":"旧市街で道路が冠水しています","ro":"きゅうしがいで どうろが かんすい しています","who":"*Roads in the old town are under water.* 道路 (どうろ) is a road, and 冠水 (かんすい) means covered with water."}]},
{"t":"narr","text":"かもめ荘のみんなが体育館に来て、もう二時間たった。あおいからは、ずっと前に「[着]{つ}いた」とメッセージが来ている。チェスカは、タオルをくばる[係]{かかり}を手伝っていた。午後十時半。[暗]{くら}い雨の中から、[若]{わか}い女の人が六人、入って来た。魚の工場の[上着]{うわぎ}を着ている。ひざまで、びしょびしょだ。[先頭]{せんとう}の人は、スマホをビニールぶくろに入れていた。","en":"The Kamome House group has been at the gym for two hours now. Aoi's message came long ago: 着いた (I'm here). Cheska is helping at the towel table. At 10:30 p.m., six young women come in out of the dark rain. They are wearing jackets from the seafood plant and are wet up to the knees. The woman in front has her phone in a plastic bag.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"こんばんは。タオルをどうぞ。[何人]{なんにん}ですか。","en":"Good evening. Have a towel. How many of you are there?","tag":"warm, professional","ref":"E9·L20"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"oops","ja":"デウィさん！","en":"Dewi-san!","tag":"shocked, relieved","ref":"E9·L21"},
{"t":"line","who":"dewi","mood":"hello","ja":"ロドリゴさん！…よかった。","en":"Rodrigo-san! ...Thank goodness.","tag":"out of breath, relieved","ref":"E9·L22"},
{"t":"narr","text":"ロドリゴとデウィは、同じ工場で[働]{はたら}いている。デウィは、チェスカの方を[向]{む}いた。","en":"Rodrigo and Dewi work at the same seafood plant. Dewi turns to Cheska.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"dewi","mood":"hello","ja":"ありがとうございます。六人です。魚の工場の[寮]{りょう}から来ました。デウィです。","en":"Thank you. Six. We've come from the dormitory at the seafood plant. I'm Dewi.","gl":"寮 (りょう): a dormitory. 工場 (こうじょう): a factory, a plant.","tag":"shivering, polite","ref":"E9·L23"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"チェスカです。[寮]{りょう}の人は、これで[全員]{ぜんいん}ですか。","en":"I'm Cheska. Is this everyone from the dormitory?","tag":"calm, kind","ref":"E9·L24"},
{"t":"line","who":"dewi","mood":"tip","ja":"はい。[数]{かぞ}えました。[全員]{ぜんいん}います。","en":"Yes. I counted. Everyone is here.","gl":"数える (かぞえる): to count.","tag":"firm, proud","ref":"E9·L25"},
{"t":"narr","text":"デウィ・ラハユはインドネシア人で、チェスカはフィリピン人だ。二人は、日本語で話している。","en":"Dewi Rahayu is from Indonesia, and Cheska is from the Philippines. They are talking in Japanese.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"think","ja":"スマホのアラームは[鳴]{な}りましたか。","en":"Did the alarm on your phones go off?","gl":"鳴る (なる): to sound, to ring.","tag":"careful","ref":"E9·L26"},
{"t":"line","who":"dewi","mood":"oops","ja":"[鳴]{な}りました。大きい音で、[二回]{にかい}。でも、漢字ばかりで、だれも読めませんでした。","en":"It did. Loudly, twice. But it was all kanji, and none of us could read it.","gl":"～ばかり: nothing but ～.","tag":"frustrated","ref":"E9·L27"},
{"t":"line","who":"dewi","mood":"think","ja":"「ひなん」という[言葉]{ことば}は知っています。聞けば分かります。でも、字は読めないんです。","en":"I know the word hinan, \"evacuate.\" If I hear it, I understand. But I can't read the characters.","gl":"言葉 (ことば): a word; language.","tag":"upset, explaining","ref":"E9·L28"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"think","ja":"会社から[連絡]{れんらく}はありませんでしたか。","en":"Did the company contact you?","tag":"probing, gentle","ref":"E9·L29"},
{"t":"line","who":"dewi","mood":"hello","ja":"[寮]{りょう}には、会社の人が知らせることになっています。でも、今日は工場が休みで、だれも来ませんでした。","en":"Someone from the company is supposed to tell the dormitory. But the plant was closed today, and nobody came.","gl":"知らせる (しらせる): to let someone know. ～ことになっている: it is the arrangement that ～.","tag":"tired, bitter","ref":"E9·L30"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"think","ja":"じゃあ、どうして分かったんですか。","en":"Then how did you find out?","tag":"curious, gentle","ref":"E9·L31"},
{"t":"line","who":"dewi","mood":"hello","ja":"友だちのおかげです。別の[寮]{りょう}の友だちが、ボイスメッセージを送ってくれました。「水が来るよ、学校に行って」って。インドネシア語で。","en":"Thanks to a friend. A friend in another dormitory sent us a voice message: \"The water's coming, go to the school.\" In Indonesian.","gl":"ボイスメッセージ: a voice message.","tag":"grateful","ref":"E9·L32"},
{"t":"narr","text":"メッセージが来たとき、[寮]{りょう}の前の[段]{だん}まで、もう水が来ていた。六人は、前の人のそでを持って、[一列]{いちれつ}で[坂]{さか}を[上]{のぼ}った。足もとの道は、見えなかった。","en":"By the time that message came, the water had already reached the dormitory step. The six of them walked up the hill in a line, each holding the sleeve of the person in front. They couldn't see the road under their feet.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"dewi","mood":"think","ja":"もっと早く、分かる[言葉]{ことば}で知らせてほしかったです。","en":"I wish they had told us sooner, in words we could understand.","tag":"quiet, hurt","ref":"E9·L33"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"…そうですね。読めなかったのは、デウィさんたちのせいじゃありません。知らせ[方]{かた}のせいです。","en":"...Yes. It isn't your fault that you couldn't read it. The problem is how the warning was sent.","gl":"知らせ方 (しらせかた): the way of telling people.","tag":"gentle, firm","ref":"E9·L34"},
{"t":"narr","text":"これは、チェスカが大学で研究していることだ。でも今夜は、メモはとらない。[毛布]{もうふ}を六[枚]{まい}、[取]{と}りに行った。","en":"This is exactly what Cheska studies at the university. But tonight she doesn't take notes. She goes to get six blankets.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"dewi","mood":"think","ja":"[寮]{りょう}は[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}でしょうか。","en":"Do you think the dormitory will be all right?","tag":"worried, quietly","ref":"E9·L35"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"sleepy","ja":"分かりません。朝まで、だれにも分からないと思います。うちも同じです。","en":"I don't know. I don't think anyone will know until morning. It's the same for our house.","tag":"tired, honest","ref":"E9·L36"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[夜中]{よなか}の二時。[正一]{しょういち}さんは、かべにもたれて、すわったままねむっている。四十年、フェリーの[機関室]{きかんしつ}で[働]{はたら}いていたころからのくせだ。[文子]{ふみこ}さんは、となりで起きている。ひざの上に、手紙のかんがある。まりやが、となりのトビーに小さい声で言った。","en":"2 a.m. Shōichi-san is asleep sitting up, leaning against the wall. It is a habit from his forty years in the engine room of the harbor ferry. Fumiko-san is awake beside him, with the tin of letters in her lap. Mariya speaks quietly to Toby, next to her.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"sleepy","ja":"[島]{しま}は[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}だって。お母さんから。","en":"Mom says the island's fine.","gl":"島 (しま): an island. ～だって: \"I hear ～\", \"they say ～\" (casual).","tag":"whispering, relieved","ref":"E9·L37"},
{"t":"narr","text":"チェスカのスマホが、ぽっと[光]{ひか}った。","en":"Cheska's phone lights up.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"hello","ja":"起きてる？水は店の前の[段]{だん}で止まったよ。中には入ってない。","en":"You awake? The water's stopped at the step in front of the shop. It hasn't come in.","gl":"段 (だん): a step.","tag":"softly, relieved","ref":"E9·L38"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"yay","ja":"写真を送るね。[段]{だん}の上に、だれがいると思う？","en":"I'm sending a photo. Guess who's on the step?","tag":"playful, conspiratorial","ref":"E9·L39"},
{"t":"narr","text":"写真が来た。[屋根]{やね}の下のつばめ[通]{どお}りは、茶色い水でいっぱいだ。その上の、たった一つかわいた段に、白と黒のねこがすわっている。とても、めいわくそうな[顔]{かお}だ。","en":"The photo arrives. Under the roof, Tsubame Street is full of brown water. Above it, on the one dry step, sits a black-and-white cat. She looks very annoyed about the whole thing.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"cat","pose":"worried","alt":"The cat on the dry step, looking sideways at the water, annoyed"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"yay","ja":"…ミンミン！","en":"...Mingming!","tag":"delighted, holding back a laugh","ref":"E9·L40"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"sleepy","ja":"おばあちゃんは「うちのまっちゃ」って言ってるけどね。","en":"But Grandma calls her \"our Matcha.\"","tag":"amused, fond","ref":"E9·L41"},
{"t":"narr","text":"あおいも「まっちゃ」とよんでいることは、メッセージには書いていない。","en":"Aoi doesn't write that she calls the cat Matcha too.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"チェスカのとなりで、正一さんが、目をとじたまま言った。","en":"Next to Cheska, Shōichi-san speaks without opening his eyes.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"sleepy","ja":"…ねこは、高い所を知っとる。","en":"...Cats know where the high ground is.","gl":"知っとる (しっとる): 知っている, in the local dialect.","tag":"sleepy mumble","ref":"E9·L42"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"think","ja":"そこから、[家]{いえ}の[方]{ほう}は見える？","en":"Can you see toward the house from there?","tag":"whispering, worried","ref":"E9·L43"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"oops","ja":"見えない。そっちの道は、[全部]{ぜんぶ}水の下。電気はついてるのに。","en":"No. The lights are on, but the road that way is all under water.","gl":"全部 (ぜんぶ): all of it.","tag":"whispering, uneasy","ref":"E9·L44"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"…ポンプは動いているはず。雨も、もうすぐ[止]{や}むはず。","en":"...The pumps should be running. And the rain should stop soon.","gl":"止む (やむ): to stop, of rain or snow. Same kanji as 止まる, different verb.","tag":"quietly, trying to believe it","ref":"E9·L45"},
{"t":"note","text":"はず is for things you have good reason to expect but no way to check. つばめ通りは少し高いはず. ポンプは動いているはず. On a night like this, people use はず a lot, because nobody can be sure about the next few hours."},
{"t":"narr","text":"チェスカは、スマホの[画面]{がめん}を上にして、マットに[置]{お}いた。すぐ見えるように。[横]{よこ}にはならない。体育館のすみで、デウィがだれかに、小さい声でメッセージを[録音]{ろくおん}している。雨はまだふっている。でも、さっきより[弱]{よわ}い。かもめ荘のろうかに、今、どのくらい水があるのか。ここにいるだれにも分からない。朝になれば、分かる。","en":"Cheska lays her phone on the mat, screen up, where she can see it right away. She doesn't lie down. In a corner of the gym, Dewi is quietly recording a message for someone. It is still raining, but less than before. How much water is in the hall of Kamome House right now? Nobody here knows. They will know in the morning.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u9-x1","type":"mcq","q":"The first alert says 【[警戒]{けいかい}レベル3】[高齢者]{こうれいしゃ}[等]{とう}[避難]{ひなん}. What is it asking people in the old town to do?","options":[{"t":"Older people, and anyone else who needs extra time, should evacuate now; everyone else should get ready","why":"Right. [高齢者]{こうれいしゃ} is older people, and [等]{とう} adds *and others*. At Kamome House that means the Satōs, as Fumiko-san points out herself. The others could wait, but they choose to go now.","ok":true},
{"t":"Everyone should wait indoors for Level 5","why":"Level 5 is not a signal to leave. It means the disaster is already happening, so the aim is to be somewhere safe before then."},
{"t":"Only people over seventy-five need to do anything","why":"The alert gives no age, and [等]{とう} widens it to anyone who needs time: small children, people who are ill, people who walk slowly. Everyone else is told to get ready."},
{"t":"Everyone must leave the old town at once","why":"That is Level 4, [避難指示]{ひなんしじ}, which arrives at 9:30 p.m. Level 3 starts with the people who need the most time."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u9-x2","type":"mcq","q":"Dewi says [寮]{りょう}には、会社の人が知らせることになっています. What does ことになっています tell you?","options":[{"t":"It is the arrangement: someone from the company is supposed to tell the dormitory","why":"Right. ～ことになっている describes a rule or an arrangement that somebody else has made. Tonight the arrangement existed, but nobody was there to carry it out.","ok":true},
{"t":"Dewi has decided to tell the dormitory herself","why":"Your own decision is ～ことにする, as in Aoi's おばあちゃんの[所]{ところ}に行くことにする. ことになっている is a decision made for you."},
{"t":"Someone from the company told the dormitory tonight: She goes on","why":"でも、今日は工場が休みで、だれも来ませんでした. The rule says someone should; tonight nobody did."},
{"t":"The company will tell the dormitory from now on: That would be a new decision","why":"知らせることになりました. ～ことになっています describes how things already stand."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u9-x3","type":"mcq","q":"Cheska says 出るのは、早ければ早いほどいいです. What does she mean?","options":[{"t":"The earlier they leave, the better","why":"Right. ～ば～ほど means \"the more ～, the more ～.\" 早ければ早いほど: the earlier, the better.","ok":true},
{"t":"They should leave only if it is early","why":"\"Only if\" would be 早ければ alone, or ～ときだけ. The repeated 早い is the clue."},
{"t":"If they leave early, everything will be fine","why":"That would be 早く出れば大丈夫です. ～ば～ほど compares degrees: the earlier, the better."},
{"t":"It doesn't matter when they leave","why":"That is the opposite of her point. She wants them out now."}]}},
{"t":"lang","items":["Who decided? 行くことにしました (Fumiko-san), おばあちゃんの[所]{ところ}に行くことにする (Aoi) and トビーとは私が歩くことにするね (Mariya) are the speaker's own decisions. 会社の人が知らせることになっています is an arrangement somebody else made, and Dewi can only report it.","An opinion and a wish: 今出た方がいいと思います says what Cheska thinks is best. みんなに[決]{き}めてほしいです and 学校に行ってほしい say what she wants other people to do. ～てほしい is a wish, not an order, which is why Aoi can answer 分かってる and still go to her grandmother's.","Credit and blame: 友だちのおかげです gives a friend the credit for a good result. デウィさんたちのせいじゃありません。知らせ[方]{かた}のせいです moves the blame off the people and onto the way the warning was sent."]},
{"t":"reflect","q":"Cheska says what she thinks the house should do, and then says みんなに[決]{き}めてほしいです. When you are the person in the room who knows the most, how do you decide what to leave to everyone else?"}]},{"unit":"e3u10","n":10,"title":"After the water","month":"September–November","level":"N3","enDefault":false,"parts":[{"t":"narr","text":"雨の夜、あおいは、おばあちゃんの千代さんと、店の二階にいた。かもめ荘のほかのみんなは、早めに学校の[体育館]{たいいくかん}へひなんした。デウィの[寮]{りょう}には、だれも読めない[警報]{けいほう}が[届]{とど}いた。水は、千代さんの店の[段]{だん}で止まった。かもめ荘がどうなったかは、朝まで分からなかった。","en":"On the night of the rain, Aoi stayed upstairs at the tea shop with her grandmother, Chiyo. Everyone else at Kamome House evacuated early to the school gym. Dewi's dormitory got an alert that nobody there could read. The water stopped at the step of Chiyo's shop. Nobody knew what had happened to Kamome House until morning.","recap":true,"lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"朝、みんなが家に帰ると、ねこが[玄関]{げんかん}の前で待っていた。ドアを開けると、だれよりも先に中に入って、[階段]{かいだん}の[四段目]{よんだんめ}にすわった。それより下には、[下]{お}りて来ない。","en":"In the morning, when everyone comes home, the cat is waiting at the front door. As soon as they open it, she walks in ahead of everyone and sits on the fourth stair. She won't come down any further.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"cat","pose":"worried","alt":"The black-and-white cat on the fourth stair, looking sideways at the wet hallway"},
{"t":"narr","text":"水は、一階の[床]{ゆか}の上、十二センチまで来て、もう[引]{ひ}いていた。ろうかのかべに、茶色い[線]{せん}が[残]{のこ}っている。その上のバロメーターは、ぬれていなかった。一階のチェスカ、ロドリゴ、まりやの部屋のふとんと、[居間]{いま}のたたみは、ぜんぶ道に出された。","en":"The water had come up twelve centimeters over the downstairs floor and had already gone down again. It left a brown line on the hallway walls. The barometer above the line was dry. The futons from the three downstairs rooms (Cheska's, Rodrigo's and Mariya's) and the tatami mats from the living-room corner all went out to the curb.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"それから三週間、チェスカが[写真]{しゃしん}とリストと[当番表]{とうばんひょう}を作って、そうじを進めた。まりやのお母さんは、島からフェリーで、新しいふとんを送ってくれた。ふとんの中には、[干物]{ひもの}が十二まい入っていた。文子さんと正一さんの[息子]{むすこ}の[浩之]{ひろゆき}さんは、大阪から毎晩電話をかけてくるようになった。文子さんは、毎晩「[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}」と答えた。そして、家がかわいたとき、チェスカのする仕事は、何もなくなった。","en":"For the next three weeks, Cheska ran the cleanup with photos, lists and a schedule. Mariya's mother sent her a new futon on the ferry from the island, with twelve dried fish rolled up inside it. Hiroyuki, the Satōs' son, started calling from Osaka every night, and every night Fumiko-san told him 大丈夫, \"We're fine.\" Then the house was dry, and there was nothing left for Cheska to do.","gl":"干物 (ひもの): dried fish.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"十月のなかば。[水害]{すいがい}のあと、多くの[手続]{てつづ}きは、市の「[罹災]{りさい}[証明書]{しょうめいしょ}」から始まる。文子さんにたのまれて、あおいとチェスカが[市役所]{しやくしょ}へ[申請]{しんせい}に来た。あおいは、文子さんが書いた[委任状]{いにんじょう}を持っている。[防災課]{ぼうさいか}のまどぐちにいるのは、あの夜、体育館でリストを持っていた[松本]{まつもと}さんだ。あれから、家に帰っていないような顔をしている。","en":"Mid-October. After a flood, much of the paperwork starts with the city's certificate of disaster damage. Fumiko-san has asked Aoi and Cheska to go to the city office and apply for one. Aoi is carrying a letter from Fumiko-san that lets them apply for her. At the disaster-prevention counter sits Mr. Matsumoto, the man who held the list at the gym that night. He looks as if he hasn't been home since.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"matsumoto","mood":"hello","ja":"[四十七番]{よんじゅうななばん}の[方]{かた}、お[待]{ま}たせいたしました。[防災課]{ぼうさいか}の[松本]{まつもと}でございます。","en":"Number 47, thank you for waiting. I'm Matsumoto, from the disaster-prevention section.","gl":"お待たせいたしました: \"thank you for waiting,\" very politely. でございます: the very polite です.","tag":"tired, very polite","ref":"E10·L1"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"hello","ja":"[罹災証明書]{りさいしょうめいしょ}の[申請]{しんせい}に[参]{まい}りました。[大家]{おおや}の[佐藤]{さとう}さんの[代理]{だいり}です。こちらが[委任状]{いにんじょう}です。","en":"We've come to apply for a certificate of disaster damage. We're here on behalf of our landlady, Mrs. Satō. This is her letter of authorization.","gl":"罹災証明書 (りさいしょうめいしょ): the city's certificate that a home was damaged in a disaster. 申請 (しんせい): an application. 参る (まいる): the humble \"come\". 代理 (だいり): someone acting for another person. 委任状 (いにんじょう): a letter that lets someone act for you.","tag":"polished, formal","ref":"E10·L2"},
{"t":"line","who":"matsumoto","mood":"tip","ja":"かしこまりました。[被害]{ひがい}の分かるお[写真]{しゃしん}は、お[持]{も}ちでしょうか。","en":"Certainly. Do you have photos that show the damage?","gl":"被害 (ひがい): damage. お持ちでしょうか: the respectful \"do you have?\"","tag":"polite, businesslike","ref":"E10·L3"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"はい。そうじの前に、とりました。水は、ここまで来ました。十二センチです。","en":"Yes. I took them before we cleaned. The water came up to here. Twelve centimeters.","tag":"calm, efficient","ref":"E10·L4"},
{"t":"narr","text":"チェスカの日本語は、あおいの[敬語]{けいご}より、ずっとかんたんだ。でも、写真は一まいずつ、[日付]{ひづけ}と[場所]{ばしょ}の[順]{じゅん}にならんでいる。「先に写真、そうじはそのあと」。チェスカは、フィリピンで、この言葉を何百人もの人に教えてきた。","en":"Cheska's Japanese is much simpler than Aoi's keigo. But her photos are in order, one by one, by date and by place. \"Photos first, cleaning second\": Cheska taught that rule to hundreds of people back in the Philippines.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"matsumoto","mood":"hello","ja":"[大変]{たいへん}[助]{たす}かります。[調査]{ちょうさ}に[伺]{うかが}うのは、[三週間]{さんしゅうかん}ほど[先]{さき}になりますが、よろしいでしょうか。","en":"That's a great help. It will be about three weeks before we can come and inspect. Would that be all right?","gl":"調査 (ちょうさ): an inspection. 伺う (うかがう): the humble \"visit\". ～ほど: about ～.","tag":"relieved, polite","ref":"E10·L5"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"think","ja":"…はい。[松本]{まつもと}さん、一つ、[聞]{き}いてもいいですか。あの夜の[避難情報]{ひなんじょうほう}は、日本語だけでしたね。","en":"...Yes. Mr. Matsumoto, may I ask one thing? The evacuation alerts that night were only in Japanese, weren't they?","gl":"避難情報 (ひなんじょうほう): evacuation information.","tag":"careful, steady","ref":"E10·L6"},
{"t":"line","who":"matsumoto","mood":"oops","ja":"はい。[決]{き}まりの[通]{とお}りに、お[送]{おく}りいたしました。","en":"Yes. We sent them as the rules say.","gl":"決まり (きまり): a rule. お送りいたしました: the humble \"sent\".","tag":"uncomfortable","ref":"E10·L7"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"送っても、読めなければ、[届]{とど}いたわけではありません。魚の工場の[寮]{りょう}では、「[避難]{ひなん}」の字を、だれも読めませんでした。","en":"Even if you send them, if people can't read them, they haven't really arrived. At the dormitory at the seafood plant, nobody could read the characters for \"evacuate.\"","gl":"届く (とどく): to arrive, to reach someone. ～わけではない: it doesn't mean that ～.","tag":"quiet, firm","ref":"E10·L8"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"oops","ja":"[申]{もう}し[訳]{わけ}ございません。[松本]{まつもと}さんを[責]{せ}めているわけではないんです。","en":"I'm very sorry. We're not blaming you, Mr. Matsumoto.","gl":"申し訳ございません: the most polite \"I'm sorry\". 責める (せめる): to blame.","tag":"hurried, apologetic","ref":"E10·L9"},
{"t":"line","who":"matsumoto","mood":"think","ja":"…いいえ、おっしゃる[通]{とお}りです。[水産]{すいさん}工場の[寮]{りょう}のことは、私も聞いております。[実]{じつ}は、その[件]{けん}で、大学の[先生方]{せんせいがた}にご[相談]{そうだん}しようと[考]{かんが}えております。","en":"...No, you're right. I heard about the dormitory at the seafood plant, too. As a matter of fact, we're planning to ask some professors at the university for advice on exactly that.","gl":"おっしゃる: the respectful \"say\". 実は (じつは): as a matter of fact. 件 (けん): a matter. ご相談する: the humble \"consult\".","tag":"sighs, honest","ref":"E10·L10"},
{"t":"narr","text":"松本さんが言う「先生方」は、二人いる。チェスカとあおいの先生で、[防災]{ぼうさい}ガバナンス（だれが、どうやって防災のことを決めるか）を教えている[大西]{おおにし}先生。それから、イエンの先生で、[情報]{じょうほう}科学のアモアコ先生だ。アモアコ先生はガーナ[出身]{しゅっしん}で、日本に来て二十年になる。[汐浦]{しおうら}の[方言]{ほうげん}が話せて、だじゃれが大好きだ。","en":"Mr. Matsumoto means two professors. One is Prof. Ōnishi, Cheska and Aoi's supervisor, who teaches disaster governance: how governments and communities make decisions about disasters. The other is Dr. Amoako, Yến's supervisor, who teaches information science. Dr. Amoako is from Ghana and has lived in Japan for twenty years. He speaks the Shioura dialect and loves terrible puns.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"外に出ると、あおいはバス[停]{てい}のベンチにすわった。チェスカも、となりにすわった。","en":"Outside, Aoi sits down on the bench at the bus stop, and Cheska sits down next to her.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"think","ja":"さっきのチェスカ、ちょっとこわかったよ。ていねいなのに。","en":"You were kind of scary in there. Even though you were so polite.","tag":"teasing, a little impressed","ref":"E10·L11"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"sleepy","ja":"ごめん。[最近]{さいきん}、ちょっと[寝不足]{ねぶそく}なだけ。[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}。","en":"Sorry. I haven't been sleeping much lately, that's all. I'm fine.","gl":"寝不足 (ねぶそく): not getting enough sleep.","tag":"tired, brushing it off","ref":"E10·L12"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"sleepy","ja":"まだ何も聞いてないけど。","en":"I haven't asked you anything yet.","tag":"dry","ref":"E10·L13"},
{"t":"narr","text":"バスが来て、そのまま行ってしまった。","en":"A bus comes and goes.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"think","ja":"…じゃあ、私が先に言うね。「おばあちゃんのために[汐浦]{しおうら}に来た」って、みんなに言ってるでしょ。あれは、[半分]{はんぶん}だけ。東京の[大学院]{だいがくいん}に[落]{お}ちたの。","en":"...OK, I'll go first. You know how I tell everyone I came to Shioura for my grandmother? That's only half of it. I failed the exam for graduate school in Tokyo.","gl":"半分 (はんぶん): half. 大学院 (だいがくいん): graduate school. 落ちる (おちる): to fall; here, to fail an exam.","tag":"hesitant, then deciding","ref":"E10·L14"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"[知]{し}ってた。","en":"I knew.","tag":"matter-of-fact","ref":"E10·L15"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"oops","ja":"え、いつから？","en":"What? Since when?","tag":"startled","ref":"E10·L16"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"四月から。部屋のダンボール、まだ開けてないでしょ。","en":"Since April. You still haven't unpacked your boxes.","tag":"a small smile","ref":"E10·L17"},
{"t":"narr","text":"あおいは、何も言えない。本当のことだ。","en":"Aoi can't argue with that. It's true.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"hello","ja":"でも、あの夜、あおいは[電話]{でんわ}を[三回]{さんかい}かけて、雨の中を行ったでしょ。あれは、[半分]{はんぶん}じゃなかったよ。","en":"But that night, you called three times, and then you went out into that rain. There was nothing half about that.","tag":"warm, sincere","ref":"E10·L18"},
{"t":"narr","text":"あおいは、自分の[秘密]{ひみつ}を先に話した。チェスカは、今日は自分の話をしない。でも、帰りのバスでは、二人はとなりにすわった。","en":"Aoi has told her secret first. Cheska doesn't tell hers, not today. But on the bus home, they sit together.","gl":"秘密 (ひみつ): a secret.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"十月の終わり。朝の四時、チェスカは台所のテーブルで、[雨雲]{あまぐも}レーダーを見ている。外の空は、[晴]{は}れている。だれかが[作業]{さぎょう}ぐつで、ろうかをしずかに歩こうとしている。ロドリゴだ。でも、ロドリゴは、しずかに歩くのが[苦手]{にがて}だ。","en":"The end of October. At four in the morning, Cheska is at the kitchen table, watching the rain radar under a clear sky. Someone comes down the hallway in work boots, trying to be quiet. It is Rodrigo, and quiet has never been his strength.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"think","ja":"ロドリゴ？こんな時間に、どこに行くの？","en":"Rodrigo? Where are you going at this hour?","tag":"suspicious","ref":"E10·L19"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"oops","ja":"…[仕事]{しごと}だ。つばめ[通]{どお}りの[裏]{うら}の[倉庫]{そうこ}を[片付]{かたづ}ける。朝までで[一万円]{いちまんえん}、[現金]{げんきん}で。","en":"...Work. Clearing out a warehouse behind Tsubame Street. Ten thousand yen until morning, in cash.","gl":"裏 (うら): the back. 倉庫 (そうこ): a warehouse. 現金 (げんきん): cash.","tag":"caught, whispering","ref":"E10·L20"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"[今週]{こんしゅう}は、もう[工場]{こうじょう}で[二十八時間]{にじゅうはちじかん}[働]{はたら}いたでしょ。[留学生]{りゅうがくせい}は、[週]{しゅう}に二十八時間までだよ。","en":"You've already worked twenty-eight hours at the plant this week. International students can only work twenty-eight hours a week.","gl":"留学生 (りゅうがくせい): an international student.","tag":"firm","ref":"E10·L21"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"think","ja":"[書類]{しょるい}のない[仕事]{しごと}だ。だれにも分からない。","en":"There's no paperwork for this job. Nobody will know.","gl":"書類 (しょるい): paperwork, documents.","tag":"defensive","ref":"E10·L22"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"だれにも分からなくても、ルールは同じ。それに、朝まで[働]{はたら}いたら、[学校]{がっこう}に行けないでしょ。[出席]{しゅっせき}が[足]{た}りないと、ビザの[更新]{こうしん}ができなくなるかもしれないよ。一万円のために、日本のスタジオで働くチャンスをなくしてもいいの？","en":"Even if nobody knows, the rule is the same. And if you work all night, you can't go to school in the morning. If your attendance drops, you might not be able to renew your visa. Are you going to lose your chance at a Japanese studio for ten thousand yen?","gl":"出席 (しゅっせき): attendance. 更新 (こうしん): renewal.","tag":"calm, serious","ref":"E10·L23"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"oops","ja":"…[金]{かね}がないんだ。ふとんも買えない。","en":"...I have no money. I can't even buy a futon.","gl":"金 (かね): money (a rough word).","tag":"quiet, ashamed","ref":"E10·L24"},
{"t":"narr","text":"ロドリゴのふとんは、水害で道に出された。それから五週間、ロドリゴはざぶとん三まいの上でねている。みんなには、「サムライは、こうやってねるんだ」と言っていた。","en":"Rodrigo's futon went out to the curb after the flood. For five weeks, he has slept on three floor cushions, and he has told everyone that this is how a samurai sleeps.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"think","ja":"どうして言わなかったの？","en":"Why didn't you tell anyone?","tag":"softer","ref":"E10·L25"},
{"t":"line","who":"rodrigo","mood":"tip","ja":"チェスカだって言わないじゃないか。雨がふっていなくても、[毎晩]{まいばん}、雨のレーダーを見ているのに。","en":"You don't tell anyone either. You check the rain radar every night, even when it isn't raining.","gl":"～だって: ～ too. ～じゃないか: \"don't you?\", pushing back.","tag":"pushing back gently","ref":"E10·L26"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"sleepy","ja":"…私は[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}。","en":"...I'm fine.","tag":"pause, quietly","ref":"E10·L27"},
{"t":"narr","text":"二人とも、気づかれたくなかった。でも、二人とも、気づかれていた。ロドリゴは作業ぐつをぬいで、ホットチョコレートを作った。チェスカも、二はい飲んだ。朝ごはんのころ、102号室のドアに、一まいの紙がはってあった。市の「水害にあった人へのお[見舞金]{みまいきん}」の申しこみ[用紙]{ようし}だ。ロドリゴがまちがえそうな所には、えんぴつでしるしがついている。","en":"Neither of them wanted to be noticed, and both of them were. Rodrigo takes off his work boots and makes hot chocolate instead. Cheska drinks two cups. By breakfast, a form is taped to the door of Room 102: the city's application for support money for people hit by the flood. Every box Rodrigo might get wrong is marked in pencil.","gl":"お見舞金 (おみまいきん): money given to help someone after an accident or a disaster.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"十一月。水害のあと、はじめての大雨の夜。夜中の一時に、あおいが水を飲みに下りて来ると、チェスカが階段の一番下にすわっていた。[服]{ふく}を着て、家の中なのにくつまではいて、となりには[荷物]{にもつ}をつめたかばんがある。","en":"November brings the first heavy rain since the flood. At one in the morning, Aoi comes down for a glass of water and finds Cheska sitting on the bottom stair. She is dressed, with her shoes on indoors, and a packed bag beside her.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"think","ja":"雨の音がするたびに、[目]{め}が[覚]{さ}めるの。[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}なわけじゃない。でも、だめなわけでもないの。ただ、[眠]{ねむ}れないだけ。","en":"Every time I hear rain, I wake up. It's not that I'm fine. But it's not that I'm falling apart, either. I just can't sleep.","gl":"～たびに: every time ～. 目が覚める (めがさめる): to wake up. 眠る (ねむる): to sleep.","tag":"tired, small voice","ref":"E10·L28"},
{"t":"note","text":"「大丈夫じゃない」と言うと、大きな[問題]{もんだい}に聞こえます。「大丈夫なわけじゃない」は、もっと小さくて、[正確]{せいかく}です。「だから大丈夫だ」という考えだけを、[打]{う}ち[消]{け}します。チェスカは、この秋、もう二回「大丈夫」と言いました。「大丈夫」は、[学習者]{がくしゅうしゃ}が最初に[覚]{おぼ}える言葉の一つです。そして、一番[信]{しん}じてはいけない言葉の一つです。","en":"大丈夫じゃない would sound like an alarm. 大丈夫なわけじゃない is smaller and more exact. It only takes back one idea: \"so I must be fine.\" Cheska has already said 大丈夫 twice this fall. It is often the first word learners pick up for \"I'm OK,\" and one of the words you should be most careful about believing.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"チェスカの家に水が入ったことは、前にも一度ある。十代のころ、フィリピンで。長い話だ。あおいは、今夜はそれを聞かない。ただ、となりにすわった。","en":"Water came into Cheska's home once before, in the Philippines, when she was a teenager. It is a long story, and Aoi doesn't ask for it tonight. She just sits down next to her.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"tip","ja":"[一人]{ひとり}で[起]{お}きていることはないよ。雨の夜は、だれかがいっしょに起きていればいいでしょ。","en":"There's no need to sit up on your own. On rainy nights, someone can just sit up with you.","gl":"～ことはない: there is no need to ～.","tag":"gently","ref":"E10·L29"},
{"t":"narr","text":"その[週末]{しゅうまつ}、家のアプリに、新しい[行]{ぎょう}がふえた。「雨の夜」。かいとが作って、イエンが四分でレビューした。次の雨の夜、かいとは、[勉強]{べんきょう}しているふりをして、居間で起きていた。チェスカは、一九九八年のホラー[映画]{えいが}をつけた。","en":"That weekend, the house app gets a new row: 雨の夜, \"rainy nights.\" Kaito built it, and Yến reviewed it in four minutes. On the next rainy night, Kaito stays up in the living room, pretending to study. Cheska puts on a horror movie from 1998.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"sleepy","ja":"この[映画]{えいが}、[犯人]{はんにん}、[最初]{さいしょ}から分かるよ。あの[男]{おとこ}だよ。","en":"You can tell who did it from the start. It's that guy.","gl":"犯人 (はんにん): the person who did the crime.","tag":"confident, bored","ref":"E10·L30"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"yay","ja":"ちがうよ。見てて。","en":"No, it isn't. Just watch.","tag":"delighted","ref":"E10·L31"},
{"t":"narr","text":"かいとの[予想]{よそう}は、[大]{おお}はずれだった。最後の十分、かいとはクッションをだいて、ずっと「うそだろ」と言っていた。チェスカは、その夜、六時間ねむった。ねこは、チェスカのかばんの上でねた。","en":"Kaito's guess turns out to be completely wrong. For the last ten minutes, he hugs a cushion and keeps saying \"No way.\" That night, Cheska sleeps for six hours. The cat sleeps on her packed bag.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"cat","pose":"sleepy","alt":"The cat curled up asleep on Cheska's packed bag"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"市の[資料館]{しりょうかん}の[地下]{ちか}も、水につかった。ぬれた古い書類を、一まいずつかわかす。キッチンペーパーをページの間にはさんで、せんぷうきをかける。この作業を、「[資料]{しりょう}レスキュー」という。日曜日の夕食で文子さんが話したので、かもめ荘のみんなが手伝いに来た。古い字が読めるトビーは、だれもさわりたがらない[台帳]{だいちょう}を[担当]{たんとう}している。","en":"The basement of the city archive flooded too. The wet old papers have to be dried one sheet at a time, with kitchen paper between the pages and fans blowing on them. This work is called 資料レスキュー, document rescue. Fumiko-san mentioned it at Sunday dinner, so the whole house has come to help. Toby can read old handwriting, so he has the ledger that nobody else wants to touch.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"plates","title":"The ledger","hint":"Read each line of the page, then tap it to check.","items":[{"ja":"住居表示 新旧対照表","ro":"じゅうきょひょうじ しんきゅうたいしょうひょう","who":"*Addresses, old and new, side by side.* 住居表示 is the modern way of numbering addresses. Many Japanese cities changed to it in the 1960s, one district at a time, and kept a list like this so that an old address could still be traced."},{"ja":"昭和四十三年 四月一日 実施","ro":"しょうわ よんじゅうさんねん しがつ ついたち じっし","who":"*In effect from April 1, Shōwa 43.* 昭和 is the name of the era, and its forty-third year is 1968. 実施 (じっし) means putting something into effect."},{"ja":"旧：川南 一二六番地","ro":"きゅう：かわみなみ ひゃくにじゅうろく ばんち","who":"*Old: lot 126, Kawaminami.* 旧 marks what something used to be, as in 旧市街, the old town."},{"ja":"新：川南町二丁目 四番九号","ro":"しん：かわみなみちょう にちょうめ よんばん きゅうごう","who":"*New: 4-9, Kawaminami-chō 2-chōme.* From that day, 126 Kawaminami was no longer anyone's address."},{"ja":"世帯主：村井 （転居）","ro":"せたいぬし：むらい （てんきょ）","who":"*Head of household: Murai.* Next to the name, in a clerk's pencil: 転居, *moved within the city*."}]},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"think","ja":"「[川南]{かわみなみ}、[一二六番地]{ひゃくにじゅうろくばんち}」…。あおい、この[住所]{じゅうしょ}、どこかで見なかったっけ？","en":"\"Kawaminami, lot 126\"... Aoi, haven't we seen this address somewhere?","gl":"番地 (ばんち): a lot number in an address. ～っけ: said when you are trying to remember.","tag":"slowly, puzzled","ref":"E10·L32"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"yay","ja":"見た。[物置]{ものおき}で見つけたかんの[手紙]{てがみ}。[全部]{ぜんぶ}、この[住所]{じゅうしょ}だった。","en":"We did. The letters in the tin we found in the storeroom. Every one had this address.","tag":"excited, whispering","ref":"E10·L33"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"think","ja":"え、それ、さとうさんの手紙？","en":"Wait, you mean Mrs. Satō's letters?","tag":"surprised","ref":"E10·L34"},
{"t":"narr","text":"文子さんが、となりのテーブルから来て、めがねをかけた。","en":"Fumiko-san comes over from the next table and puts on her glasses.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"think","ja":"[村井]{むらい}は、私の[結婚]{けっこん}する前の名前です。…父ですね。","en":"Murai was my name before I married. ...That's my father.","gl":"結婚する (けっこんする): to get married.","tag":"quietly, reading","ref":"E10·L35"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"この年の[春]{はる}に、うちは町の[反対側]{はんたいがわ}に[引]{ひ}っ[越]{こ}したんです。同じ春に、[住所]{じゅうしょ}の書き方まで[変]{か}わったんですね。","en":"That spring, my family moved to the other side of town. And that same spring, the way addresses were written changed too.","gl":"反対側 (はんたいがわ): the other side. 引っ越す (ひっこす): to move to a new home.","tag":"thoughtful","ref":"E10·L36"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"think","ja":"四月からは、「[川南]{かわみなみ}[一二六]{ひゃくにじゅうろく}」に手紙を出しても、[届]{とど}かなかったでしょうね。新しい[住所]{じゅうしょ}は、手紙で知らせたはずなんですけど。父は、[郵便局]{ゆうびんきょく}に[転居届]{てんきょとどけ}を出すのを、忘れていたのかもしれません。","en":"From that April, a letter mailed to \"126 Kawaminami\" wouldn't have arrived, I suppose. I'm sure I wrote and told her my new address, though. Maybe my father forgot to tell the post office we'd moved.","tag":"slowly, piecing it together","ref":"E10·L37"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"sleepy","ja":"手紙というのは、[住所]{じゅうしょ}がちがうと、どんなに[待]{ま}っても[届]{とど}かないものですから。","en":"With the wrong address, a letter never arrives, however long you wait. That's how letters are.","gl":"どんなに～ても: however much ～. ～ものだ: that is how things are.","tag":"softly","ref":"E10·L38"},
{"t":"narr","text":"文子さんは、五十年[以上]{いじょう}、待っていたのだ。ぬれたページの下に、かわいた紙をしいて、手でそっとのばした。そして、自分のテーブルに[戻]{もど}った。あおいは、そのページの写真をとった。","en":"Fumiko-san has been waiting for more than fifty years. She slips a dry sheet under the wet page, smooths it flat with her hand, and goes back to her own table. Aoi takes a photo of the page.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"その日の夕方、文子さんは、資料館の階段の下で、まりやを見つけた。まりやは、スーツを着ている。","en":"That evening, Fumiko-san finds Mariya at the bottom of the archive stairs. Mariya is wearing a suit.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"oops","ja":"[来週]{らいしゅう}、[留学]{りゅうがく}の[面接]{めんせつ}を[受]{う}けるんです。今日は、大学で面接の[練習]{れんしゅう}をしてきたんです。[島]{しま}を出たいわけじゃないんです。でも、行ってみたいんです。","en":"Next week I have an interview for studying abroad. I had a practice interview at the university today. It's not that I want to leave the island. But I'd like to give it a try.","gl":"留学 (りゅうがく): studying abroad. 面接 (めんせつ): an interview. 練習 (れんしゅう): practice.","tag":"nervous laugh","ref":"E10·L39"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"行ってみなければ、分からないこともありますよ。","en":"Some things you can't know until you go.","tag":"warmly","ref":"E10·L40"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"十一月には、ほかにもいろいろなことがあった。","en":"Other things happened in November too.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"市は、アモアコ先生の[研究室]{けんきゅうしつ}に、警報をいろいろな言葉で出すページをたのんだ。イエンは、一週間で、六つの言葉のページを作った。そして、大学の小さい会議室で、デウィに見せた。","en":"The city asked Dr. Amoako's lab for a web page that gives its alerts in many languages. In one week, Yến built a page in six languages. Then she showed it to Dewi in a small meeting room at the university.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"dewi","mood":"think","ja":"きれいなページですね。でも…[寮]{りょう}のみんなは、字より声です。[暗]{くら}い中で、長いページは読みません。","en":"It's a nice page. But... at the dormitory, people use voice, not text. They won't read a long page in the dark.","tag":"polite, honest","ref":"E10·L41"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"think","ja":"…分かりました。[最初]{さいしょ}から、作り[直]{なお}します。","en":"...I understand. I'll start again from the beginning.","tag":"pause, accepting","ref":"E10·L42"},
{"t":"narr","text":"一週間後、新しいページは、六つの言葉で、警報を声で読むようになった。アモアコ先生は、六つ全部聞いた。","en":"A week later, the new page reads the alerts aloud in six languages. Dr. Amoako listens to all six.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"amoako","mood":"yay","ja":"イエンさんのページは、何も[言]{い}えん。…イエンだけに！","en":"Yến-san's page leaves me speechless. ...Get it? Yến!","gl":"言えん (いえん): 言えない, \"can't say,\" in the local dialect. It sounds just like Yến's name.","tag":"jolly, local dialect","ref":"E10·L43"},
{"t":"narr","text":"イエンは、[三秒]{さんびょう}考えて、笑った。デウィは、笑うまでに十秒かかった。","en":"Yến needs three seconds before she laughs. Dewi needs ten.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"その夜、かいとは、イエンの新しいコードを読んだ。","en":"That night, Kaito reads Yến's new code.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"tip","ja":"イエン、ここ、バグ。","en":"Yến, there's a bug here.","tag":"deadpan, a little smug","ref":"E10·L44"},
{"t":"line","who":"yen","mood":"sleepy","ja":"…ありがとう。","en":"...Thank you.","tag":"sighs, smiling","ref":"E10·L45"},
{"t":"narr","text":"六月のコードレビューのけんかを考えると、これは大きな一歩だ。市は、この仕事のお金を大学に[払]{はら}うことになった。ロドリゴも、絵で見るひなんガイドをかく仕事をもらった。どの言葉を読む人にも分かるガイドだ。イエンの声の警報と、ロドリゴの絵は、同じページにのる。イエンは、ロドリゴの[下書]{したが}きを見るたびに、「この線、いいね」と言う。ロドリゴは、そのたびに少し赤くなる。つばめ通りでは、[商店街]{しょうてんがい}の人たちが、来年もまつりをすることに決めた。","en":"After their fight over code reviews in June, this is a big step. The city has agreed to pay the university for the work, and Rodrigo has been hired to draw a picture guide to evacuating that anyone can follow, whatever language they read. Yến's voice alerts and Rodrigo's drawings will go on the same page. Every time Yến sees one of his sketches, she says, \"I like this line,\" and every time, Rodrigo goes a little pink. On Tsubame Street, the shopkeepers have decided to hold the festival again next year.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"木曜日の夜は、英語の時間だ。トビーとまりやは、居間で英語で話す。ほかの人は、木曜日の夜は、なぜか居間に入って来ない。今夜のテーマは、「家族」だ。まりやは、トビーに[反対]{はんたい}させようとする。トビーは、いつものように笑って、\"Everything's fine at home.\" と言いかけた。でも、まりやの顔を見て、やめた。","en":"Thursday night is English night. Toby and Mariya talk in English in the living room. For some reason, nobody else comes into the living room on Thursday nights. Tonight's topic is \"family.\" Mariya keeps trying to make Toby disagree with her. As usual, Toby smiles and starts to say, \"Everything's fine at home.\" Then he sees Mariya's face and stops.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"oops","ja":"Actually, no. My dad's sick. I've been telling everyone it's fine.","en":"じつは、ちがうんだ。父が病気なんだ。ずっと、みんなに大丈夫って言ってた。","lang":"en","tag":"quietly, the smile gone","audio":"the next two lines are in English. Toby: Australian accent. Mariya: Japanese learner, careful.","ref":"E10·L46"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"tip","ja":"Then... stop saying that. Call him.","en":"じゃあ…それ、言うのやめて。お父さんに電話して。","lang":"en","tag":"gently, but firm","ref":"E10·L47"},
{"t":"narr","text":"トビーが父のことを本当に話したのは、これがはじめてだ。それも、英語で。日本語でも、まだだれにも言っていない。その夜、二人は、いつもより長く居間にいた。","en":"It is the first time Toby has told anyone the truth about his dad, and he said it in English. He still hasn't told anyone in Japanese. That night, the two of them stay in the living room longer than usual.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u10-x1","type":"mcq","q":"On the stairs Cheska says [大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}なわけじゃない。でも、だめなわけでもないの。 What is she telling Aoi?","options":[{"t":"She isn't simply fine, and she isn't in a terrible state either; the truth is in between","why":"Right. ～わけではない takes back an idea without saying the opposite. She takes back \"so I must be fine,\" and then \"so I must be falling apart\" as well. What is left is ただ、[眠]{ねむ}れないだけ.","ok":true},
{"t":"She is completely fine, as she said before","why":"That was [大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}, on the bench and in the kitchen. ～なわけじゃない takes that back."},
{"t":"There is no reason for Aoi to worry","why":"わけ can mean \"reason,\" but ～わけではない is a set pattern: \"it isn't that ～.\" And she is talking about herself."},
{"t":"She can't cope at all","why":"She says that isn't true either: だめなわけでもない. も adds a second thing that isn't the case."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u10-x2","type":"mcq","q":"At the counter, Aoi says [申請]{しんせい}に[参]{まい}りました, and Mr. Matsumoto asks お[写真]{しゃしん}は、お[持]{も}ちでしょうか. What is each of them doing?","options":[{"t":"Aoi lowers her own action, and Mr. Matsumoto raises the visitors'","why":"Right. [参]{まい}る is the humble \"come,\" for Aoi's own action. お持ちでしょうか is the respectful \"do you have?\", for the visitors. Mr. Matsumoto lowers his own side too: [伺]{うかが}う, お[送]{おく}りいたしました.","ok":true},
{"t":"Aoi is raising herself, because she is the customer","why":"Nobody raises themselves in keigo. [参]{まい}る lowers the speaker's own coming and going."},
{"t":"Both verbs are respectful, about Mr. Matsumoto","why":"[参]{まい}りました is about Aoi's own coming, and お持ちでしょうか is about what the visitors have."},
{"t":"Mr. Matsumoto is being humble about his own photos","why":"The photos are Cheska's. お + [持]{も}ち is the respectful pattern for the other person."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u10-x3","type":"mcq","q":"At four in the morning, Cheska says だれにも分からなくても、ルールは同じ. What does ～ても add?","options":[{"t":"\"Even if\": even if nobody finds out, the rule doesn't change","why":"Right. ～ても accepts the first half (nobody will know) and says the second half is true anyway.","ok":true},
{"t":"\"Because\": nobody knows, so the rule is the same","why":"\"Because\" would be から or ので. Cheska isn't giving a reason."},
{"t":"\"If\": if nobody knows, then it's the same rule","why":"\"If\" would be 分からなければ or 分からなかったら. ～ても is \"even if.\""},
{"t":"\"When\": the rule changes when people find out","why":"That is the opposite of her point. The rule is the same either way."}]}},
{"t":"lang","items":["Even if: 送っても、読めなければ… (Cheska), だれにも分からなくても (Cheska), 雨がふっていなくても (Rodrigo), どんなに[待]{ま}っても[届]{とど}かない (Fumiko-san). ～ても accepts the first half and says the second half is true anyway.","Not exactly: [届]{とど}いたわけではありません, [責]{せ}めているわけではないんです, [大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}なわけじゃない, [島]{しま}を出たいわけじゃない.","Two kinds of polite: Aoi and Mr. Matsumoto use full keigo ([参]{まい}りました, でございます). Cheska uses plain です and ます with short sentences. Both are polite, and both are clear.","A pun needs two meanings: Dr. Amoako's 言えん is \"can't say\" in the local dialect, and it sounds like イエン."]},
{"t":"reflect","q":"Aoi says [一人]{ひとり}で[起]{お}きていることはないよ, and the house adds a row to its app. When someone you know keeps saying [大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}, what kind of help have you found they can accept?"}]},{"unit":"e3u11","n":11,"title":"Winter visitors","month":"December–January","level":"N3","enDefault":false,"parts":[{"t":"narr","text":"水は、一階の[床]{ゆか}の上十二センチまで来て、[引]{ひ}いた。チェスカは「[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}」と言うのをやめた。家のアプリには、「雨の夜」の[行]{ぎょう}がふえた。[資料館]{しりょうかん}のぬれた[台帳]{だいちょう}から、文子さんの手紙の[住所]{じゅうしょ}が、[昔]{むかし}のある春になくなっていたことが分かった。","en":"The water came up twelve centimeters over the downstairs floor, then went down again. Cheska stopped saying she was fine, and the house app got a row for rainy nights. A wet ledger at the city archive showed that the address on Fumiko-san's letters stopped existing one spring, long ago.","recap":true,"lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[階段]{かいだん}のそばの[棚]{たな}のことは、もうみんな知っている。こわれた物をそこに[置]{お}いておくと、何日かあとに、[直]{なお}って[戻]{もど}ってくる。メモは何もない。だれが直しているのか、みんな分かっている。でも、だれも口に出さない。それが、この家のやり方だ。","en":"By now, everyone knows about the shelf by the stairs. If you leave something broken on it, a few days later it comes back fixed, with no note. Everyone knows who fixes things, but nobody ever says so. That is how this house works.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"十二月の[第二週]{だいにしゅう}に、はじめての[大雪]{おおゆき}がふった。朝六時、[正一]{しょういち}さんは、また風でこわれたまりやのかさを直して、道をわたって来た。棚に戻すつもりだった。そして、[玄関]{げんかん}の前の[三段]{さんだん}の[石段]{いしだん}で、すべって[転]{ころ}んだ。五分後、[夜勤]{やきん}から帰ってきたかいとが、雪の中にすわっている正一さんを見つけた。正一さんは立ち上がれない。そして、そのことに、ものすごく[怒]{おこ}っている。","en":"The first heavy snow comes in the second week of December. At six in the morning, Shōichi-san crosses the street with Mariya's umbrella. The wind broke it again, and he has just fixed it. He is going to put it back on the shelf. On the three stone steps in front of the door, he slips and falls. Five minutes later, Kaito, coming home from his night shift, finds him sitting in the snow. Shōichi-san can't get up, and he is extremely annoyed about it.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"plates","title":"On the ward","hint":"Read each sign, then tap it to check.","items":[{"ja":"整形外科 病棟","ro":"せいけいげか びょうとう","who":"*Orthopedic ward.* 整形外科 is the hospital department for bones and joints. 病棟 is a ward."},{"ja":"面会時間 午後2時～7時","ro":"めんかいじかん ごご にじ から しちじ","who":"*Visiting hours: 2 to 7 p.m.* 面会 means meeting someone face to face. Hospitals use it for visits."},{"ja":"転倒注意","ro":"てんとうちゅうい","who":"*Caution: risk of falling.* 転倒 is a fall, and 注意 is care. This card hangs above Shōichi-san's bed. In his opinion, it is a little late."},{"ja":"退院予定日：未定","ro":"たいいんよていび：みてい","who":"*Planned discharge date: not decided.* 退院 is leaving the hospital, the opposite of 入院. 未定 means \"not decided yet.\""}]},
{"t":"narr","text":"[腰]{こし}の[骨]{ほね}に、小さいひびが入っていた。[手術]{しゅじゅつ}はしないで、コルセットをつけて、二週間ぐらい入院する。[恵]{めぐみ}さんが[看護師]{かんごし}として働いている、[市民病院]{しみんびょういん}だ。三日目の午後、学校の帰りに面会に来たのは、[颯太]{そうた}だった。","en":"There is a small crack in a bone in his lower back. There will be no operation. He will wear a back brace and stay in the hospital for about two weeks. It is the city hospital, where Megumi works as a nurse. On the third afternoon, Sōta comes to visit, straight from school.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"sota","mood":"yay","ja":"おじいちゃん、にゃん[助]{すけ}は元気だよ。学校の帰りに、毎日ぼくがごはんをあげてるから、[安心]{あんしん}して。","en":"Grandpa, Nyansuke's fine. I feed him every day on the way home from school, so don't worry.","gl":"安心する (あんしんする): to stop worrying, to feel safe.","tag":"proud, cheerful","ref":"E11·L1"},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"tip","ja":"にゃん[太郎]{たろう}だ。","en":"He's Nyantarō.","tag":"gruff, without looking up","ref":"E11·L2"},
{"t":"line","who":"sota","mood":"hello","ja":"にゃん[助]{すけ}だってば。","en":"It's Nyansuke. I keep telling you.","gl":"～ってば: \"I'm telling you,\" said when the other person isn't listening.","tag":"exasperated","ref":"E11·L3"},
{"t":"narr","text":"次に来たのは、かいとだった。紙ぶくろを持っている。","en":"The next visitor is Kaito, with a paper bag.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"think","ja":"あの、[棚]{たな}にラジオが[置]{お}いてあったんですけど。音が出なくて。","en":"Um, someone left a radio on the shelf. It doesn't make any sound.","gl":"棚 (たな): a shelf.","tag":"hesitant","ref":"E11·L4"},
{"t":"narr","text":"棚が正一さんのものだと、正一さんに言った人は、まだ一人もいない。今も、かいとは言っていない。","en":"Nobody has ever told Shōichi-san that the shelf is his. Strictly speaking, Kaito still hasn't.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"think","ja":"…中を見たか。","en":"...Did you look inside?","tag":"pause, interested","ref":"E11·L5"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"oops","ja":"見ました。[線]{せん}が一本、[外]{はず}れていました。","en":"I did. One wire had come off.","gl":"線 (せん): a line; here, a wire. 外れる (はずれる): to come off.","tag":"nervous","ref":"E11·L6"},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"tip","ja":"はんだごては、[机]{つくえ}の右の[引]{ひ}き[出]{だ}しだ。[熱]{あつ}いから、ゆっくりやれ。","en":"The soldering iron is in the right-hand drawer of the desk. It gets hot, so take your time.","gl":"はんだごて: a soldering iron. 引き出し (ひきだし): a drawer. やれ: the blunt command form of やる.","tag":"matter-of-fact","ref":"E11·L7"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[説明]{せつめい}は、それだけだった。ちょうどそのとき、[休憩]{きゅうけい}中の恵さんが、白い[制服]{せいふく}のまま[病室]{びょうしつ}に入ってきた。","en":"That is the whole explanation. Just then, Megumi comes into the room on her break, still in her white uniform.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"megumi","mood":"sleepy","ja":"[以心伝心]{いしんでんしん}ね。うちの男の人は、[大事]{だいじ}なことほど、言葉にしないんだから。","en":"No need for words, I see. With the men in this family, the more something matters, the less they say.","gl":"以心伝心 (いしんでんしん): understanding each other without words. 大事 (だいじ): important.","tag":"amused, fond","ref":"E11·L8"},
{"t":"narr","text":"かいとは、ラジオを持って帰った。ろうかで、コートを着た男の人とすれちがった。恵さんの[兄]{あに}の[浩之]{ひろゆき}さんだ。大阪から、朝一番の電車で来た。手には、マンションのパンフレットを持っている。","en":"Kaito leaves with the radio. In the hallway, he passes a man in a coat: Megumi's older brother, Hiroyuki. He came from Osaka on the first train of the morning, and he is holding a brochure for an apartment building.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"hiroyuki","mood":"tip","ja":"かもめ[荘]{そう}を[売]{う}って、うちの近くのマンションに[引]{ひ}っ[越]{こ}せばいいんだ。エレベーターもあるし、病院も近い。雪も、ほとんどふらない。","en":"They should sell Kamome House and move into an apartment near us. There's an elevator, and the hospital is close. It hardly ever snows, either.","gl":"マンション: an apartment building (not a mansion).","tag":"tired, already decided","ref":"E11·L9"},
{"t":"line","who":"megumi","mood":"think","ja":"お父さんの[顔]{かお}を見る前に、もうその話？","en":"You haven't even seen Dad yet, and you're already on that?","tag":"annoyed","ref":"E11·L10"},
{"t":"line","who":"hiroyuki","mood":"oops","ja":"[水害]{すいがい}の次は[骨折]{こっせつ}だぞ。[不安]{ふあん}で、夜も[眠]{ねむ}れないよ。毎晩電話しても、母さんは「[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}」しか言わないし。","en":"First a flood, now a broken bone. I'm so worried I can't sleep. I call every night, and all Mom ever says is \"We're fine.\"","gl":"骨折 (こっせつ): a broken bone. 不安 (ふあん): worried, uneasy.","tag":"worried, rising voice","ref":"E11·L11"},
{"t":"line","who":"megumi","mood":"tip","ja":"毎週あの家に行って、[薬]{くすり}を[数]{かぞ}えて、あの[階段]{かいだん}を見て[心配]{しんぱい}しているのは、私だよ。お兄ちゃんが来るのは、年に二回でしょ。","en":"I'm the one who goes over every week, counts the pills, and looks at those stairs and worries. You come twice a year.","gl":"薬 (くすり): medicine.","tag":"sharp, tired","ref":"E11·L12"},
{"t":"line","who":"megumi","mood":"hello","ja":"それなのに、[大事]{だいじ}なことを[決]{き}めるときだけ、[長男]{ちょうなん}の[顔]{かお}をするんだから。","en":"And yet whenever there's something important to decide, you show up as the oldest son.","gl":"それなのに: and yet. 長男 (ちょうなん): the oldest son. ～の顔をする: to act like ～.","tag":"bitter","ref":"E11·L13"},
{"t":"line","who":"hiroyuki","mood":"think","ja":"…[遠]{とお}くにいるから、よけいにこわいんだよ。","en":"...It's because I'm far away that it scares me even more.","gl":"よけいに: even more.","tag":"quietly","ref":"E11·L14"},
{"t":"narr","text":"どちらも、まちがっていない。だから、家族のけんかになる。それから二週間、棚に置いた物は、ちゃんと直って戻ってきた。前より少しだけへただったし、一度は「すみません」と書いたメモまでついていた。これは、この家のやり方とちがう。かいとが「ししょう」と[呼]{よ}ぶねこは、かいとの仕事を、いつもそばで見ていた。二十六日、正一さんは、コルセットとつえで家に帰ってきた。","en":"Neither of them is wrong, and that is what makes it a family argument. For the next two weeks, things left on the shelf keep coming back fixed. They are a little less neat than before, and once there is even a note that says \"Sorry,\" which is not how this house works. The cat, whom Kaito calls ししょう, \"master,\" sits beside him the whole time and watches him work. On the twenty-sixth, Shōichi-san comes home with a back brace and a cane.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"cat","pose":"curious","alt":"The cat looking up with her ears forward, watching Kaito solder a radio"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[年末]{ねんまつ}、日本人の[住人]{じゅうにん}は、みんな家に帰った。まりやは島へ、あおいは千代さんの店へ、かいとは山の町へ。かもめ荘に[残]{のこ}ったのは、チェスカ、ロドリゴ、イエン、トビーの四人だ。四人は、文子さんに教えてもらって、はじめておせち[料理]{りょうり}を作った。","en":"At the end of the year, the Japanese residents all go home: Mariya to her island, Aoi to Chiyo's shop, and Kaito to his town in the mountains. The four who stay at Kamome House (Cheska, Rodrigo, Yến and Toby) make New Year food for the first time, with Fumiko-san teaching them.","gl":"おせち料理 (おせちりょうり): special food for the New Year.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"そば[屋]{や}がいちばんいそがしいのは、大みそかだ。年の終わりに、町じゅうの人が年こしそばを食べるからだ。かいとの家の店も、夜の十一時まで、ずっと[客]{きゃく}がいた。最後の客が帰ると、かいとは何も言わないで、一人分のそばを[打]{う}った。そして、お父さんの前に置いた。","en":"A soba shop's busiest night is New Year's Eve, when the whole town eats soba to see the old year out. At Kaito's family's shop, there are customers until eleven at night. When the last one leaves, Kaito, without a word, makes one bowl of soba by hand and puts it in front of his father.","gl":"年こしそば (としこしそば): soba eaten on New Year's Eve. そばを打つ (うつ): to make soba noodles by hand.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"お父さんは、だまって食べた。それから、からのおわんをかいとの方に出した。","en":"His father eats it in silence. Then he pushes the empty bowl toward Kaito.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"kuze","mood":"hello","ja":"…おかわり。","en":"...Another bowl.","gl":"おかわり: a second helping.","tag":"gruff, quiet","ref":"E11·L15"},
{"t":"line","who":"kuze","mood":"tip","ja":"水が少し多い。次はへらせ。","en":"A little too much water. Use less next time.","gl":"へらす: to use less, to reduce.","tag":"flat","ref":"E11·L16"},
{"t":"narr","text":"あきらめた[相手]{あいて}のそばに、[文句]{もんく}は言わない。かいとは、それを知っている。だから、次の言葉が言えた。","en":"Nobody complains about the soba of someone they've given up on. Kaito knows that, and it gives him the courage to say the next thing.","gl":"あきらめる: to give up on. 文句 (もんく): a complaint.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"think","ja":"父さん。おれ、プログラムを書く仕事がしたい。でも、そばを[打]{う}つのも好きなんだ。どっちも本当。","en":"Dad. I want to write programs for a living. But I love making soba too. Both are true.","tag":"nervous, then steady","ref":"E11·L17"},
{"t":"line","who":"kuze","mood":"think","ja":"店は、ばあちゃんの[介護]{かいご}を[支]{ささ}えている。町には、もうほかに食べる所もない。「好きにしろ」とは、かんたんには言えん。","en":"The shop pays for your grandma's care. And there's nowhere else left in town to eat. I can't just say, \"Do what you want.\"","gl":"介護 (かいご): care for an older or sick person. 支える (ささえる): to support. 言えん: 言えない, in his Gifu dialect.","tag":"slow, heavy","ref":"E11·L18"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"hello","ja":"分かってる。","en":"I know.","tag":"quietly","ref":"E11·L19"},
{"t":"line","who":"kuze","mood":"tip","ja":"お前の名前の「[海]{かい}」はな、おれが[若]{わか}いころ、行きたかった所だ。山を出て、海の見える町で働くつもりだった。[結局]{けっきょく}、行かなかったけどな。","en":"The \"sea\" in your name: that's where I wanted to go when I was young. I meant to leave the mountains and work in a town by the sea. In the end, I never went.","gl":"お前 (おまえ): \"you,\" from a father to a son. 若い (わかい): young. 結局 (けっきょく): in the end. Kaito's name is written 海斗; 海 means \"sea.\"","tag":"softer, looking away","ref":"E11·L20"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"oops","ja":"…はじめて聞いた。","en":"...That's the first time I've heard that.","tag":"surprised, soft","ref":"E11·L21"},
{"t":"line","who":"kuze","mood":"hello","ja":"だから、お前が海の町にいるのは、悪い気はしない。店のことは、まだ決めてない。春に、また話そう。","en":"So I don't mind you being in a town by the sea. The shop is still undecided. We'll talk again in the spring.","gl":"悪い気はしない: \"I don't mind\"; it actually feels rather good.","tag":"gruff, almost smiling","ref":"E11·L22"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"一月十日、日曜日。みんなが、かもめ荘に戻ってきた。かいとは、お父さんにもらったそば[粉]{こ}のふくろを持って帰ってきた。今夜の夕ごはんは、かいとのそばだ。浩之さんも、大阪から来ている。恵さんと颯太もいる。十二人分のそばが行きわたると、文子さんがはしを置いた。","en":"Sunday, January 10. Everyone is back at Kamome House. Kaito has come back with a bag of buckwheat flour from his father, so tonight's dinner is Kaito's soba. Hiroyuki has come from Osaka, and Megumi and Sōta are here too. When all twelve have a bowl, Fumiko-san puts down her chopsticks.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"食べながらでいいので、聞いてください。この家を[売]{う}るか、売らないか。どちらにも[一長一短]{いっちょういったん}があって、家族だけでは[決]{き}められません。","en":"Please keep eating, but listen. Whether to sell this house or not: each choice has its good and bad points, and the family can't decide alone.","gl":"一長一短 (いっちょういったん): having good points and bad points.","tag":"calm, serious","ref":"E11·L23"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"tip","ja":"ここは、[皆]{みな}さんの家でもあります。[遠慮]{えんりょ}しないで、[意見]{いけん}を聞かせてください。","en":"This is your house too. Please don't hold back. Tell us what you think.","gl":"遠慮する (えんりょする): to hold back to be polite. 意見 (いけん): an opinion.","tag":"warmly","ref":"E11·L24"},
{"t":"narr","text":"トビーがはじめてこの家に[泊]{と}まったのは、十五さいのときだ。それに、トビーは、相手が聞きたいことを言ってしまう人だ。でも、今このテーブルでは、二人の人が[反対]{はんたい}のことを聞きたがっている。","en":"Toby first stayed in this house when he was fifteen. He is also someone who tells people what they want to hear. But at this table, two people want to hear opposite things.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"think","ja":"…[売]{う}らないでほしいです。十五さいのとき、はじめてここに[泊]{と}めてもらいました。今も、ここが日本のぼくの家です。","en":"...I hope you won't sell it. I first stayed here when I was fifteen. It's still my home in Japan.","gl":"泊める (とめる): to let someone stay the night.","tag":"hesitant, then sincere","ref":"E11·L25"},
{"t":"line","who":"hiroyuki","mood":"oops","ja":"その気持ちは、うれしいです。でも、父はもう[階段]{かいだん}を[上]{のぼ}れません。むこうの家の[寝室]{しんしつ}も二階です。それに、ここは水も来る所です。","en":"I'm glad you feel that way. But my father can't climb stairs anymore, and my parents' bedroom across the street is upstairs too. And besides, this area floods.","gl":"寝室 (しんしつ): a bedroom.","tag":"polite, strained","ref":"E11·L26"},
{"t":"line","who":"cheska","mood":"tip","ja":"水は、本当に[危険]{きけん}です。でも、水が来る前には、[警報]{けいほう}が出ます。私たちは、早くひなんできます。階段と雪は、何も知らせてくれません。","en":"The water really is dangerous. But before the water comes, there's an alert. We can evacuate early. Stairs and snow don't warn you about anything.","gl":"危険 (きけん): dangerous.","tag":"calm, sure","ref":"E11·L27"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"think","ja":"[物置]{ものおき}は一階で、おふろとトイレのとなりですよね。あそこを部屋にすれば、階段は[一段]{いちだん}も使わなくていいんじゃないですか。","en":"The storeroom is downstairs, right next to the bath and the toilets. If we made it into a room, he wouldn't have to use a single stair.","gl":"物置 (ものおき): a storeroom. 一段も～ない: not even one step.","tag":"thinking out loud","ref":"E11·L28"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"think","ja":"それに、ここなら、いつもだれかいます。あの朝、ぼくが帰ってくるまで、だれもいませんでした。","en":"And here, there's always someone around. That morning, nobody was there until I got home.","tag":"quiet, firm","ref":"E11·L29"},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"tip","ja":"[柱]{はしら}はしっかりしている。前の[石段]{いしだん}をスロープにして、[手]{て}すりを[付]{つ}ければ、[住]{す}める。","en":"The posts are solid. Turn the stone steps out front into a ramp, put in a handrail, and we can live there.","gl":"柱 (はしら): a post, a pillar. スロープ: a ramp. 手すり (てすり): a handrail.","tag":"matter-of-fact","ref":"E11·L30"},
{"t":"narr","text":"正一さんは、もう[測]{はか}ってあるらしい。たぶん、十月に。恵さんが、おわんを置いた。","en":"Shōichi-san has apparently measured everything already, probably back in October. Megumi puts down her bowl.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"megumi","mood":"think","ja":"[賛成]{さんせい}したい。でも、[正直]{しょうじき}に言うね。私は、これ[以上]{いじょう}は[無理]{むり}。[夜勤]{やきん}もあるし、[颯太]{そうた}もいるし。","en":"I want to agree. But I'll be honest. I can't do any more than I already do. I work night shifts, and I have Sōta.","gl":"賛成 (さんせい): agreeing. 正直に (しょうじきに): honestly. 無理 (むり): impossible, too much.","tag":"honest, tired","ref":"E11·L31"},
{"t":"narr","text":"恵さんが、お母さんの前で「無理」と言ったのは、これがはじめてだ。浩之さんは、しばらく[妹]{いもうと}の顔を見ていた。","en":"It is the first time Megumi has said 無理 in front of her mother. Hiroyuki looks at his sister for a while.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"hiroyuki","mood":"think","ja":"…[恵]{めぐみ}が毎週行ってくれるから、おれは遠くで働けるんだよな。ありがとうって、一度も言ってなかった。","en":"...I can only work far away because you go over every week. I've never once said thank you.","tag":"slowly, ashamed","ref":"E11·L32"},
{"t":"line","who":"megumi","mood":"sleepy","ja":"…毎晩の電話、お母さん、楽しみにしてるよ。私も、言ってなかったけど。","en":"...Mom looks forward to your call every night, you know. I never told you that either.","gl":"楽しみにする (たのしみにする): to look forward to.","tag":"softening","ref":"E11·L33"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"oops","ja":"あの…[家賃]{やちん}を少し安くしていただけるなら、[管理人]{かんりにん}の仕事は私がやります。家賃を[集]{あつ}めたり、[修理]{しゅうり}をたのんだり、ごみの[当番]{とうばん}を決めたり。","en":"Um... If you could lower my rent a little, I'd do the manager's work. Collecting the rent, calling for repairs, making the garbage schedule.","gl":"家賃 (やちん): rent. 管理人 (かんりにん): a building manager. 修理 (しゅうり): a repair. 当番 (とうばん): a turn on a schedule.","tag":"awkward, rushing","ref":"E11·L34"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"sleepy","ja":"[親切]{しんせつ}で言っているわけではありません。[家賃]{やちん}のためです。","en":"I'm not offering to be nice. It's for the rent.","gl":"親切 (しんせつ): kindness.","tag":"stiffly formal, embarrassed","ref":"E11·L35"},
{"t":"narr","text":"テーブルのだれも、それを[信]{しん}じていない。ねこも、信じていない顔をしている。","en":"Nobody at the table believes that. The cat doesn't look convinced either.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"cat","pose":"smug","alt":"The cat sitting by the low table, looking pleased with herself"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"yay","ja":"[一石二鳥]{いっせきにちょう}ですね。主人は[階段]{かいだん}を使わない。私は仕事がへる。","en":"Two birds with one stone, then. My husband stays off the stairs, and I have less work.","gl":"一石二鳥 (いっせきにちょう): one stone, two birds. へる: to go down, to become less.","tag":"pleased, a little playful","ref":"E11·L36"},
{"t":"line","who":"hiroyuki","mood":"think","ja":"…でも、お金はどうするの？","en":"...But how will you pay for it?","tag":"cautious","ref":"E11·L37"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"tip","ja":"むこうの家を[売]{う}れば、[足]{た}ります。","en":"If we sell our house across the street, that will cover it.","gl":"足りる (たりる): to be enough.","tag":"brisk","ref":"E11·L38"},
{"t":"line","who":"hiroyuki","mood":"oops","ja":"…[結局]{けっきょく}、家を売るんだね。","en":"...So you're selling a house after all.","tag":"half laughing","ref":"E11·L39"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"yay","ja":"ええ。あなたが[考]{かんが}えていた家とは、ちがいますけど。","en":"Yes. Just not the one you had in mind.","tag":"dry, amused","ref":"E11·L40"},
{"t":"line","who":"hiroyuki","mood":"hello","ja":"…もう[階段]{かいだん}を[上]{のぼ}らないと[約束]{やくそく}してくれるなら、[反対]{はんたい}はしないよ。","en":"...If you promise never to climb those stairs again, I won't say no.","gl":"約束 (やくそく): a promise. 反対 (はんたい): opposing; the opposite of 賛成.","tag":"relenting","ref":"E11·L41"},
{"t":"line","who":"shoichi","mood":"sleepy","ja":"[約束]{やくそく}する。二階の[電球]{でんきゅう}は、かいとに[任]{まか}せた。","en":"I promise. The light bulbs upstairs are Kaito's job now.","gl":"電球 (でんきゅう): a light bulb. 任せる (まかせる): to leave something to someone.","tag":"gruff, final","ref":"E11·L42"},
{"t":"line","who":"kaito","mood":"oops","ja":"…え、ぼくですか？","en":"...Wait, me?","tag":"startled, mouth full","ref":"E11·L43"},
{"t":"narr","text":"これで決まった。かもめ荘は売らない。道のむこうの小さい家を売る。物置は、[段]{だん}のない部屋になる。あおいは管理人になる。そして、かいとは、二階の電球の[係]{かかり}になった。","en":"So it is decided. Kamome House stays, and the little house across the street will be sold. The storeroom will become a room with no steps, Aoi will be the manager, and Kaito is now in charge of the light bulbs upstairs.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"note","text":"言葉の前について、「ない」という意味をそえる漢字があります。たとえば、[不]{ふ}、[無]{む}、[未]{み}です。浩之さんの「不安」は、安心が「ない」。恵さんの「無理」は、[方法]{ほうほう}が「ない」。「未定」は、「まだ」決まっていない。「未」は「まだ～ない」という意味なので、「[未来]{みらい}」は「まだ来ていない時」です。","en":"Some kanji go in front of a word and add the meaning \"not.\" Three of them are 不, 無 and 未. Hiroyuki's 不安 means there is no peace of mind. Megumi's 無理 means there is no way. 未定 means \"not decided yet.\" 未 means \"not yet,\" which is why it is also in 未来, \"the future\": the time that hasn't come yet.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"その夜、102号室では、ロドリゴが、アニメのスタジオから来たメールを、もう十五回も読んでいる。ロドリゴのひなんガイドを見た、[藤原]{ふじわら}さんというプロデューサーからだ。まだ、ねこにしか話していない。そして物置では、コルセットをつけた人が、[懐中電灯]{かいちゅうでんとう}で入口の[幅]{はば}を[測]{はか}っていた。もちろん、階段は使っていない。","en":"That night, in Room 102, Rodrigo is reading an email from an animation studio for the fifteenth time. It is from a producer named Fujiwara, who saw his evacuation guide. So far, he has told only the cat. And in the storeroom, by flashlight, a man in a back brace is measuring the doorway. Of course, he didn't use the stairs to get there.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u11-x1","type":"mcq","q":"The card above Shōichi-san's bed says [転倒注意]{てんとうちゅうい}. What is it telling people?","options":[{"t":"Be careful: this patient could fall","why":"Right. [転倒]{てんとう} is a fall, and 注意 is care. Hospitals put this card by the beds of patients who are not steady on their feet.","ok":true},
{"t":"No visitors without permission","why":"Visits are [面会]{めんかい}, as in 面会時間. This card is about the patient's balance."},
{"t":"The patient is moving to another ward","why":"[転]{てん} can mean \"move\" in some words, but here it goes with [倒]{とう}, \"fall over.\" 転倒 is a fall."},
{"t":"Be careful: the floor is wet","why":"There is nothing about floors or water in these four kanji: a fall, and care."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u11-x2","type":"mcq","q":"Fumiko-san says [一石二鳥]{いっせきにちょう}ですね. What are her two birds?","options":[{"t":"Her husband stays off the stairs, and she has less work","why":"Right. She names them herself: 主人は[階段]{かいだん}を使わない。私は仕事がへる。 One decision (a room downstairs and a manager) gets both.","ok":true},
{"t":"Selling the house and moving near Hiroyuki","why":"That was Hiroyuki's plan in the hospital hallway. The family has just decided against it."},
{"t":"Aoi pays less rent, and the cat gets fed","why":"Aoi does ask for lower rent, but Fumiko-san's two birds are her husband's and her own."},
{"t":"Everyone has a different opinion","why":"That would be [十人十色]{じゅうにんといろ}: ten people, ten colors."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u11-x3","type":"mcq","q":"Kaito's father says お前が海の町にいるのは、悪い気はしない. How does he feel about it?","options":[{"t":"He is quietly pleased","why":"Right. 悪い気はしない is literally \"it doesn't feel bad,\" but people use it to say they like something without saying so directly. From Kaito's father, that is a lot.","ok":true},
{"t":"He feels guilty about it","why":"悪い here is about how it feels to him, not about doing something wrong."},
{"t":"He has no feelings about it","why":"The understatement hides a feeling. He has just told Kaito where the \"sea\" in his name comes from."},
{"t":"He thinks it is a bad idea","why":"Then he would say something like よくない. He says the opposite, in a roundabout way."}]}},
{"t":"lang","items":["Four-kanji idioms can often be read from their parts. [以心伝心]{いしんでんしん}: the heart passes to the heart. [一長一短]{いっちょういったん}: one long, one short, so a good point and a bad point. [一石二鳥]{いっせきにちょう}: one stone, two birds.","\"Not\" in front: 不安 (no peace of mind), 無理 (no way, too much) and 未定 (not decided yet). Two pairs of opposites from this episode: 入院 and [退院]{たいいん}, [賛成]{さんせい} and [反対]{はんたい}.","Family words change with the listener. Inside the family, Megumi says お父さん, お母さん and お兄ちゃん. Talking to the residents, Hiroyuki calls the same man 父, and Fumiko-san calls him 主人. Use these plain words for your own family when you talk to other people."]},
{"t":"reflect","q":"Megumi stayed in Shioura, and Hiroyuki moved away. Each of them was carrying something the other had never said thank you for. In your family or your home, who does the visiting, and who worries from far away?"}]},{"unit":"e3u12","n":12,"title":"Letters in spring","month":"February–March","level":"N3","enDefault":false,"parts":[{"t":"narr","text":"[正一]{しょういち}さんは、雪の[石段]{いしだん}で[転]{ころ}んで、二週間入院した。一月に、[佐藤]{さとう}さんの家族は、かもめ荘のみんなの意見を聞いて、決めた。かもめ荘は売らない。そのかわり、道のむこうの小さい家を売る。[物置]{ものおき}を、[段]{だん}のない部屋にする。あおいが[管理人]{かんりにん}になる。かいとのお父さんは、そばをおかわりした。","en":"Shōichi-san slipped on the snowy stone steps and spent two weeks in the hospital. In January, the Satō family asked everyone at Kamome House what they thought, and then decided. Kamome House stays; the Satōs' little house across the street will be sold instead. The storeroom will become a room with no steps. Aoi will be the manager. Kaito's father asked for a second bowl of soba.","recap":true,"lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"二月。[大工]{だいく}さんが二人、物置を部屋に作りかえている。道のむこうの家には、「[売家]{うりいえ}」の紙がはってある。正一さんは、コルセットをつけてコートを三まい着て、庭で台所のいすにすわっている。そして、正しいけれど、だれも聞きたくないアドバイスをしている。","en":"February. Two carpenters are turning the storeroom into a room. On the Satōs' little house across the street, there is a For Sale sign. Shōichi-san sits on a kitchen chair in the garden, wearing his back brace and three coats. His advice is correct, and nobody wants it.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"手紙の相手をさがすのに、冬じゅうかかった。トビーは、タスマニアの自分の高校に[連絡]{れんらく}した。[汐浦]{しおうら}との[姉妹都市]{しまいとし}の[交流]{こうりゅう}は、昔、その高校から始まったのだ。高校の先生が、トビーのふるさとの町の[郷土史]{きょうどし}の会を[紹介]{しょうかい}してくれた。一月、七十代の女の人から[返事]{へんじ}が来た。名前は、ロレイン。そして今日、ロレインから[小包]{こづつみ}が[届]{とど}いた。","en":"Finding the person who wrote the letters took all winter. Toby contacted his old high school in Tasmania, where the sister-city exchange with Shioura began long ago. A teacher there put him in touch with the local history society in his hometown. In January, a woman in her seventies wrote back. Her name is Lorraine. Today, a package from Lorraine has arrived.","gl":"姉妹都市 (しまいとし): a sister city. 郷土史 (きょうどし): local history. 小包 (こづつみ): a package.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"中には、うすい水色の[封筒]{ふうとう}が[三通]{さんつう}入っていた。ロレインが文子さんに出した手紙だ。でも、文子さんには届かないで、ロレインの所に[戻]{もど}ってきた。ロレインは、五十年[以上]{いじょう}、その手紙を[捨]{す}てられなかった。","en":"Inside are three thin, light-blue envelopes. They are letters Lorraine sent to Fumiko-san. They never reached her. They went back to Lorraine instead, and for more than fifty years, she couldn't bring herself to throw them away.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"plates","title":"The envelope","hint":"Read what is written and stamped on it, then tap to check.","items":[{"ja":"汐浦市 川南 126","ro":"しおうらし かわみなみ ひゃくにじゅうろく","who":"The address, in English, with the kanji copied carefully underneath. It is the same handwriting as on every envelope in the tin."},{"ja":"あて所に尋ねあたりません","ro":"あてどころに たずねあたりません","who":"*Not found at this address.* A purple stamp from the Japanese post office. あて所 is the address a letter is sent to. 尋ねあたる means to ask around and find. Japanese mail that can't be delivered still gets this stamp today. Next to it, smaller, is a label in French, the language of international mail: *Inconnu*, \"unknown.\" That was the part Lorraine could read."},{"ja":"差出人に返送","ro":"さしだしにんに へんそう","who":"*Return to sender.* 差出人 is the person who sent the letter. 返送 means sending it back."},{"ja":"43.5.12","ro":"","who":"A date stamp from the Japanese post office, added when the letter was sent back. Japanese post offices used the era year: Shōwa 43, so May 12, 1968. That is the spring when 126 Kawaminami disappeared. The envelopes have never been opened."}]},
{"t":"narr","text":"[文子]{ふみこ}さんは、くだものナイフで一通目を開けた。でも、英語の手書きの字が読めない。だから、トビーが日本語にしながら、声に出して読んだ。","en":"Fumiko-san opens the first envelope with a fruit knife. But she can't read the handwritten English, so Toby reads it aloud, putting it into Japanese as he goes.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"「フミコへ。お元気ですか。前の手紙のお[返事]{へんじ}が、まだ来ません。」","en":"\"Dear Fumiko, How are you? I still haven't had an answer to my last letter.\"","gl":"返事 (へんじ): a reply.","tag":"reading aloud, translating carefully","ref":"E12·L1"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"think","ja":"「病気ではないかと、[心配]{しんぱい}しています。それとも、私が何か[失礼]{しつれい}なことを書いたのでしょうか。」","en":"\"I'm worried you might be ill. Or did I write something rude?\"","gl":"それとも: or. 失礼 (しつれい): rude.","tag":"reading aloud, softer","ref":"E12·L2"},
{"t":"narr","text":"三通目は、その年の十二月の手紙だ。","en":"The third letter is from December of that year.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"「これが、[最後]{さいご}の手紙になるかもしれません。でも、あなたの[住所]{じゅうしょ}は、もう何も見ないで書けるようになりました。」","en":"\"This may be my last letter. But I can write your address now without looking.\"","gl":"最後 (さいご): the last.","tag":"reading aloud, quietly","ref":"E12·L3"},
{"t":"narr","text":"だれも、何も言わない。まりやは、お茶をいれるふりをするのを、やめた。","en":"Nobody says anything. Mariya has stopped pretending to make tea.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"think","ja":"…「[失礼]{しつれい}なこと」を書いたのは、私のほうだと思っていました。","en":"...I always thought I was the one who wrote something rude.","tag":"barely above a whisper","ref":"E12·L4"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"oops","ja":"[引]{ひ}っ[越]{こ}す前に出した手紙で、あの子の漢字の書き[順]{じゅん}を[直]{なお}したんです。「さんずいは、上から書きましょう」と。","en":"In the letter I sent before we moved, I corrected her stroke order. I wrote, \"Let's write the water radical from the top.\"","gl":"書き順 (かきじゅん): stroke order. 直す (なおす): to correct. さんずい: the three-stroke *water* part, as in 汐 and 浦.","tag":"embarrassed, remembering","ref":"E12·L5"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"oops","ja":"え、それで、ロレインさんを[怒]{おこ}らせたと思っていたんですか。五十年[以上]{いじょう}も？","en":"Wait, so you thought that made Lorraine angry? For more than fifty years?","gl":"怒らせる (おこらせる): to make someone angry.","tag":"disbelieving","ref":"E12·L6"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"sleepy","ja":"ですから、それからは、人を[直]{なお}すのは[一回]{いっかい}だけにしているんです。","en":"That's why, ever since, I only correct a person once.","tag":"wry, a little sad","ref":"E12·L7"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"tip","ja":"その手紙は、たぶん[届]{とど}いていませんよ。新しい[住所]{じゅうしょ}といっしょに。","en":"That letter probably never arrived. And your new address was in it.","tag":"gently","ref":"E12·L8"},
{"t":"narr","text":"文子さんは、返事を、先に日本語でえんぴつで書いた。そして、昔、教室で作文を読んだときのように、台所のみんなに読んで聞かせた。英語にするのは、まりやだ。","en":"Fumiko-san writes her reply in Japanese first, in pencil. Then she reads it to everyone in the kitchen, the way she used to read compositions to her class. Mariya will put it into English.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"「ロレインさんへ。お手紙は、五十年以上かかって[届]{とど}きました。ありがとうございます。」","en":"\"Dear Lorraine, Your letters have arrived. It took them more than fifty years. Thank you.\"","tag":"clear, like reading to a class","ref":"E12·L9"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"「あの春、私の家は[引]{ひ}っ[越]{こ}しをしました。その上、町の[住所]{じゅうしょ}の書き方も[変]{か}わりました。新しい住所を書いた手紙は、あなたに届かなかったようです。」","en":"\"That spring, my family moved. On top of that, the town changed the way it wrote its addresses. It seems the letter with my new address never reached you.\"","gl":"その上 (そのうえ): on top of that.","tag":"steady","ref":"E12·L10"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"think","ja":"「私は長い間、あなたが書くのをやめたのだと思っていました。しかし、やめた人は、だれもいなかったのです。」","en":"\"For a long time, I believed you had stopped writing. But nobody had stopped.\"","gl":"しかし: but, however (written style).","tag":"steady, moved","ref":"E12·L11"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"tip","ja":"「つまり、[悪]{わる}かったのは、私でもあなたでもなく、[住所]{じゅうしょ}でした。」","en":"\"In other words, it wasn't your fault or mine. It was the address.\"","gl":"つまり: in other words.","tag":"dry, a hint of humor","ref":"E12·L12"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"yay","ja":"「今度は、メールアドレスも書いておきます。お[返事]{へんじ}をお待ちしています。文子」","en":"\"This time, I am also giving you my email address. I look forward to your reply. Fumiko\"","tag":"warm, hopeful","ref":"E12·L13"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"三月。ロレインのお[孫]{まご}さんが、ビデオ[通話]{つうわ}を用意してくれた。タブレットは、すいはんきに立てかけてある。文子さんは、いちばんいいカーディガンを着ている。となりには、[通訳]{つうやく}のまりやがすわっている。まりやは、英語を書くのはとても上手だ。でも、話すのは、まだ木曜日の練習のときだけだ。トビーも、テーブルのはしにいる。トビーなら、通訳ができる。でも、文子さんは、まりやにたのんだ。トビーは、何も言わないで、お茶を飲んでいる。画面の中で、白いかみの女の人が、顔を近づけた。","en":"March. Lorraine's granddaughter has set up a video call. The tablet is propped against the rice cooker, and Fumiko-san is wearing her best cardigan. Mariya sits next to her to interpret. Mariya writes English beautifully, but she still only speaks it at Thursday practice. Toby is at the end of the table. He could interpret, but Fumiko-san asked Mariya, and Toby sips his tea and says nothing. On the screen, a white-haired woman leans in close.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"lorraine","mood":"yay","ja":"Fumiko? Is that really you? Goodness me. You've got old!","en":"文子？本当にあなた？まあ。年を取ったわね！","lang":"en","tag":"elderly Australian woman, delighted and teasing","audio":"Lorraine's lines are in English, with an Australian accent. She is in her seventies.","ref":"E12·L14"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"oops","ja":"えーと…「[文子]{ふみこ}さん、本当にあなたですか。年を[取]{と}りましたね」とおっしゃっています。","en":"Um... She says, \"Fumiko, is it really you? You've gotten old.\"","gl":"えーと: \"um,\" while you look for words. 年を取る (としをとる): to get old. ～とおっしゃっています: \"she is saying ～,\" respectfully.","tag":"nervous, trying not to soften it","ref":"E12·L15"},
{"t":"narr","text":"まりやは、少しやわらかく[訳]{やく}そうかと思った。でも、そうしなかった。","en":"Mariya thought about making it a little softer. But she didn't.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"yay","ja":"「あなたもね」と[伝]{つた}えてください。","en":"Please tell her, \"So have you.\"","gl":"伝える (つたえる): to pass on a message.","tag":"laughing","ref":"E12·L16"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"それから…「お[久]{ひさ}しぶりです」と。","en":"And... \"Ohisashiburi desu.\"","gl":"お久しぶりです: what you say to someone you haven't seen for a long time.","tag":"softly, after a pause","ref":"E12·L17"},
{"t":"narr","text":"「あなたもね」で、画面のこちらでもむこうでも、笑い声が上がった。次のは、むずかしい。英語には、ぴったりの言葉がない。まりやは、少し考えて、言った。\"It's been a while.\" 画面の中で、ロレインはめがねを外した。","en":"\"So have you\" gets a laugh on both sides of the screen. The next one is harder, because English has no exact match for it. Mariya thinks for a moment and says, \"It's been a while.\" On the screen, Lorraine takes off her glasses.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"note","text":"「お久しぶりです」は、どのぐらい会っていなかったかを言いません。三週間でも、五十年でも、同じ言葉です。長さは、二人がそれぞれ心の中で考えます。でも、英語にするときは、通訳が長さを[選]{えら}ばなければなりません。まりやは、いちばん短い時間に聞こえる言い方を選びました。それで、よかったのです。","en":"お久しぶりです doesn't say how long it has been. The same phrase works for three weeks or for fifty years, and each person fills in the length in their own mind. But to put it into English, the interpreter has to choose a length. Mariya chose the one that sounds like the shortest time, and she was right.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"lorraine","mood":"think","ja":"I always thought I'd written something rude. That's why I could never throw those letters out.","en":"ずっと、私が何か失礼なことを書いたんだと思っていたの。だから、あの手紙は、どうしても捨てられなかった。","lang":"en","tag":"elderly Australian woman, quietly","ref":"E12·L18"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"think","ja":"「何か[失礼]{しつれい}なことを書いたのだと、ずっと思っていた」そうです。あのー、それで、手紙はどうしても[捨]{す}てられなかった、と。","en":"She says she always thought she had written something rude. And, um, that's why she could never throw the letters away.","gl":"あのー: \"um,\" a filler. どうしても～ない: just can't ～.","tag":"carefully","ref":"E12·L19"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"think","ja":"私も同じです、と…あ、いえ。それは、自分で言います。","en":"Tell her it was the same for... oh, no. I'll say that one myself.","tag":"catching herself","ref":"E12·L20"},
{"t":"narr","text":"文子さんは、高校生のころのように、[背中]{せなか}をまっすぐにした。そして、英語で、一つずつ、ゆっくり言った。","en":"Fumiko-san sits up straight, the way she must have sat as a schoolgirl. Then she says it in English, slowly, one word at a time.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"think","ja":"I thought... you were angry. I corrected your kanji.","en":"あなたが怒っていると…思っていました。私が、あなたの漢字を直したから。","lang":"en","tag":"slow, careful English, Japanese accent","audio":"Mrs. Satō's next line is in careful English, with a Japanese accent.","ref":"E12·L21"},
{"t":"narr","text":"ロレインは、少し考えた。その手紙は、届いていない。それから、笑って、紙を一まい、カメラに向けた。","en":"Lorraine needs a moment. That letter never reached her. Then she laughs and holds a sheet of paper up to the camera.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"lorraine","mood":"yay","ja":"Well, go on, then. Correct it now!","en":"じゃあ、どうぞ。今、直してちょうだい！","lang":"en","tag":"laughing, elderly Australian woman","ref":"E12·L22"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"yay","ja":"「じゃあ、今[直]{なお}して」って。あ、紙を見せていらっしゃいます。「[汐浦]{しおうら}」って書いてありますよ！","en":"She says, \"Then correct it now!\" Oh, she's showing us a piece of paper. It says \"Shioura\"!","tag":"excited","ref":"E12·L23"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"think","ja":"…[上手]{じょうず}です。[直]{なお}す所はありません、と[伝]{つた}えてください。","en":"...It's very good. Please tell her there's nothing to correct.","tag":"pause, fondly","ref":"E12·L24"},
{"t":"narr","text":"本当は、少しちがう。さんずいは、今も下から書いてある。線の形を見れば分かる。でも、文子さんは、もう直した。五十年以上前に、届かなかった手紙で。人を直すのは、一回だけだ。ロレインが、また何か言った。まりやの顔が、赤くなった。","en":"That isn't quite true. The water radicals are still written from the bottom up; you can tell from the shape of the strokes. But Fumiko-san already corrected them once, more than fifty years ago, in the letter that never arrived. She only corrects a person once. Lorraine says something else, and Mariya's face turns pink.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"lorraine","mood":"hello","ja":"And your interpreter's English is lovely, by the way.","en":"それから、通訳さんの英語、とてもすてきね。","lang":"en","tag":"warm, offhand, elderly Australian woman","ref":"E12·L25"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"oops","ja":"あの…今のは、[訳]{やく}さなくてもいいですか。私のことなので。","en":"Um... Do I have to translate that one? It's about me.","gl":"訳す (やくす): to translate.","tag":"flustered, whispering","ref":"E12·L26"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"tip","ja":"[訳]{やく}してください。[全部]{ぜんぶ}[伝]{つた}えるのが、[通訳]{つうやく}の仕事でしょう。","en":"Please translate it. Passing on everything is an interpreter's job, isn't it?","gl":"通訳 (つうやく): interpreting; an interpreter.","tag":"kind but firm, teacherly","ref":"E12·L27"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"sleepy","ja":"…「通訳の[方]{かた}の英語は、とてもすてきですね」とおっしゃっています。自分で言うと、はずかしいんですけど…。","en":"...She says, \"The interpreter's English is lovely.\" It's embarrassing to say it myself...","gl":"はずかしい: embarrassing. ～んですけど…: a sentence left unfinished on purpose.","tag":"embarrassed, quick","ref":"E12·L28"},
{"t":"narr","text":"まりやは、もう二十分も英語で話している。自分では、気づいていなかった。自分のためじゃなくて、だれかのためなら、こわくないのかもしれない。テーブルのはしで、トビーが少し笑った。最後に、ロレインが言った。\"Write to me. On paper.\"","en":"Mariya has been speaking English for twenty minutes without noticing. Maybe it isn't scary when you're doing it for someone else. At the end of the table, Toby smiles a little. As the call ends, Lorraine says, \"Write to me. On paper.\"","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"hello","ja":"書きます。今度は、[住所]{じゅうしょ}を[三回]{さんかい}[確]{たし}かめてから出します、と[伝]{つた}えてください。","en":"I will. Please tell her that this time, I'll check the address three times before I mail it.","gl":"確かめる (たしかめる): to check, to make sure.","tag":"smiling","ref":"E12·L29"},
{"t":"break"},
{"t":"narr","text":"三月の終わり。新しい部屋は、新しい木のにおいがする。[玄関]{げんかん}の前の[石段]{いしだん}は、手すりのついたスロープになった。夕方、正一さんは、新しい部屋のまどからとうだいを見て、うで時計を見た。そして、言った。「とうだい、[三秒]{さんびょう}おそい」。去年の春と、同じだ。","en":"Late March. The new room smells of fresh wood, and the stone steps by the front door have become a ramp with a handrail. In the evening, Shōichi-san watches the lighthouse from the window of his new room, checks his watch, and says, \"The lighthouse. Three seconds late.\" It is the same as last spring.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"一年がたった。でも、みんなの話は、まだとちゅうだ。みんな、次にすることがある。ロドリゴは、藤原さんのスタジオから仕事の話をもらって、ビザを変える[申請]{しんせい}も出した。でも、答えはまだ出ていない。[書類]{しょるい}は、イエンが四分でレビューした。イエンは、この夏、ベトナムと日本にチームがある会社で、インターンをすることになった。うまくいけば、ブリッジSEとして働けるかもしれない。トビーは、[修士論文]{しゅうしろんぶん}を出した。三月の終わりに、[卒業]{そつぎょう}する。でも、そのあとどうするかは、まだ決めていない。国に帰るか、日本で仕事をさがすか、[博士課程]{はかせかてい}に[進]{すす}むか。かいとは、春休みに家に帰って、店を手伝う。ノートパソコンも持って行く。","en":"A year has gone by, but nobody's story is finished. Each of them has a next step. Rodrigo has a job offer from Ms. Fujiwara's studio, and he has applied to change his visa. But there is no answer yet. Yến reviewed his paperwork in four minutes. This summer, Yến will do an internship at a company with teams in Vietnam and Japan. If it goes well, it could lead to a job as a bridge SE. Toby has handed in his master's thesis and graduates at the end of March, but he still hasn't decided what comes next: going home, looking for work in Japan, or staying on for a PhD. Kaito is going home for spring break to help at the shop. He is taking his laptop.","gl":"申請 (しんせい): an application. ブリッジSE: a \"bridge\" systems engineer. 修士論文 (しゅうしろんぶん): a master's thesis. 博士課程 (はかせかてい): a PhD program.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"市の[警報]{けいほう}のプロジェクトのチームは、毎週火曜日に集まる。中心は、あおいとイエンだ。チェスカは、わざとテーブルのはしにすわっている。インドネシア語の声のメッセージは、デウィが[録音]{ろくおん}した。あおいがこの春に[応募]{おうぼ}した会社は、全部、汐浦の会社だ。朝はときどき、なりはまを歩く。もう、だれにもかくしていない。すなは、ちゃんと[鳴]{な}く。","en":"The city's alert project team meets every Tuesday. Aoi and Yến lead it. Cheska sits at the end of the table on purpose. Dewi recorded the voice message in Indonesian. Every company Aoi has applied to this spring is in Shioura. Some mornings, she walks on Nari-hama, and she doesn't hide it from anyone anymore. The sand sings.","gl":"応募する (おうぼする): to apply for a job.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"つばめ通りでは、去年のポスターが、またお茶の店のまどにはってある。日付だけ、ぬりかえてある。千代さんは、店の前で、今年はじめてのつばめを数えた。[二羽]{にわ}だ。[港]{みなと}では、トビーの[録音]{ろくおん}に、[源]{げん}さんと[岩田]{いわた}さんが二人とも入っている。昔の大水が何年だったか、二人はずっと言い合っている。町の人に言わせれば、それも話していることになる。","en":"On Tsubame Street, last year's poster is back in the tea shop window, with only the date painted over. In front of her shop, Chiyo counts the first swallows of the year. There are two. At the harbor, Toby's recording has both Gen-san and Iwata-san on it. The two of them keep arguing about the year of the old flood. According to the town, that counts as talking.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"narr","text":"庭では、トビーが[畑]{はたけ}をほっている。まりやは、となりで[種]{たね}をまいている。","en":"In the garden, Toby is digging the vegetable bed. Mariya is planting seeds beside him.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"hello","ja":"きのう、家に電話したよ。「[大丈夫]{だいじょうぶ}」って言うのは、もうやめた。父さんの病気のことも、ちゃんと聞いた。","en":"I called home yesterday. I've stopped saying \"Everything's fine.\" And I asked properly about Dad's illness.","tag":"quiet, steady","ref":"E12·L30"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"think","ja":"…じゃあ、帰るの？","en":"...So are you going back?","tag":"carefully casual","ref":"E12·L31"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"think","ja":"まだ分からない。まりやは？[留学]{りゅうがく}、[受]{う}かったんでしょ。タスマニアの大学。行くの？","en":"I don't know yet. What about you? You got into the exchange, right? The university in Tasmania. Are you going?","gl":"受かる (うかる): to pass, to be accepted.","tag":"curious, gentle","ref":"E12·L32"},
{"t":"narr","text":"まりやの大学の[姉妹校]{しまいこう}は、タスマニアの大学だ。汐浦の姉妹都市にあって、トビーが[育]{そだ}った町のすぐ近くだ。","en":"Mariya's university has a sister university in Tasmania. It is in Shioura's sister city, very close to the town where Toby grew up.","gl":"交換留学 (こうかんりゅうがく): a student exchange.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"sleepy","ja":"まだ分からない。行ったら、[島]{しま}を[捨]{す}てるみたいで…。[返事]{へんじ}のしめ切りは、金曜日なんだけど。","en":"I don't know yet. If I go, it feels like I'm abandoning the island... The deadline to answer is Friday, though.","gl":"しめ切り (しめきり): a deadline.","tag":"torn","ref":"E12·L33"},
{"t":"line","who":"toby","mood":"tip","ja":"ぼくは、行ったほうがいいと思う。…これは、ぼくの[意見]{いけん}だよ。「はい」って言ってるだけじゃないよ。","en":"I think you should go. ...That's my real opinion, by the way. I'm not just saying yes.","tag":"sincere, then a little shy","ref":"E12·L34"},
{"t":"line","who":"mariya","mood":"yay","ja":"…木曜日の[練習]{れんしゅう}、ちゃんと[効]{き}いてるね。","en":"...Thursday practice is really working.","gl":"効く (きく): to work, to have an effect.","tag":"teasing, warm","ref":"E12·L35"},
{"t":"narr","text":"[門]{もん}の横では、管理人のあおいが、ポストの古い名前のラベルを、全部書き直した。205[号室]{ごうしつ}には、新しいラベルがある。まだ、名前は書いていない。文子さんは、げんかんで、えんぴつを持って、けいじばんの前にいる。","en":"Out at the gate, Aoi, as manager, has rewritten every faded label on the mailboxes. Room 205 has a new label, still blank. Inside, Fumiko-san is standing at the bulletin board with her pencil.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"think","ja":"あおいさん、205[号室]{ごうしつ}の[方]{かた}がいらっしゃるのは、[明日]{あした}でしたっけ。","en":"Aoi, the new person for Room 205 is coming tomorrow, isn't it?","gl":"～っけ: said when you are trying to remember.","tag":"curious","ref":"E12·L36"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"think","ja":"[明日]{あした}のはずですけど…。","en":"It should be tomorrow, but...","tag":"uncertain","ref":"E12·L37"},
{"t":"narr","text":"ドアを、三回ノックする音がした。ていねいなノックだ。住所を何回も確かめてから来た人の音だ。ねこが、だれよりも先に、ドアの前に行った。","en":"Three knocks at the door. Careful ones, from someone who has checked the address more than once. The cat gets to the door before anyone else.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"cat","pose":"back","alt":"The cat seen from behind, sitting and facing the front door"},
{"t":"line","who":"aoi","mood":"hello","ja":"はーい、今行きます。","en":"Coming!","tag":"calling out, cheerful","ref":"E12·L38"},
{"t":"line","who":"fumiko","mood":"yay","ja":"ねこさんの名前が、また一つふえそうですね。","en":"It looks like the cat is about to get one more name.","gl":"ふえる: to increase.","tag":"delighted","ref":"E12·L39"},
{"t":"narr","text":"あおいが、ドアを開ける。台所では、ロドリゴが、もう立ち上がっている。「はじめまして」は、一人に一回しか言えない。","en":"Aoi opens the door. In the kitchen, Rodrigo is already on his feet. You can only say はじめまして to each person once.","lang":"ja"},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u12-x1","type":"mcq","q":"In her letter, Fumiko-san writes: 私は長い間、あなたが書くのをやめたのだと思っていました。しかし、やめた人は、だれもいなかったのです。 What does she want Lorraine to understand?","options":[{"t":"Neither of them ever stopped writing","why":"Right. The first sentence gives what she used to believe (～と思っていました). しかし turns it around, and the sentence after it carries the point, with ～のです to explain. Then つまり sums it up: the fault was the address.","ok":true},
{"t":"Lorraine stopped writing to her that year","why":"That is what she used to think. ～と思っていました puts it in the past, and しかし turns away from it."},
{"t":"She herself stopped writing because her family moved","why":"She did move, but she wrote with her new address. やめた人は、だれもいなかった: nobody stopped."},
{"t":"She is angry with the people who changed the addresses","why":"She does blame the address in the next sentence, but lightly, and she doesn't blame any person. The point is that the silence was nobody's choice."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u12-x2","type":"mcq","q":"Mariya says 「通訳の[方]{かた}の英語は、とてもすてきですね」とおっしゃっています. Whose words are inside the quotation marks, and how can you tell?","options":[{"t":"Lorraine's: ～とおっしゃっています reports what someone else is saying, respectfully","why":"Right. と marks the quote, and おっしゃる is the respectful \"say,\" so the speaker is someone Mariya respects: Lorraine. The compliment is about Mariya herself, which is why she wanted to skip it.","ok":true},
{"t":"Mariya's own: she is praising Lorraine's English","why":"Mariya would never use the respectful おっしゃる about her own words. And 通訳の方 is the interpreter: Mariya."},
{"t":"Fumiko-san's: Mariya is putting her Japanese into English","why":"In this line, the interpreting goes the other way, from Lorraine's English into Japanese. Fumiko-san's messages end with ～と[伝]{つた}えてください."},
{"t":"Nobody's: it is a set phrase, like お[久]{ひさ}しぶりです","why":"It is a real comment that Lorraine has just made, quoted with と."}]}},
{"t":"ex","ex":{"id":"story-e3u12-x3","type":"mcq","q":"Fumiko-san says 今度は、[住所]{じゅうしょ}を[三回]{さんかい}[確]{たし}かめてから出します. What will she do?","options":[{"t":"Check the address three times, and only then mail the letter","why":"Right. ～てから means \"after ～,\" with a clear order: first the checking, then the mailing.","ok":true},
{"t":"Mail it three times, to be sure it arrives","why":"三回 goes with 確かめる, not with 出す. One letter, three checks."},
{"t":"Mail it, and check the address afterward","why":"That is the wrong order. ～てから puts 確かめる first."},
{"t":"Check the address while she writes it","why":"\"While\" would be ～ながら. ～てから is one thing after another."}]}},
{"t":"lang","items":["The shape of a letter shows where its point is. Fumiko-san starts with an old belief (～と思っていました), turns with しかし, explains with ～のです, and sums up with つまり. Read the sentence after the turn twice.","An interpreter's Japanese is full of reporting: 「…」とおっしゃっています, 「…」そうです, 「…」って. Going the other way, Fumiko-san hands over each message with ～と[伝]{つた}えてください.","Real speech has gaps. えーと and あのー buy Mariya time. あ、いえ takes a sentence back. ～んですけど… and [明日]{あした}のはずですけど… stop early and let the listener finish the thought."]},
{"t":"reflect","q":"For more than fifty years, each woman believed the other had stopped writing, and each thought it was her own fault. Is there someone you lost touch with, where the reason might have been as small as an address?"}]}]};
